Object.assign(window.IND_FEED_BODY, {"hp-fk.hornbill-honour-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-honour:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Hornbill Feather Is Earned","text":"\"इसलिए जब कोई आदमी वह पंख लगाता था,\" दादाजी ने कहा, \"तो गाँव का कहना होता था: इस इंसान की ज़ुबान हॉर्नबिल जैसी पक्की है। वह फल लेकर ज़रूर लौटेगा। इन पहाड़ियों में यह बात सोने से भी ज़्यादा कीमती थी, क्योंकि इन पहाड़ियों में हम एक-दूसरे के वादे के भरोसे जीते थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"So when a man wore that feather,\" said his grandfather, \"the village was saying: this one's word holds like the hornbill's. He will come back with the fruit. In these hills that was worth more than gold, because in these hills we lived by each other's word.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-honour.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-honour|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-honour-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-honour:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Hornbill Feather Is Earned","text":"महीनों बाद लड़के ने देखा कि कीचड़ की दीवार टूट चुकी थी और पूरा परिवार डाली पर बाहर आ गया था — माँ दुबली लेकिन शानदार लग रही थी, बच्चे खूब शोर मचा रहे थे, और सच कहें तो, पिता पूरी तरह थका हुआ दिख रहा था। किसी ने उसे कोई पंख नहीं दिया। वह खुद ही वह पंख था।","lang":"hi","body":"Months later the boy saw the mud wall broken open and the whole family out on the branch — the mother thin and glorious, the young ones loud, the father looking, frankly, exhausted. Nobody gave him a feather. He was the feather.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-honour.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-honour|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-kisama-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-kisama:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of Festivals","text":"\"नागालैंड किसी एक समुदाय का नहीं है। यहाँ कई समुदाय हैं — आओ, अंगामी, सूमी, लोथा, कोन्याक, चाखेसांग, रेंगमा, और भी बहुत से — हर एक की अपनी भाषा, अपनी बुनाई, अपने त्योहार, और घर बनाने का अपना अनोखा तरीका। एक कोन्याक और एक अंगामी उतने ही अलग हैं जितने एक तमिल और एक पंजाबी, और उन्हें इस बात का पूरा भरोसा भी है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Nagaland is not one people. It is many — Ao, Angami, Sumi, Lotha, Konyak, Chakhesang, Rengma, and more — each with its own language, its own weave, its own festivals, its own way of building a house. A Konyak and an Angami are as different as a Tamil and a Punjabi, and just as sure about it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-kisama.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-kisama|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-kisama-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-kisama:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of Festivals","text":"\"साल के ज़्यादातर दिनों में, हर समुदाय अपनी-अपनी पहाड़ियों पर अपने त्योहार मनाता है। लेकिन दिसंबर में कुछ अलग ही होता है। कोहिमा के पास किसामा नाम की एक पहाड़ी ढलान पर एक ऐसा गाँव बसता है जो किसी एक समुदाय का नहीं है — क्योंकि वह उन सबका है। हर समुदाय के लिए एक 'मोरुंग' यानी एक बड़ा घर, एक ही कतार में अगल-बगल बना हुआ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"For most of the year, each people keeps its own feasts in its own hills. But in December, something else happens. On a hillside called Kisama, near Kohima, a village stands that belongs to no one people — because it belongs to all of them. A morung, a great house, for each community, side by side in one row.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-kisama.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-kisama|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-kisama-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-kisama:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of Festivals","text":"\"यह है हॉर्नबिल उत्सव। दस दिनों के लिए पूरा राज्य किसामा में उमड़ पड़ता है: ढलानों के आर-पार एक-दूसरे की थाप पर गूँजते लकड़ी के नगाड़े, लाल और काले रंगों की दर्जनों छटाओं में थिरकते नर्तक, पहलवान, गायक, आग जलाने वाले करतबबाज़, और पहाड़ियों की हर रसोई की परंपरा का खाना, जो सब एक साथ पक रहा होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"This is the Hornbill Festival. For ten days the whole state comes to Kisama: log drums answering each other across the slope, dancers in a dozen different reds and blacks, wrestlers, singers, fire-makers, and food from every kitchen tradition in the hills, all cooking at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-kisama.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-kisama|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-kisama-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-kisama:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of Festivals","text":"\"एक बच्ची अपने पिताजी के साथ आई, और इस सब के बीचों-बीच खड़े होकर धीरे-धीरे गोल घूमी। \\\"मुझे ठीक इसी जगह खड़े होकर पाँच भाषाएँ सुनाई दे रही हैं,\\\" उसने कहा। \\\"छह,\\\" पिताजी बोले। \\\"तुम्हारे पीछे वाली आंटियों ने अभी-अभी दूसरी भाषा शुरू कर दी।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"A girl came with her father, and stood in the middle of it, turning slowly. \"I can hear five languages from this exact spot,\" she said. \"Six,\" said her father. \"The aunties behind you switched.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-kisama.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-kisama|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-kisama-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-kisama:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of Festivals","text":"\"हॉर्नबिल हर नागा समुदाय के गीतों और कहानियों में उड़ता नज़र आता है — हर किसी के यहाँ अलग तरह से, और यही तो ख़ास बात है। इस त्योहार ने किसी से भी एक जैसा बनने को नहीं कहा। इसने तो बस सबसे यही कहा कि वे जैसे हैं, वैसे ही चले आएँ, और अपनी पहचान को एक कतार में सजाएँ ताकि बाकी सब उसकी तारीफ़ कर सकें।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The hornbill flies through the songs and stories of every Naga people — each one differently, and that is the point. The festival did not ask anyone to become alike. It asked everyone to bring what they already were, and put it in a row where the others could admire it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-kisama.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-kisama|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-kisama-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-kisama:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of Festivals","text":"\"इसलिए उस लड़की ने आओ मोरुंग के बाहर बैठकर कोन्याक खाना खाया, जबकि चखेसांग ढोल वादक ढोल बजा रहे थे, और किसी को भी यह अजीब नहीं लगा, क्योंकि दिसंबर के दस दिनों में किसामा बना ही इसी के लिए है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So the girl ate Konyak food outside an Ao morung while Chakhesang drummers played, and nobody thought that was strange, because for ten days in December that is exactly what Kisama is for.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-kisama.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-kisama|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-kisama-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-kisama:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of Festivals","text":"\"जब वे वहाँ से निकले, तो उसके पिता ने उसके लिए एक शॉल खरीदी — किसी दूसरे समुदाय के एक बुनकर से, जिन्होंने उस डिज़ाइन और उसके मायने समझाए, यह बताया कि उनके यहाँ घर पर इसे पहनने की इजाज़त किसे थी, और एक मेहमान के लिए यह सादी वाली शॉल ही क्यों सही थी। उसने उसे बरसों सँभालकर रखा। वह आज भी उसके पास है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When they left, her father bought her a shawl — from a weaver of a community not their own, who explained the pattern, and what it meant, and who was allowed to wear it at home, and why this plainer one was the right one for a guest. She kept it for years. She keeps it still.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-kisama.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-kisama|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cat-tiger-lesson-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cat-tiger-lesson:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lesson the Cat Kept Back","text":"\"नागा पहाड़ियों में लोग कहते हैं कि बाघ पैदा होते ही बाघ बनना नहीं जान गया था। बहुत समय पहले, वह बस बड़ा था — बड़ा और अनाड़ी, जहाँ जाता धड़ाम-धूम मचाता, और शिकार से भरे जंगल में भी भूखा ही घूमता रहता। और उन पहाड़ियों की सबसे बेहतरीन शिकारी तुम्हारे दोनों हाथों जितनी बड़ी एक जीव थी: बिल्ली।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the Naga hills they tell that the tiger was not born knowing how to be a tiger. Once, long ago, he was just big — big and clumsy, all thump and crash, going hungry in a forest full of dinner. And the finest hunter in those hills was somebody the size of your two hands: the cat.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cat-tiger-lesson.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cat-tiger-lesson|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cat-tiger-lesson-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cat-tiger-lesson:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lesson the Cat Kept Back","text":"\"बाघ बहुत झेंपता हुआ, अपने भारी-भरकम शरीर के साथ उसके पास आया। उसने कहा, \\\"मुझे सिखाओ। मेरे पास पंजे हैं, मज़बूत कंधे हैं, फिर भी मेरे हाथ कुछ नहीं लगता।\\\" और बिल्ली ने, जो सिखाने की बात को बड़े ध्यान से लेती थी, उसे ऊपर से नीचे तक देखा और कहा: \\\"बहुत खूब। पहला सबक: पहाड़ दरकने की तरह धड़धड़ाते हुए चलना बंद करो।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"The tiger came to her, enormous and embarrassed. \"Teach me,\" he said. \"I have the claws and I have the shoulders and I catch nothing at all.\" And the cat, who took teaching seriously, looked him over and said: \"Very well. Lesson one: stop walking like a landslide.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cat-tiger-lesson.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cat-tiger-lesson|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cat-tiger-lesson-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cat-tiger-lesson:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lesson the Cat Kept Back","text":"उसने उसे बहुत अच्छे से सिखाया, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे एक अच्छा गुरु सिखाता है। दबे पाँव चलना, एक-एक पंजा जमाकर। अचानक बिल्कुल थम जाना, और उस ठहराव के अंदर धीरज रखना। घास के बीच झुककर चुपचाप सरकना। पिछले पैरों को समेटना, और फिर छलांग लगाना। वह एक अच्छा शिष्य था, और उसने उसे यह बात बताई भी—जैसा कि हर गुरु को बताना चाहिए।","lang":"hi","body":"She taught him properly, the way a good teacher does. The soft walk, paw by paw. The freeze, and the patience inside the freeze. The low flow through the grass. The gathering of the back legs, and the spring. He was a good student, and she told him so, which teachers should.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cat-tiger-lesson.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cat-tiger-lesson|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cat-tiger-lesson-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cat-tiger-lesson:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lesson the Cat Kept Back","text":"मौसम बीतने के साथ-साथ बाघ और बेहतर होता गया, और फिर वह सचमुच बेहद शानदार बन गया। वह धुएँ की तरह सरकता था। पत्थर की तरह चुपचाप इंतज़ार करता था। पूरा जंगल उसकी मौजूदगी के हिसाब से ढलने लगा। और इसी दौरान कहीं, वह अपनी छोटी-सी गुरु को एक अलग ही नज़र से देखने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"Season by season the tiger got better, and then he got magnificent. He moved like smoke. He waited like a stone. The whole forest reorganised itself around the fact of him. And somewhere in there, he began to look at his small teacher differently.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cat-tiger-lesson.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cat-tiger-lesson|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cat-tiger-lesson-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cat-tiger-lesson:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lesson the Cat Kept Back","text":"\"यह बड़ी अजीब बात है,\" एक दिन अपने शरीर को तानते हुए बाघ ने कहा, \"कि मुझे इतने छोटे से जीव का इतना आभारी होना पड़े।\" और उसने तय कर लिया—जैसे बहुत ज़्यादा ताकतवर लोग कभी-कभी कर बैठते हैं—कि अब उसके साथ तमीज़ से पेश आने की कोई ज़रूरत नहीं है। \"ये पहाड़ियाँ अब मेरी हैं,\" उसने कहा, और छलांग लगा दी, उसे ठीक-ठीक यह दिखाने के लिए कि उसने उसे कितना बढ़िया सिखाया था।","lang":"hi","body":"\"It is odd,\" said the tiger one day, flexing, \"that I should owe so much to somebody so small.\" And he decided — the way the too-strong sometimes do — that he no longer needed to be polite to her. \"These hills are mine now,\" he said, and sprang, to show her exactly how well she had taught him.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cat-tiger-lesson.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cat-tiger-lesson|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cat-tiger-lesson-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cat-tiger-lesson:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lesson the Cat Kept Back","text":"उसके पंजे खाली घास पर जा गिरे। उसने बाएँ देखा, दाएँ देखा—और फिर ऊपर। और वहाँ उसकी गुरु, पेड़ की एक डाल पर आराम से बैठी, अपना कान साफ़ कर रही थी, उसकी पहुँच से कोसों दूर।","lang":"hi","body":"His paws hit the empty grass. He looked left, right — then up. And there was his teacher, settled comfortably on a branch, washing an ear, entirely out of reach.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cat-tiger-lesson.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cat-tiger-lesson|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cat-tiger-lesson-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cat-tiger-lesson:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lesson the Cat Kept Back","text":"\"आपने मुझे पेड़ पर चढ़ना तो कभी नहीं सिखाया,\" बाघ ने नीचे से कहा। \"हाँ,\" बिल्ली ने सहमति जताई। \"यह दाँव मैंने अपने पास ही रखा था। और इसे मैंने ठीक आज ही की दोपहर के लिए बचाकर रखा था।\" और उसने बड़े इत्मीनान से अपना कान साफ़ करना पूरा किया, जबकि उसका सबसे बड़ा शिष्य पेड़ के नीचे बैठा अपनी तमीज़ के बारे में सोचता रहा।","lang":"hi","body":"\"You never taught me the climb,\" said the tiger, from below. \"No,\" agreed the cat. \"I kept that one. I have been keeping it for exactly this afternoon.\" And she finished her ear at leisure while the biggest of all her students sat at the bottom of the tree and thought about his manners.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cat-tiger-lesson.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cat-tiger-lesson|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cat-tiger-lesson-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cat-tiger-lesson:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lesson the Cat Kept Back","text":"यही वजह है कि आज तक बिल्ली पेड़ पर चढ़ जाती है और बाघ नहीं चढ़ पाता—और इसीलिए, कुछ बुज़ुर्ग मुस्कुराते हुए कहते हैं, बिल्ली हमेशा खुद से इतनी संतुष्ट दिखाई देती है। वह दुनिया की इकलौती ऐसी गुरु है जिसका सबसे बुरा शिष्य भी उसे कभी पकड़ नहीं पाया।","lang":"hi","body":"That is why, to this day, the cat climbs and the tiger cannot — and why, some elders add with a smile, a cat always looks so pleased with herself. She is the only teacher whose worst student never caught her.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cat-tiger-lesson.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cat-tiger-lesson|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sungkong-drum-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sungkong-drum:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Drum the Whole Village Pulled","text":"\"नागालैंड के एक आओ गाँव में सबसे बुलंद आवाज़ किसी इंसान की नहीं होती। वह आवाज़ सुंगकोंग यानी लट्ठे से बने ढोल की होती है। एक पूरा का पूरा विशाल पेड़, जिसे काटकर, अंदर से खोखला कर, नाव के आकार का ढोल बनाया जाता है — इतना लंबा कि कई लोग सिर से पैर मिलाकर लेट जाएँ — जो पूरी घाटी में गाँव की आवाज़ बनकर गूँजता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In an Ao village in Nagaland, the biggest voice does not belong to any person. It belongs to the sungkong — the log drum. A whole great tree, felled, hollowed and carved into a boat-shaped drum longer than several men lying head to foot, that speaks for the village across the valleys.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sungkong-drum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sungkong-drum|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sungkong-drum-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sungkong-drum:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Drum the Whole Village Pulled","text":"\"इसे बनाने की शुरुआत आदर-सम्मान से होती है। पेड़ को ध्यान से चुना जाता है और बाक़ायदा उससे अनुमति माँगी जाती है — कुल्हाड़ी का पहला वार करने से पहले पुरानी रस्में निभाई जाती हैं — क्योंकि आप किसी विशालकाय पेड़ को यूँ ही छीनकर नहीं लाते। आप उसे न्योता देकर लाते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Making one begins with respect. The tree is chosen carefully and asked properly — the old rites are said over it before an axe ever touches it — because you do not just take a giant. You invite one.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sungkong-drum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sungkong-drum|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sungkong-drum-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sungkong-drum:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Drum the Whole Village Pulled","text":"\"कारीगर जंगल में वहीं काम करते हैं जहाँ पेड़ गिरा था: उसके पेट को खोखला करते हैं, सिर को आकार देते हैं, और वह लंबी दरार तराशते हैं जो उसका मुँह बनेगी। और फिर आती है वह मुश्किल, जिससे यह कहानी कहानी बनती है। बनकर तैयार हुआ ढोल एक पूरे घर जितना भारी होता है। और उसे खींचकर गाँव तक ले जाने में पूरा एक दिन लगता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The carvers work where the tree fell, up in the forest: hollowing the belly, shaping the head, cutting the long slit that will be its mouth. And then comes the problem that makes this story a story. The finished drum weighs as much as a house. And it is a day's haul from home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sungkong-drum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sungkong-drum|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sungkong-drum-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sungkong-drum:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Drum the Whole Village Pulled","text":"\"पहली बार ढोल खींचने की इस मुहिम में शामिल हुए एक लड़के ने पत्तों पर पड़ी उस भारी-भरकम चीज़ को देखा, फिर बेंत की रस्सियों के घेरों को देखा, और एक समझदार बच्चे की तरह अपना हिसाब लगाया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A boy on his first drum-hauling looked at the great thing lying in the leaves, and at the coils of cane rope, and did the arithmetic of a sensible child.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sungkong-drum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sungkong-drum|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sungkong-drum-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sungkong-drum:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Drum the Whole Village Pulled","text":"\"और वह ऐसा दिन था जिसे वह लड़का कभी नहीं भूल पाया। रस्सियों पर पूरा का पूरा गाँव — आदमी, औरतें, हर कोई जिसने रस्सी थाम रखी थी — और उनके आगे गूँजता ढोल खींचने का गीत, और हर अंतरे पर पाँच सौ लोग मिलकर एक जान होकर ज़ोर लगाते, और गोल लट्ठों पर वह महाकाय ढोल एक-एक हाथ आगे खिसकता जाता।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And that is the day the boy never forgot. The whole village on the ropes — men, women, everyone with a grip — and the drum-hauling song rolling out ahead of them, and on each chorus five hundred people pulling as one person, and the giant sliding forward another arm's length on its rollers.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sungkong-drum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sungkong-drum|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sungkong-drum-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sungkong-drum:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Drum the Whole Village Pulled","text":"पूरा दिन लग गया, और यह साल का सबसे बढ़िया दिन था। क्योंकि जो गाँव मिलकर ढोल खींचता है, वह उसके बाद अपने बारे में एक बात जान जाता है: अगर हम एक बोल पर साथ मिलकर ज़ोर लगाएँ, तो इस पहाड़ी पर ऐसी कोई चीज़ नहीं जिसे हम हिला न सकें।","lang":"hi","body":"It took all day, and it was the best day of the year. Because a village that has hauled a drum together knows something about itself afterwards: there is nothing on this ridge we cannot move, if we pull on the same word.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sungkong-drum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sungkong-drum|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sungkong-drum-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sungkong-drum:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Drum the Whole Village Pulled","text":"घर पहुँचकर, अपनी आदर की जगह पर सजने के बाद, ढोल का असली काम शुरू हुआ। अलग-अलग ख़बरों के लिए अलग-अलग थाप: ख़तरे के लिए एक ताल, दावत के लिए दूसरी, जीत के लिए तीसरी, और गाँव वालों को इकट्ठा बुलाने के लिए एक और। \"यह एक आवाज़ है,\" लड़के के दादाजी ने उससे कहा। \"इसके शब्दों को भी वैसे ही सीखो जैसे किसी और की बोली सीखते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Home, and set in its place of honour, the drum began its real work. Different beats for different news: one rhythm for danger, one for a feast, one for triumph, one for calling the village in. \"It is a voice,\" the boy's grandfather told him. \"Learn its words like anybody's words.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sungkong-drum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sungkong-drum|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sungkong-drum-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sungkong-drum:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Drum the Whole Village Pulled","text":"और इस तरह उस गाँव का बच्चा बिना मुँह वाली एक भाषा सीखकर बड़ा हुआ — बिस्तर में लेटे-लेटे, ढोल की थाप से पूरी घाटी का हाल जान लेता: वह तो बस अभ्यास है; वह दूर वाले गाँव में दावत है; वह, ज़रा उठकर बैठो, कोई ज़रूरी ख़बर है।","lang":"hi","body":"And so a child of that village grew up bilingual in a language with no mouth — lying in bed, reading the valley by drumbeat: that is only practice; that is a feast at the far village; that, sit up, is news.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sungkong-drum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sungkong-drum|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bomong-bong-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bomong-bong:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sun Sisters","text":"अरुणाचल प्रदेश के आदि लोग बताते हैं कि शुरुआत में आसमान को दो बहनों ने थाम रखा था, जो खुद धरती और आकाश की बेटियाँ थीं: बोमोंग और बोंग। दोनों ही चमकती थीं। दोनों ही सूरज थीं। और वे एक-दूसरे से बिल्कुल वैसे ही प्यार करती थीं जैसे बहनें करती हैं — पूरे दिल से, और बारी-बारी से कमान सँभालते हुए।","lang":"hi","body":"The Adi people of Arunachal Pradesh tell that in the beginning the sky was held up by two sisters, daughters of the Earth and the Sky themselves: Bomong and Bong. Both of them shone. Both of them were suns. And they loved each other the way sisters do — completely, and taking turns being in charge.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bomong-bong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bomong-bong|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bomong-bong-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bomong-bong:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sun Sisters","text":"लेकिन दो सूरज, ज़रूरत से एक ज़्यादा थे। जब बोमोंग पश्चिम में ढलती, तो बोंग पूरब में निकल आती, और रात नाम की तो कोई चीज़ ही नहीं थी — न कोई आराम, न कोई ठंडक, और न कोई ओस। आधी रात को भी चट्टानें गरम रहती थीं। नदियाँ उथली पड़ गईं। दुनिया दिन भर आँखें सिकोड़े रहती और फिर रात भर भी आँखें सिकोड़े रहती।","lang":"hi","body":"But two suns is one sun too many. When Bomong went down in the west, Bong came up in the east, and there was no night at all — and no rest, and no cool, and no dew. The rocks were warm at midnight. The rivers ran shallow. The world squinted all day and then squinted all night.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bomong-bong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bomong-bong|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bomong-bong-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bomong-bong:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sun Sisters","text":"इस नई-नई दुनिया के सारे जीव-जंतु जितनी भी छाँव मिली, वहीं इकट्ठे हो गए और आपस में बात करने लगे। बहनों से कोई नाराज़ नहीं था — भला चमकने के लिए भी कोई किसी से नाराज़ होता है क्या? लेकिन सब भीतर तक थक चुके थे, अपनी हड्डियों तक, वैसे ही जैसे कोई तब थकता है जब कभी एक बार भी रात न हुई हो।","lang":"hi","body":"The creatures of the young world gathered in whatever shade there was and talked it over. Nobody was angry with the sisters — how can you be angry at somebody for shining? But everybody was tired, down in their bones, the way you are tired when there has never once been a night.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bomong-bong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bomong-bong|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bomong-bong-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bomong-bong:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sun Sisters","text":"इसलिए उन्होंने ऊपर एक संदेशवाहक भेजा — इस कहानी के मुताबिक, एक छोटा और समझदार जीव — ताकि वह बहनों के सामने सच्चाई से अपनी परेशानी रख सके।","lang":"hi","body":"So they sent a messenger up — in this telling, a small and sensible one — to put the problem to the sisters honestly.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bomong-bong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bomong-bong|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bomong-bong-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bomong-bong:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sun Sisters","text":"बहनों ने उसकी बात सुनी। और पुरानी कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि यह जुदाई बहुत कठिन थी — उसमें एक तीर की बात है, एक गहरे दुख की, और लंबे समय तक छिपने की, और वह हिस्सा मैं बड़ों को ही सुनाने दूँगा, क्योंकि वह कहानी उन्हीं की है। मगर हर कहानी जिस बात पर सहमत है, वह यह है कि इसका अंत कैसे हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"The sisters heard it. And the old tellings say this parting was hard — there is an arrow in them, and a grief, and a long hiding, and I will let the elders tell that part, because it is theirs. What every telling agrees on is how it ended.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bomong-bong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bomong-bong|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bomong-bong-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bomong-bong:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sun Sisters","text":"बोंग ने अपनी आग को ठंडा होने दिया। उसने उसे धीमा किया, और धीमा करती गई — सफ़ेद से सुनहरा और फिर एक कोमल, शांत चाँदी सा — यहाँ तक कि उसकी तरफ़ देखा जा सके, और फिर यहाँ तक कि वह देखने में बेहद प्यारी लगने लगी। और उसने रात का पहरा संभाल लिया, ताकि उसकी बहन दिन को संभाल सके।","lang":"hi","body":"Bong let her fire cool. Down and down she turned it, from white to gold to a soft, patient silver — until she could be looked at, and then until she was lovely to look at. And she took the night watch, so her sister could keep the day.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bomong-bong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bomong-bong|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bomong-bong-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bomong-bong:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sun Sisters","text":"वह पहली रात, दुनिया की सबसे पहली रात थी। ओस न जाने कहाँ से आ गई और हर चीज़ पर एक आशीर्वाद की तरह बैठ गई। सारे जीव सोए — सचमुच गहरी नींद सोए — और नदियाँ उमड़ पड़ीं, और दुनिया ने वह तरीका सीख लिया जो उसने आज तक संभाला हुआ है: पहले उजाला, फिर नर्मी, और फिर से उजाला।","lang":"hi","body":"That first night was the first night there had ever been. The dew came out of nowhere and sat on everything like a blessing. The creatures slept — really slept — and the rivers rose, and the world learned the trick it has kept ever since: bright, then gentle, then bright again.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bomong-bong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bomong-bong|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bomong-bong-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bomong-bong:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sun Sisters","text":"और बहनें आज भी इसे निभाती हैं। बोमोंग दिन में अपनी आग लेकर निकलती है, और बोंग रात में अपनी चाँदी लेकर, और दोनों के होते हुए धरती की कोई भी चीज़ कभी किसी बहन की नज़र से दूर नहीं होती।","lang":"hi","body":"And the sisters still keep it. Bomong crosses by day with the fire, and Bong crosses by night with the silver, and between them nothing on earth is ever out of a sister's sight.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bomong-bong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bomong-bong|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.donyi-polo-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.donyi-polo:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eye of the Day, the Eye of the Night","text":"अरुणाचल प्रदेश के एक गालो गाँव में, एक लड़के ने अपने दादाजी की एक बात पर ध्यान दिया। जब भी दादाजी किसी ज़रूरी बात पर अपनी ज़बान देते — खेत की मेड़ हो या किसी पड़ोसी से किया कोई वादा — वे अपनी ठुड्डी ज़रा-सी सूरज की तरफ़ उठा लेते। सब लोग इसे समझते दिखते थे। किसी ने कभी इसे समझाया नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"In a Galo village in Arunachal Pradesh, a boy noticed a thing his grandfather did. Whenever the old man gave his word on something that mattered — a field boundary, a promise to a neighbour — he would lift his chin, just slightly, toward the sun. Everyone seemed to understand it. Nobody explained it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-donyi-polo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.donyi-polo|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.donyi-polo-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.donyi-polo:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eye of the Day, the Eye of the Night","text":"तो एक शाम लड़के ने पूछ ही लिया। और दादाजी वैसे मुस्कुराए जैसे कोई इंसान सालों से किसी ख़ास सवाल का इंतज़ार कर रहा हो। उन्होंने कहा, \"दोन्यी। यानी सूरज। और पोलो, यानी चाँद। बैठो। यह कोई छोटा-सा जवाब नहीं है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So one evening the boy asked. And his grandfather smiled the smile of a man who has been waiting years for a particular question. \"Donyi,\" he said. \"The sun. And Polo, the moon. Sit down. This is not a small answer.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-donyi-polo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.donyi-polo|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.donyi-polo-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.donyi-polo:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eye of the Day, the Eye of the Night","text":"\"हम तानी लोग हैं — गालो, और आदि, न्यिशी, आपातानी, तागिन, सब के सब अबो तानी की संतान हैं। और हम दुनिया को इसी तरह देखते हैं: दोन्यी और पोलो, सूरज और चाँद, उस परम सत्य की दो आँखें हैं। उसका देखना हैं। दिन में, तुम्हारा किया कुछ भी अनदेखा नहीं रहता। और रात में भी कुछ नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"We are Tani people — Galo, and the Adi, the Nyishi, the Apatani, the Tagin, all the children of Abo Tani. And this is how we hold the world: Donyi and Polo, the sun and the moon, are the two eyes of the great truth. The seeing of it. By day, nothing you do is unseen. By night, nothing either.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-donyi-polo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.donyi-polo|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.donyi-polo-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.donyi-polo:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eye of the Day, the Eye of the Night","text":"\"जासूसी नहीं,\" उन्होंने बात आगे बढ़ाई, क्योंकि लड़के के चेहरे ने यह सवाल पूछ लिया था। \"आँगन में नज़र रखती माँ कोई जासूसी नहीं कर रही होती। दोन्यी वैसे ही देखती हैं जैसे एक माँ देखती है — सब कुछ, ममता से, और झूठ को ज़रा भी बर्दाश्त न करते हुए। इसीलिए जब हम कोई वादा करते हैं, तो उनकी तरफ़ रुख़ करते हैं। हम कह रहे होते हैं: उन्होंने भी मेरी बात सुन ली है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Not spying,\" he added, because the boy's face had asked. \"A mother watching the courtyard is not spying. Donyi sees the way a mother sees — everything, and kindly, and with very little patience for lying. That is why we point to her when we promise. We are saying: she heard me too.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-donyi-polo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.donyi-polo|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.donyi-polo-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.donyi-polo:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eye of the Day, the Eye of the Night","text":"लड़के ने उस सबसे बड़े वादे के बारे में सोचा जिसे वह जानता था — एक खेत को लेकर किसी पड़ोसी को दी गई उसके दादाजी की ज़बान, जिसे उन्होंने तीस सालों तक निभाया था।","lang":"hi","body":"The boy thought about the biggest promise he knew of — his grandfather's word to a neighbour, kept for thirty years, about a field.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-donyi-polo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.donyi-polo|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.donyi-polo-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.donyi-polo:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eye of the Day, the Eye of the Night","text":"\"और क्योंकि वह सब कुछ बिल्कुल साफ़-साफ़ देखती हैं,\" उसके दादाजी आगे बोले, \"हम इस तरह जीने की कोशिश करते हैं कि उनकी नज़र में रहने से हमें कोई झिझक न हो। बस, सच कहें तो यही पूरी बात है। सच बोलो। साफ़ बर्ताव करो। और ऐसे चलो जैसे हर घड़ी दोपहर की धूप खिली हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"And because she sees truly,\" his grandfather went on, \"we try to live so that being seen is no trouble to us. That is the whole of it, really. Speak straight. Deal straight. Walk as if it is always noon.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-donyi-polo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.donyi-polo|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.donyi-polo-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.donyi-polo:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eye of the Day, the Eye of the Night","text":"उस लड़के ने बाकी बातें वैसे ही सीखीं जैसे बच्चे सीखते हैं: त्योहारों में, प्रार्थनाओं में, और गांगगिं में — यानी वो प्रार्थना-घर जहाँ आज दोन्यी-पोलो परिवार एक साथ भजन गाने जुटते हैं। उसने जाना कि उसके लोग इस आस्था को तब से निभा रहे हैं जब से किसी ने गिनती भी नहीं शुरू की थी, इसका एक झंडा है जिस पर सूरज बना है, और ऐसे गीत हैं जिन्हें वह पहले से आधा-अधूरा जानता था।","lang":"hi","body":"The boy learned the rest the way children learn: at festivals, at prayers, in the gangging — the prayer halls where Donyi-Polo families now gather to sing. He learned that his people had held this faith since before anyone counted, and that it had a flag with a sun on it, and songs he already half knew.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-donyi-polo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.donyi-polo|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.donyi-polo-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.donyi-polo:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eye of the Day, the Eye of the Night","text":"और वह खुद भी ऐसा करने लगा — जब भी किसी दोस्त को कोई वचन देता, तो अपनी ठुड्डी ज़रा-सी सूरज की तरफ़ उठा लेता। इससे वादों का मोल ही बदल गया। यह जानना कि कोई तुम्हें देख रहा है, फिर भी प्यार करता है, और तुमसे सच्चे रहने की उम्मीद रखता है: सच तो यह है कि बड़े होने का यह बहुत ही प्यारा तरीका है।","lang":"hi","body":"And he began doing the thing himself — the small lift of the chin, sunward, when he gave his word to a friend. It changed the promises. Knowing you are seen, and loved anyway, and expected to be honest: it turns out that is a very good way to grow up.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-donyi-polo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.donyi-polo|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kine-nane-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kine-nane:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother of the Grain","text":"अरुणाचल प्रदेश के आदि लोग चावल से पहले का वह ज़माना याद करते हैं। लोग वही खाते थे जो जंगल देता था — जंगली रतालू, नई कोपलें, या दिन भर में जो हाथ लग जाए — और जंगल दिलदार तो है, पर उसका कोई पक्का भरोसा नहीं। कुछ हफ़्ते पेट भरा रहता। कुछ हफ़्ते भूख की टीस में बीतते। और कोई किसी बच्चे से यह वादा नहीं कर सकता था कि आने वाला हफ़्ता कैसा होगा।","lang":"hi","body":"The Adi of Arunachal Pradesh remember a time before rice. People ate what the forest offered — wild yams, shoots, whatever the day turned up — and the forest is generous, but not reliable. Some weeks were full. Some weeks were an ache. And nobody could promise a child which kind of week was coming.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kine-nane.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kine-nane|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kine-nane-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kine-nane:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother of the Grain","text":"अनाज था तो ज़रूर। लेकिन वह इंसानों के पास नहीं था। आदि कहानियों में, अनाज फ़सलों की माँ, किने नाने के पास था, जिनकी हिफ़ाज़त में उसका एक-एक दाना रहता था — और उनके भंडार-घर से एक भूखे गाँव के बीच की दूरी ही दुनिया की सबसे बड़ी मुश्किल थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The grain existed. But it was not with people. In the Adi tellings the grain belonged with Kine Nane, the mother of crops, the one in whose keeping every seed of it lay — and the distance between her storehouse and a hungry village was the whole problem of the world.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kine-nane.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kine-nane|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kine-nane-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kine-nane:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother of the Grain","text":"चावल उस दूरी को पार करके कैसे पहुँचा, इसकी कहानियाँ हर घाटी में अलग-अलग हैं — किसी में इसे माँग कर लाया गया, किसी में कोई जीव इसे लेकर आया, तो किसी में इसे पाने के लिए किने नाने को भारी क़ीमत चुकानी पड़ी, और बुज़ुर्ग उस हिस्से को जल्दी में नहीं छोड़ते। हर कहानी में जो बात एक जैसी रहती है, वह यह है: चावल लोगों तक एक गहरे और अनमोल तोहफ़े की तरह पहुँचा। यह यूँ ही कहीं मिला नहीं था। यह दिया गया था।","lang":"hi","body":"The tellings of how the rice crossed that distance differ from valley to valley — in some it is begged for, in some it is carried by a creature, in some the getting of it costs Kine Nane dearly, and the elders do not hurry past that part. What every telling keeps is this: the rice came to people as a gift with a weight to it. Not a finding. A giving.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kine-nane.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kine-nane|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kine-nane-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kine-nane:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother of the Grain","text":"और इस तरह, एक बसंत में, पहली बार किसी इंसान के हाथ में बीज आया। एक छोटा सा ढेर। शायद इतना कि गाँव के हर पेट को एक शानदार शाम के लिए भरा जा सके।","lang":"hi","body":"And so, one spring, there was seed in a human hand for the first time. A small heap of it. Enough, maybe, to fill every belly in the village for one single glorious evening.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kine-nane.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kine-nane|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kine-nane-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kine-nane:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother of the Grain","text":"वह पहला इंतज़ार बहुत लंबा था। लेकिन कतारों में कोंपलें फूट पड़ीं, और बालियाँ दानों से भरकर झुक गईं, और पतझड़ में पूरा गाँव अपने पहले खेत के किनारे खड़ा हुआ और समझ गया कि ज़िंदगी का ढंग बदल चुका था: अब कोई भी इंसान किसी बच्चे से अगले महीने का वादा कर सकता था।","lang":"hi","body":"That first waiting was long. But the shoots came up in their rows, and the heads filled and bowed, and in the autumn the village stood at the edge of its own first field and understood that the shape of life had changed: a person could now promise a child next month.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kine-nane.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kine-nane|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kine-nane-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kine-nane:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother of the Grain","text":"और वे यह नहीं भूले कि यह कहाँ से आया था। हर फ़सल का पहला हिस्सा वापस लौटाया गया — किसी के भी खाने से पहले उसे किने नाने के लिए निकाला गया, और पूरे आदर से धन्यवाद दिया गया। \"खेत हमारा है मेहनत करने के लिए,\" बुज़ुर्गों ने कहा। \"अनाज उनका है देने के लिए। इस बात का क्रम सीधा रखो, तो हर चीज़ का क्रम सीधा रहेगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And they did not forget where it had come from. The first of every harvest went back — set out for Kine Nane before anyone ate, with thanks said properly. \"The field is ours to work,\" the elders said. \"The grain is hers to give. Keep the order of that straight and the order of everything stays straight.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kine-nane.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kine-nane|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kine-nane-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kine-nane:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother of the Grain","text":"वही धन्यवाद एक त्योहार बन गया। सोलुंग के मौक़े पर, आदि गाँवों में, फ़सल का यह आभार निभाया जाता है — रीति-रिवाज़ पूरे किए जाते हैं, खाना बाँटकर खाया जाता है, किने नाने को नाम से याद किया जाता है — एक पूरा त्योहार जो अपने दिल में एक शुक्रिया का पत्र है, जिसे सदियों से हर साल भेजा जा रहा है।","lang":"hi","body":"That thanks grew into a festival. At Solung, in the Adi villages, the harvest's gratitude is kept — the rites said, the food shared out, Kine Nane remembered by name — a whole festival that is, at its heart, a thank-you letter that has been sent every year for centuries.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kine-nane.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kine-nane|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nyokum-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nyokum:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where Everyone Is Invited","text":"निशी अरुणाचल प्रदेश का सबसे बड़ा समुदाय हैं, और हर साल, जैसे ही सर्दियाँ ढलने लगती हैं, वे न्योकुम मनाते हैं। इस नाम का अर्थ ही सब कुछ बता देता है: 'न्योक' का मतलब है धरती, और 'न्योकुम' धरती और उसकी सुख-समृद्धि की देवी हैं — जिनका यह त्योहार है।","lang":"hi","body":"The Nyishi are the largest of the peoples of Arunachal Pradesh, and every year, as winter loosens, they keep Nyokum. The name says what it is: nyok is the land, and Nyokum is the goddess of the land and its plenty — the one whose festival this is.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nyokum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nyokum|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nyokum-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nyokum:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where Everyone Is Invited","text":"एक बच्ची अपने पहले न्योकुम की तैयारियाँ देख रही थी: ज़मीन बुहारी जा रही थी, ताज़े कटे हल्के सुनहरे बाँस से एक सुंदर और बारीक़ वेदी बनाई जा रही थी — और दादी मेहमानों की एक ऐसी सूची समझा रही थीं, जैसी उसने पहले कभी नहीं सुनी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"A girl watched her first Nyokum being prepared: the ground swept, the altar of bamboo raised — a beautiful, intricate thing, fresh-cut and pale gold — and her grandmother explaining the guest list, which was unlike any guest list she had ever heard.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nyokum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nyokum|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nyokum-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nyokum:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where Everyone Is Invited","text":"\"सबको न्योता है,\" दादी ने कहा। \"और सचमुच हर किसी को। सारे परिवारों को तो है ही — पर साथ ही नदियों की आत्माओं को भी। पहाड़ों की आत्माओं को। जंगल वालों को। घर वालों को। उन्हें भी जिनके नाम हम जानते हैं, और उन्हें भी जिनके नाम हम नहीं जानते। न्योकुम ऐसा त्योहार नहीं है जिसमें कोई दरवाज़ा हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Everyone is invited,\" said her grandmother. \"And I mean everyone. Every family, of course — but also the spirits of the rivers. The spirits of the hills. The forest ones. The house ones. The ones we have names for and the ones we do not. Nyokum is not a festival with a door.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nyokum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nyokum|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nyokum-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nyokum:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where Everyone Is Invited","text":"बच्ची ने उन दावतों के बारे में सोचा जिन्हें वह जानती थी, जो ज़्यादातर उल्टे ढंग से चलती थीं — कौन अंदर आ सकता है इसकी सूची, जिसका मतलब यह भी था कि कौन बाहर रहेगा इसकी सूची।","lang":"hi","body":"The girl thought about parties she knew of, which mostly worked the other way — lists of who was in, which meant lists of who was out.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nyokum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nyokum|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nyokum-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nyokum:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where Everyone Is Invited","text":"न्युब — यानी पुजारी — ने पूरे विधि-विधान से, पुरानी प्रार्थना की भाषा में गा-गाकर विस्तार से न्योता दिया। दावत में आइए। हमारे साथ शांति से रहिए। बारिश समय पर और मेहरबान होकर बरसे, खेत भर जाएँ, बच्चे फलें-फूलें, और इस साल किसी का रास्ता किसी और के रास्ते से न उलझे।","lang":"hi","body":"The nyub — the priest — sang the invitations properly, the long way, in the old language of asking. Come to the feast. Be at peace with us. Let the rain be on time and kindly, let the fields fill, let the children grow, let nobody's path and nobody else's path quarrel this year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nyokum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nyokum|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nyokum-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nyokum:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where Everyone Is Invited","text":"और फिर शुरू हुआ त्योहार, अपने हर सही अर्थ के साथ: एक बड़े घेरे में नाचना जिसमें कोई भी शामिल हो सकता था और हर कोई हुआ भी, गाँवों के बीच गीतों का आदान-प्रदान, कई दिनों से पक रहा स्वादिष्ट खाना, और उस जगह की वह ख़ास ख़ुशी जहाँ आया हुआ कोई भी व्यक्ति अनचाहा नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"And then it was a festival, with everything that word should mean: dancing in a great circle that anyone could join and everyone did, songs traded between villages, food that had been days in the making, and the particular happiness of a place where nobody present was unwelcome.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nyokum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nyokum|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nyokum-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nyokum:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where Everyone Is Invited","text":"\"हम दुनिया को इसी तरह सँभालकर रखते हैं,\" नाच के किनारे सुस्ताते हुए उनकी दादी ने कहा। \"इंसान ज़मीन के मालिक नहीं हैं, और न ही इसके हाकिम। हम तो बस इसमें रहने वाले पड़ोसियों का एक हिस्सा हैं। न्योकुम वह दिन है जब सारा पड़ोस — देखा भी और अनदेखा भी — एक साथ बैठकर खाना खाता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"This is how we hold the world,\" her grandmother said, resting at the edge of the dance. \"People are not the owners of the land, and not its masters. We are one set of neighbours in it. Nyokum is the day the whole neighbourhood — seen and unseen — sits down to eat together.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nyokum.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nyokum|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-taki-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-taki:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Abo Tani and the Roasted Seed","text":"अबो तानी, पहले इंसान और अरुणाचल के तानी लोगों के पूर्वज, अपनी आधी ज़िंदगी आत्माओं के साथ अक़्ल की होड़ लगाने में बिताते रहे — कभी जीते, कभी हारे, और अपनी हार को भी ऐसे सबक़ में बदल दिया जिसे उनके बच्चे आज भी काम में लाते हैं। निशी और गालो लोग शाम-शाम भर बैठकर ये क़िस्से सुनाते हैं। यह उन्हीं में से एक हल्की-फुल्की कहानी है।","lang":"hi","body":"Abo Tani, the first man, the ancestor of the Tani peoples of Arunachal, spent half his life in contests of wits with the spirits — winning some, losing some, and turning even the losses into lessons his children still use. The Nyishi and Galo tell whole evenings of these. Here is one of the gentler ones.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-taki.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-taki|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-taki-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-taki:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Abo Tani and the Roasted Seed","text":"बुआई के समय एक आत्मा बाँह पर टोकरी लटकाए, बड़े दोस्ताना अंदाज़ में अबो तानी के पास आई। \"पड़ोसी! इस साल तुम्हारा बीज छोटा और धूल भरा दिख रहा है। मेरा बीज मोटा और चमकदार है। मुझसे अदला-बदली कर लो, टोकरी के बदले टोकरी — तुम मुझे अच्छे लगते हो, और आज मेरा दिल भी बड़ा हो रहा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A spirit came to Abo Tani at planting time, friendly as anything, with a basket on his arm. \"Neighbour! Your seed looks small and dusty this year. Mine is fat and shining. Trade with me, basket for basket — I like you, and I am feeling generous.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-taki.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-taki|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-taki-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-taki:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Abo Tani and the Roasted Seed","text":"और उस आत्मा का बीज सचमुच बहुत सुंदर था — मोटा, चमकदार, और उसमें से भुने हुए अनाज की हल्की और प्यारी-सी ख़ुशबू आ रही थी। अबो तानी, जिनकी नाश्ते से पहले ही इतनी तारीफ़ हो गई थी कि वह फूले नहीं समा रहे थे, उन्होंने उसी वक़्त सौदा कर लिया। टोकरी के बदले टोकरी। वह आत्मा सीटी बजाते हुए चल दी, जो — एक बार फिर — समझ जाने के लिए काफ़ी होना चाहिए था।","lang":"hi","body":"And the spirit's seed WAS beautiful — plump, glossy, smelling faintly and pleasantly of toasted grain. Abo Tani, who had been flattered before breakfast and never quite got over it, traded on the spot. Basket for basket. The spirit went off whistling, which — again — should have been a clue.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-taki.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-taki|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-taki-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-taki:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Abo Tani and the Roasted Seed","text":"अबो तानी ने अपने खेत की झाड़ियाँ काटीं, जलाकर ज़मीन साफ़ की, और हर चमकदार बीज को बड़े जतन से बो दिया। उधर टीले के पार, आत्मा ने वे छोटे और धूल भरे बीज बोए। और फिर बारिश आई, मौसम बदला, और अबो तानी अपना खेत देखने निकले।","lang":"hi","body":"Abo Tani cut his field, burned it clean, and planted every shining seed with care. The spirit, over the ridge, planted the small dusty ones. And then the rains came, and the season turned, and Abo Tani went out to see his field.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-taki.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-taki|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-taki-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-taki:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Abo Tani and the Roasted Seed","text":"कुछ भी नहीं। एक भी कोंपल नहीं। कोने से कोने तक सिर्फ़ सूखी ज़मीन, जबकि पहाड़ी के उस पार उस आत्मा का खेत तोते के पर जैसा हरा-भरा लहलहा रहा था। ऐसा इसलिए, क्योंकि उन ख़ूबसूरत बीजों को भून दिया गया था — बस इतना ही सेंका गया था कि वे चमकें और उनमें से मीठी ख़ुशबू आए, पर वे कभी, कभी भी न अंकुरित हों।","lang":"hi","body":"Nothing. Not one shoot. Bare earth from edge to edge, while over the ridge the spirit's field came up green as a parrot's wing. Because the beautiful seed had been roasted — toasted just enough to shine and smell sweet, and to never, ever sprout.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-taki.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-taki|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-taki-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-taki:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Abo Tani and the Roasted Seed","text":"अबो तानी अपने ख़ाली खेत की मेड़ पर बैठ गए। थोड़ी देर तो उन्हें ग़ुस्सा आया, और फिर — क्योंकि अबो तानी ऐसे ही थे — उनके मन में उत्सुकता जागी। आख़िर किसी बीज पर अपना पूरा मौसम दांव पर लगाने से पहले, यह कैसे पहचाना जाए कि वह ज़िंदा है या मरा हुआ?","lang":"hi","body":"Abo Tani sat down at the edge of his empty field. He was angry for a while, and then — because this is what makes him Abo Tani — he got interested. How do you tell living seed from dead, before you bet a season on it?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-taki.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-taki|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-taki-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-taki:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Abo Tani and the Roasted Seed","text":"अगली बार जब बोआई का मौसम आया, तो वह आत्मा एक और चमकती हुई टोकरी लेकर वापस आई। अबो तानी ने बड़े प्यार से उसका धन्यवाद किया, एक चुटकी बीज लिए, उन्हें चूल्हे के पास गीली काई में लपेट कर रख दिया, और आत्मा को न्योता दिया कि जब तक वे इंतज़ार कर रहे हैं, वह रात का खाना खाकर ही जाए। आत्मा को अचानक कहीं और बहुत ज़रूरी काम याद आ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Next planting time, the spirit came back with another gleaming basket. Abo Tani thanked him warmly, took a pinch, folded it into wet moss by the fire, and invited the spirit to stay for dinner while they waited. The spirit developed an urgent appointment elsewhere.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-taki.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-taki|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-taki-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-taki:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Abo Tani and the Roasted Seed","text":"और ज़ाहिर है, वह चुटकी भर बीज कभी नहीं अंकुरित हुआ, और वह सौदा कभी नहीं हुआ, और अबो तानी ने अपने वही छोटे, धूल भरे और वफ़ादार बीज बोए और उस साल भरपेट खाया। इसके बाद वे त्योहारों पर ज़ोर-ज़ोर से सबको यह क़िस्सा सुनाते रहे — क्योंकि जिस सबक़ की क़ीमत आपने पूरे एक मौसम से चुकाई हो, उसे कम से कम मुफ़्त में तो बांट ही देना चाहिए।","lang":"hi","body":"And the pinch, of course, never sprouted, and the trade never happened, and Abo Tani planted his own small dusty faithful seed and ate well that year. He told the story on himself forever after, loudly, at festivals — because a lesson you paid a whole season for should at least be given away free.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-taki.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-taki|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"तानी लोगों की कई कहानियों में, अबो तानी — जो पहले इंसान थे — ने यूं ही किसी से शादी नहीं की। उनका दिल तो ख़ुद आसमान के घराने की बेटी पर आ गया था, यानी सूर्य, दोनी के घर की बेटी पर। जिसका मतलब था, हाथ मांगना। और आसमान का घराना धरती के पहले इंसान को यूं ही 'हां' नहीं कह देता, बिना यह परखे कि वह किस मिट्टी का बना है।","lang":"hi","body":"In many tellings of the Tani peoples, Abo Tani — the first man — did not marry just anyone. He set his heart on a daughter of the sky's own household, of the house of Donyi, the sun. Which meant asking. And the sky's house does not say yes to the first man on earth without checking what he is made of.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"\"तीन काम,\" आकाश के घर ने कहा। \"इस बड़े पहाड़ की ढलान को साफ़ करो — एक ही दिन में। इस टोकरी को छाँटो, जिसमें तीन तरह के बीज आपस में मिले हुए हैं — सुबह होने तक। और नदी से पानी लेकर आओ — जालीदार बुनी हुई टोकरी में। ये सब कर लो, फिर हम बात करेंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Three tasks,\" said the house of the sky. \"Clear the great hillside — in one day. Sort this basket, where three kinds of seed have been mixed together — by morning. And bring water up from the river — in a carrying-basket of open weave. Do those, and we will talk.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"अब, अबो तानी चतुर तो था, लेकिन उसे अपनी चतुराई पर कोई घमंड नहीं था। वह जानता था कि पहाड़ की ढलान इंसान से बड़ी होती है, रात बीजों से भरी टोकरी से छोटी होती है, और टोकरियों को लेकर पानी की अपनी ही पक्की राय होती है। इसलिए उसने वही किया जो घमंडी लोग कभी सोच भी नहीं पाते: वह गया और उसने मदद माँगी।","lang":"hi","body":"Now, Abo Tani was clever, but he was not foolish about his own cleverness. He knew a hillside is bigger than a man, a night is shorter than a mixed basket, and water has firm opinions about baskets. So he did the thing that the proud never think of: he went and asked for help.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"और यहाँ कहानियाँ मुस्कुरा उठती हैं, क्योंकि अबो तानी ने अपनी पूरी ज़िंदगी छोटे-छोटे जीवों के साथ भलाई करते हुए बिताई थी — चींटियों के साथ अपने चावल बाँटना, जंगली मधुमक्खियों के लिए उनका वाजिब आधा हिस्सा छोड़ देना, यहाँ किसी का पंख ठीक करना तो वहाँ किसी के बिल की मरम्मत कर देना — और कभी एक बार भी इसे किसी फ़ायदे की तरह नहीं सोचा था।","lang":"hi","body":"And here the tellings smile, because Abo Tani had spent his whole life being decent to small things — sharing his rice with the ants, leaving the wild bees their fair half, mending a wing here and a burrow there — never once thinking of it as an investment.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"हवा ने, जिस पर उसकी एक भलाई का उधार था, उस बड़े पहाड़ की ढलान पर लेटकर लोट लगाई, और जो साफ़-सफ़ाई पूरे एक दिन में होनी थी, वह एक ही दोपहर में हो गई। और रात में, हज़ारों चींटियाँ उस मिली-जुली टोकरी के पास आ पहुँचीं — और चींटियाँ, जैसा कि हर वह व्यक्ति जानता है जिसने कभी कोई मिठाई गिराई हो, किसी भी चीज़ को किसी भी चीज़ से अलग छाँट सकती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The wind, who owed him a kindness, lay down on the great hillside and rolled, and the clearing of one day was done in an afternoon. And in the night, the ants came to the mixed basket in their thousands — and ants, as anyone who has dropped a sweet knows, can sort anything from anything.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"अब बस वह खुली टोकरी बची थी, और नदी, और छलनी में पानी भरकर लाने की साफ़ नामुमकिन बात।","lang":"hi","body":"That left the open basket, and the river, and the flat impossibility of carrying water in a sieve.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"आकाश के घर ने साफ़ पहाड़, छाँटी हुई टोकरी, और उस नामुमकिन पानी को देखा। \"तुमने यह सब अकेले नहीं किया,\" आकाश ने कहा। \"नहीं,\" अबो तानी ने हँसमुख होकर कहा। \"कोई भी काम कोई अकेले नहीं करता। मुझे लगा परीक्षा ही यही थी।\" और कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि आकाश का घर हँस पड़ा — क्योंकि परीक्षा सचमुच यही थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The house of the sky looked at the cleared hill, the sorted basket, the impossible water. \"You did not do these alone,\" said the sky. \"No,\" said Abo Tani cheerfully. \"Nobody does anything alone. I thought that was the test.\" And the sky's house, the tellings say, laughed — because it was.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"\"तो अबो तानी ने अपनी आसमानी दुल्हन से शादी कर ली, शादी में हवा और चींटियाँ भी थीं और काई भी, शायद पानी के घड़ों के पास कहीं। और उनके बच्चे, और उनके बच्चों के बच्चे, आगे चलकर तानी लोग बने — आदि, न्यीशी, आपातानी, गालो, तागिन।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So Abo Tani married his sky bride, with the wind and the ants at the wedding and the moss, presumably, somewhere near the water pots. And their children, and their children's children, became the Tani peoples — the Adi, the Nyishi, the Apatani, the Galo, the Tagin.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.abotani-sky-bride-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.abotani-sky-bride:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Abo Tani Married the Sky","text":"\"और यह बात ज़रा ठहरकर कहने लायक है: इन कहानियों में, आज का हर तानी इंसान एक तरफ से धरती का और दूसरी तरफ से खुद आसमान के घर का वंशज है। आधी पहाड़ी, आधी रोशनी। उनके बड़े-बुजुर्ग कहते हैं कि इससे बहुत सी बातें समझ में आती हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Which is a thing worth saying slowly: in these tellings, every Tani person alive is descended from the earth on one side and the sky's own house on the other. Half hill, half light. It explains a lot, their elders say.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-abotani-sky-bride.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.abotani-sky-bride|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tawang-horse-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tawang-horse:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Horse Who Chose the Monastery","text":"\"अरुणाचल प्रदेश के सुदूर पश्चिम में, ऊँचाई पर जहाँ हवा पतली है और प्रार्थना के झंडे कभी ठहरते नहीं, वहाँ मोनपा लोग रहते हैं, जो बुद्ध के रास्ते पर चलते हैं। और उनकी घाटियों के ऊपर पूरे हिमालय के सबसे बड़े मठों में से एक खड़ा है — तवांग। मोनपा लोग बताते हैं कि इस मठ को अपनी यह जगह कैसे मिली।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the far west of Arunachal Pradesh, up where the air is thin and the prayer flags never stop moving, live the Monpa people, who follow the Buddha's path. And above their valleys stands one of the largest monasteries in all the Himalaya — Tawang. The Monpa tell this about how it found its place.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tawang-horse.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tawang-horse|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tawang-horse-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tawang-horse:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Horse Who Chose the Monastery","text":"\"तीन सौ से भी ज़्यादा साल पहले, मेरा लामा नाम के एक लामा को इन पहाड़ों में एक विशाल मठ बनाने का काम सौंपा गया था। कोई मठ यूँ ही कहीं भी नहीं खड़ा कर दिया जाता। वहाँ पानी होना चाहिए, तेज़ हवाओं से ओट होनी चाहिए, ज़मीन ऐसी जो उसे संभाल सके, और एक ऐसी चीज़ जिसका नाम लेना मुश्किल है — एक सही जगह होने का अहसास।\"","lang":"hi","body":"More than three hundred years ago, a lama called Mera Lama was charged with building a great monastery in these mountains. A monastery is not put just anywhere. It must have water, and shelter from the worst winds, and ground that can hold it, and something harder to name — a rightness.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tawang-horse.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tawang-horse|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tawang-horse-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tawang-horse:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Horse Who Chose the Monastery","text":"\"मेरा लामा खोजते रहे। एक के बाद दूसरी पहाड़ी, एक के बाद दूसरी घाटी, उन्होंने हर जगह को परखा और हर जगह बस लगभग सही थी, जो ग़लत होने का सबसे थका देने वाला रूप है। और एक शाम, खोज में गहरे डूबे हुए, वे प्रार्थना करने रुके — और जब वे प्रार्थना से उठे, तो उनका घोड़ा गायब था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Mera Lama searched. Ridge after ridge, valley after valley, he weighed each place and each place was almost right, which is the most tiring kind of wrong. And one evening, deep in the search, he stopped to pray — and when he rose from his prayers, his horse was gone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tawang-horse.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tawang-horse|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tawang-horse-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tawang-horse:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Horse Who Chose the Monastery","text":"\"ऊँचे पहाड़ों में आप भले ही बहुत-सी चीज़ें आसानी से खो बैठें, पर घोड़ा उनमें से नहीं है। वे पैदल ही उसके पीछे निकल पड़े — बुरांश के पेड़ों के बीच से ऊपर चढ़ते हुए, पहाड़ी की ढलान पार करते हुए, खुरों के निशानों के पीछे-पीछे, और उधर दिन का उजाला लगातार ढलता जा रहा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"You may lose many things lightly in the high mountains. A horse is not one of them. He went after it on foot — up through the rhododendrons, over a shoulder of hill, following the prints, and the light going all the while.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tawang-horse.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tawang-horse|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tawang-horse-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tawang-horse:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Horse Who Chose the Monastery","text":"\"उन्हें वह घोड़ा पहाड़ के एक ऊँचे और खुले ढलान पर शांत खड़ा मिला, आराम से चरता हुआ, मानो वह अपनी मंज़िल पर पहुँच गया हो। और मेरा लामा पीछा करना छोड़कर ठहर गए, और खड़े होकर अपने चारों तरफ देखा — सचमुच आँखें खोलकर देखा — उस जगह को, जिसे उनके घोड़े ने चुना था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He found the horse standing still on a high open shoulder of mountain, grazing peacefully, as though it had arrived somewhere. And Mera Lama stopped chasing and stood, and looked around him — really looked — at the place his horse had picked.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tawang-horse.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tawang-horse|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tawang-horse-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tawang-horse:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Horse Who Chose the Monastery","text":"\"पास ही पानी। पीछे की पहाड़ी हवा को रोकती हुई। नीचे खुली किताब की तरह फैली घाटियाँ, और पीछे गवाह बनकर खड़ी ऊँची चोटियाँ। उन सभी महीनों में उन्होंने जितनी भी 'लगभग सही' जगहें परखी थीं — और उनका घोड़ा बिना किसी सोच-विचार के चुपचाप चल पड़ा था, और पहाड़ों की सबसे सही जगह के बीचों-बीच जाकर खड़ा हो गया था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Water near. The wind broken by the ridge at its back. The valleys spread below like an open book, and the high peaks standing witness behind. Every almost-right place he had weighed all those months — and his horse had walked off, without a single opinion in its head, and stood down in the middle of the rightest place in the mountains.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tawang-horse.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tawang-horse|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tawang-horse-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tawang-horse:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Horse Who Chose the Monastery","text":"\"वहीं वह मठ बना, और आज भी वहीं खड़ा है — और उसका नाम पूरी कहानी को सँभाले हुए है। तवांग: घोड़े द्वारा चुना गया। 'ता' यानी घोड़ा, और 'वांग' यानी चुनना। किसी मोनपा से पूछिए कि उनके इस महान मठ के नाम का क्या मतलब है, और वे आपको एक ऐसे लामा की बात बताएँगे जो इतने समझदार थे कि उन्होंने एक घोड़े की सलाह मान ली।\"","lang":"hi","body":"There the monastery was built, and there it stands — and its name remembers the whole story. Tawang: chosen by horse. Ta for the horse, wang for the choosing. Ask a Monpa what the name of their great monastery means and they will tell you about a lama who was wise enough to take a horse's advice.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tawang-horse.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tawang-horse|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tawang-horse-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tawang-horse:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Horse Who Chose the Monastery","text":"\"आज तवांग में सैकड़ों भिक्षु रहते और पढ़ते हैं, मक्खन के दीये जलते हैं, और विशाल प्रार्थना कक्ष में घर से भी ऊँची बुद्ध की प्रतिमा है। और इस सब की कहानी के पीछे कहीं एक शाम है, एक प्रार्थना है, और चुपचाप दूर जाता हुआ एक घोड़ा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Today hundreds of monks live and study at Tawang, and the butter lamps burn, and the great prayer hall holds a Buddha figure taller than a house. And somewhere in the story of all of it is an evening, a prayer, and a horse quietly walking away.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tawang-horse.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tawang-horse|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.teesta-rangeet-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.teesta-rangeet:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Rivers","text":"सिक्किम के लेप्चा लोग बताते हैं कि उनकी दो महान नदियाँ कभी एक-दूसरे से प्यार करने वाले दो साथी थीं: रोंगन्यू, जिसे अब नक्शों में तीस्ता कहा जाता है, और रोंगीत, जिसका नाम आज भी वही है। वे ऊँची बर्फ़ में एक-दूसरे से बहुत दूर शुरू हुईं, और उन्होंने तय किया कि पहाड़ों से नीचे उतरकर नीचे घाटी में मिलेंगी।","lang":"hi","body":"The Lepcha of Sikkim tell that their two great rivers were once two who loved each other: Rongnyu, whom the maps now call the Teesta, and Rongeet, who keeps his name. They rose far apart in the high snows, and they agreed to come down through the mountains and meet in the valley below.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-teesta-rangeet.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.teesta-rangeet|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.teesta-rangeet-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.teesta-rangeet:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Rivers","text":"लेकिन पहली बार बहने वाली नदी को नीचे जाने का रास्ता नहीं पता होता—क्योंकि उससे पहले कोई कभी नीचे गया ही नहीं था। इसलिए दोनों ने एक-एक राह दिखाने वाला चुन लिया। रोंगन्यू ने परिल बू यानी साँप को चुना। रोंगीत ने तुत फ़ो यानी एक पहाड़ी चिड़िया को चुना। और आपको अभी से अंदाज़ा होने लगा होगा कि कहानी किस तरफ़ मुड़ रही है, है न?","lang":"hi","body":"But a river setting out for the first time does not know the way down — nobody had ever gone down before. So each took a guide. Rongnyu chose Paril bu, the snake. Rongeet chose Tut fo, a mountain bird. And you can already feel the story leaning, can't you.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-teesta-rangeet.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.teesta-rangeet|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.teesta-rangeet-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.teesta-rangeet:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Rivers","text":"साँप वैसे ही चला जैसे साँप चलते हैं: चुपचाप, धीरज से, ज़मीन से सटकर, ढलान का रास्ता चुनते हुए और उसी पर टिके रहते हुए। और रोंगन्यू लंबे, सहज घुमावों में उसके पीछे-पीछे नीचे बहती रही, रास्ते में छोटी धाराओं को समेटती हुई, और शांत, भरपूर और समय से पहले घाटी में पहुँच गई।","lang":"hi","body":"The snake went as snakes go: smooth, patient, low, choosing the fall of the land and keeping to it. And Rongnyu followed him down in long easy curves, gathering streams as she went, arriving in the valley calm and full and early.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-teesta-rangeet.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.teesta-rangeet|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.teesta-rangeet-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.teesta-rangeet:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Rivers","text":"चिड़िया वैसे ही उड़ी जैसे चिड़ियाँ उड़ती हैं। उसे कोई देखने लायक चोटी दिखी तो वह उसे देखने लगी। उसका मन किसी बेर पर आ गया तो वह रास्ता बदलकर उधर उड़ गई। पूरी-पूरी दोपहर वह भूल ही जाती कि कोई उसके पीछे भी आ रहा है। और उसके पीछे रोंगीत तंग घाटियों में टकराता और मुड़ता हुआ, हर उस गलत घाटी में भटकता चला गया जहाँ चिड़िया की मौज उसे ले गई।","lang":"hi","body":"The bird went as birds go. He saw a ridge worth looking at and looked at it. He fancied a berry and detoured for it. He forgot, for whole afternoons, that anyone was following him at all. And behind him Rongeet went crashing and doubling through the gorges, taking every wrong valley the bird's fancy took.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-teesta-rangeet.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.teesta-rangeet|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.teesta-rangeet-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.teesta-rangeet:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Rivers","text":"इसलिए जब रोंगीत आखिरकार मिलने की जगह पर पहुँचा—थका-हारा, झाग छोड़ता हुआ, कई दिन देर से—तो रोंगन्यू पहले से ही वहाँ उसका इंतज़ार कर रही थी। और खुशी होने के बजाय, उसे सबसे पहले हार जाने की तीखी जलन महसूस हुई। \"थी सा था?\" वह चिल्लाया—\"तुम कब पहुँचीं?\" लेप्चा लोग आपको बताएंगे कि तीस्ता नाम उसी पुकार की याद दिलाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"So when Rongeet came down at last into the meeting place — tired, foaming, days behind — Rongnyu was already there, waiting. And instead of gladness, the first thing he felt was the hot rush of having been beaten. \"Thee sa tha?\" he cried — \"When did YOU arrive?\" The Lepcha will tell you the name Teesta remembers that very cry.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-teesta-rangeet.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.teesta-rangeet|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.teesta-rangeet-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.teesta-rangeet:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Rivers","text":"और अपने आहत स्वाभिमान में, रोंगीत पीछे हट गया और मुड़ने लगा—उलटा, ऊपर पहाड़ की तरफ़, दूर बहने लगा—और उसका पानी पूरी घाटी में ऊपर चढ़कर काँपने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"And in his hurt pride, Rongeet reared back and began to turn — to flow backwards, uphill, away — and the waters rose and trembled through the whole valley.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-teesta-rangeet.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.teesta-rangeet|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.teesta-rangeet-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.teesta-rangeet:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Rivers","text":"पानी शांत हो गया। रोंगीत आखिरी मील हौले-हौले बहती हुई आई, और दोनों नदियाँ आपस में मिल गईं — और तब से वे कभी अलग नहीं हुईं। आज भी तुम मेल्ली के नीचे उस संगम पर खड़े होकर उन्हें मिलते देख सकते हो: पानी के दो अलग-अलग रंग, जो फिसलकर एक हो जाते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The waters settled. Rongeet came the last mile gently, and the two rivers met — and they have never parted since. You can stand today at the meeting place below Melli and watch them join: two colours of water, sliding into one.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-teesta-rangeet.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.teesta-rangeet|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.teesta-rangeet-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.teesta-rangeet:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Rivers","text":"और लेपचा लोग कहते हैं कि खुद घाटी भी खुश हो गई थी। नदियों के उस मिलन पर, आज भी हवा तितलियों से भर जाती है — बादलों जैसे झुंड, जो उस पानी के ऊपर मँडराते रहते हैं जहाँ रोंगन्यू और रोंगीत मिली थीं। जाकर देखो। वे वहीं हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And the Lepcha say the valley itself was glad. At the joining of the rivers, to this day, the air fills with butterflies — clouds of them, drifting over the water where Rongnyu and Rongeet met. Go and see. They are there.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-teesta-rangeet.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.teesta-rangeet|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tendong-hill-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tendong-hill:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hill That Held Its People Up","text":"सिक्किम के लेपचा लोग बहुत पुराने ज़माने की एक बात बताते हैं, जब बारिश रुकने का नाम ही नहीं ले रही थी। कुछ कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि यह सब दोनों नदियों के झगड़े से शुरू हुआ; कुछ में कोई वजह नहीं बताई जाती, क्योंकि बारिश हमेशा वजह बताकर नहीं आती। घाटियाँ भर गईं। नदियाँ अपने किनारे भूल गईं। पानी बढ़ता ही चला गया।","lang":"hi","body":"The Lepcha of Sikkim tell of a time, deep in the long-ago, when the rains would not stop. Some tellings say it began with the quarrel of the two rivers; some do not say why at all, because rain does not always give reasons. The valleys filled. The rivers forgot their banks. The water rose.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tendong-hill.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tendong-hill|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tendong-hill-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tendong-hill:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hill That Held Its People Up","text":"लोग ऊपर चढ़ते गए, क्योंकि इसके सिवा कोई चारा भी नहीं था। उनके पीछे एक के बाद एक पहाड़ी डूबती चली गई। और कहानियाँ सच-सच बताती हैं कि उस वक़्त कैसा लग रहा था: उनकी जानी-पहचानी दुनिया उस मटमैले पानी के नीचे सिमटती जा रही थी, और कोई नहीं बता सकता था कि यह सिमटना कहाँ जाकर रुकेगा।","lang":"hi","body":"The people climbed, because that is all you can do. Hill after hill went under behind them. And the tellings are honest about how that felt: the world they knew was being folded away under grey water, and nobody could say where the folding would stop.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tendong-hill.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tendong-hill|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tendong-hill-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tendong-hill:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hill That Held Its People Up","text":"तभी, डूबी हुई घाटियों के ऊपर, एक पहाड़ी ने वह कर दिखाया जो कोई पहाड़ी नहीं करती। दक्षिणी सिक्किम में तेंदोंग पहाड़ी ऊपर उठने लगी। जैसे-जैसे पानी चढ़ा, पहाड़ी भी ऊपर उठती गई — उसने खुद को और अपने ऊपर मौजूद हर इंसान को बाढ़ से ऊपर उठा लिया, ठीक वैसे ही धीरज के साथ जैसे कोई दादाजी किसी बच्चे को पानी भरे गड्ढे के ऊपर उठा लेते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Then, above the drowned valleys, one hill did what no hill does. Tendong, in the south of Sikkim, rose. As the water climbed, the hill climbed — lifting itself, and everyone on it, above the flood, patient as a grandfather raising a child over a puddle.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tendong-hill.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tendong-hill|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tendong-hill-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tendong-hill:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hill That Held Its People Up","text":"कई दिनों तक वह पहाड़ी चोटी ही पूरा देश बनी रही — सबका एक गाँव, जो धूसर पानी और धूसर आसमान के बीच टिका था। सब एक-दूसरे को गर्माहट दे रहे थे और नन्हे-मुन्नों को किनारे से दूर रख रहे थे, जबकि उनके नीचे तेंडोंग डटा रहा, और डटा रहा, और डटा रहा।","lang":"hi","body":"For days the hilltop was the whole country — a village of everyone, perched between grey water and grey sky, keeping each other warm and keeping the little ones from the edge, while below them Tendong held, and held, and held.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tendong-hill.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tendong-hill|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tendong-hill-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tendong-hill:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hill That Held Its People Up","text":"और फिर एक सुबह बारिश बस थम गई। पानी बिना किसी हड़बड़ी के घटने लगा, बिल्कुल वैसे ही जैसे वह आया था। एक-एक कगार के साथ दुनिया लौट आई — धुली हुई, बदली हुई, पर वहीं मौजूद। और लोग तेंडोंग से उतरकर उसमें आए, और फिर से नई शुरुआत की।","lang":"hi","body":"And then one morning the rain simply finished. The water began to go down, unhurried, the way it had come. Ridge by ridge the world came back — rinsed, changed, but there. And the people came down off Tendong into it, and began again.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tendong-hill.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tendong-hill|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tendong-hill-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tendong-hill:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hill That Held Its People Up","text":"वे भूले नहीं। तुम उस ज़मीन को नहीं भूलते जिसने तुम्हें थामे रखा। तब से हर साल — पीढ़ियों-दर-पीढ़ियों से, हर एक साल — लेपचा लोग उस पहाड़ का धन्यवाद करने ऊपर चढ़ते हैं। इस त्योहार को तेंडोंग ल्हो रम फ़ात कहा जाता है: तेंडोंग पहाड़ की पूजा। यह आज भी, हर अगस्त में मनाया जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"They did not forget. You do not forget the ground that held you up. Every year since — every single year, down all the generations — the Lepcha have climbed to thank the hill. The festival is called Tendong Lho Rum Faat: the worship of the Tendong hill. It is kept still, each August.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tendong-hill.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tendong-hill|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tendong-hill-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tendong-hill:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hill That Held Its People Up","text":"परिवार मिलकर ऊपर जाते हैं, पुरानी रस्में निभाई जाती हैं, और बच्चों को यह कहानी उसी पहाड़ पर सुनाई जाती है जहाँ यह घटी थी — जो किसी भी कहानी के लिए सबसे अच्छी पाठशाला है।","lang":"hi","body":"Families go up together, the old rites are said, and the children are told this story on the hill it happened on — which is the best classroom any story ever had.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tendong-hill.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tendong-hill|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khangchendzonga-five-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khangchendzonga-five:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Five Treasures of the Great Snow","text":"सिक्किम के ऊपर खांगचेंदजोंगा खड़ा है, जो दुनिया का तीसरा सबसे ऊँचा पर्वत है — और भूटिया तथा लेपचा लोगों के लिए, यह उससे कहीं बढ़कर है। इसका नाम धीरे-धीरे बोलो, वैसे ही जैसे भूटिया लोगों ने इसे नाम दिया था: खांग-चेन-द्ज़ों-गा। पाँच खज़ानों की महान बर्फ़। यह नाम महज़ एक विवरण नहीं है। यह तो खज़ानों की पूरी सूची है।","lang":"hi","body":"Over Sikkim stands Khangchendzonga, the third-highest mountain in the world — and to the Bhutia and the Lepcha, far more than that. Say its name slowly, the way the Bhutia gave it: Khang-chen-dzö-nga. The great snow of the five treasuries. The name is not a description. It is an inventory.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khangchendzonga-five.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khangchendzonga-five|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khangchendzonga-five-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khangchendzonga-five:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Five Treasures of the Great Snow","text":"\"पाँच चोटियाँ, पाँच ख़ज़ाने। कहानियों में इन्हें आमतौर पर ऐसे गिनाया जाता है: सोना, चाँदी और कीमती रत्न; अनाज; और पवित्र ग्रंथ — पावन ज्ञान। कुछ लोग इसमें नमक जोड़ते हैं, तो कुछ दवाइयाँ। यह सब कुछ पहाड़ के भीतर बंद है, दुनिया की सबसे गहरी बर्फ़ के नीचे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Five summits, five treasuries. The tellings usually count them so: gold, and silver, and precious stones; grain; and sacred books — the holy knowledge. Some add salt, some add medicines. Locked in the mountain, all of it, under the deepest snow on earth.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khangchendzonga-five.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khangchendzonga-five|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khangchendzonga-five-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khangchendzonga-five:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Five Treasures of the Great Snow","text":"\"और इन ख़ज़ानों के एक रखवाले भी हैं। ज़ोंगा, सिक्किम के रक्षक देवता, ऊँची बर्फ़ पर सवार होकर धरती की निगरानी करते हैं — पांग ल्हाबसोल के त्योहार पर आप उन्हें नृत्य के रूप में देख सकते हैं, लाल मुखौटा पहने हुए, भव्य, मानो पहाड़ को ही एक दिन के लिए एक चेहरा मिल गया हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the treasuries have a keeper. Dzönga, the guardian god of Sikkim, rides the high snows and watches over the land — you can see him danced at the festival of Pang Lhabsol, masked in red, magnificent, the mountain itself given a face for a day.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khangchendzonga-five.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khangchendzonga-five|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khangchendzonga-five-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khangchendzonga-five:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Five Treasures of the Great Snow","text":"\"अब यहाँ वह सवाल आता है जो सिक्किम का कोई भी बच्चा कभी न कभी ज़रूर पूछता है, और यह सवाल बिल्कुल सही है: अगर पहाड़ सोने और अनाज से भरा है, तो कोई वहाँ जाकर उसे ले क्यों नहीं आता?\"","lang":"hi","body":"Now here is the question a child in Sikkim eventually asks, and it is the right question: if the mountain is full of gold and grain, why does nobody go and get it?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khangchendzonga-five.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khangchendzonga-five|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khangchendzonga-five-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khangchendzonga-five:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Five Treasures of the Great Snow","text":"\"सोचिए कि इससे ख़ज़ाने का क्या मतलब हो जाता है। जो सोना आप ख़र्च कर देते हैं, वह ख़त्म हो जाता है। पर जो सोना पहरे में इंतज़ार करता है, उस दिन के लिए जब सबको उसकी ज़रूरत होगी — वह सिर्फ़ दौलत नहीं रह जाता। वह उम्मीद की एक ऐसी जमा-पूँजी बन जाता है, जिसे साढ़े आठ हज़ार मीटर की ऊँचाई पर सहेज कर रखा गया है, जहाँ किसी का लालच नहीं पहुँच सकता।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Think what that does to a treasure. Gold you spend is gone. Gold that waits, guarded, for the day everyone needs it — that is not wealth any more. That is a reserve of hope, parked where nobody's greed can reach it, at eight and a half thousand metres.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khangchendzonga-five.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khangchendzonga-five|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khangchendzonga-five-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khangchendzonga-five:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Five Treasures of the Great Snow","text":"\"इससे पहाड़ को देखने का नज़रिया ही बदल जाता है। किसी साफ़ सुबह पूरा सिक्किम इसे देख सकता है — और पुरानी परंपरा कहती है कि वे जो देख रहे हैं, वह दुनिया का आपातकालीन भंडार है, जिसे इसके रक्षक ने पूरी निष्ठा से संभाल कर रखा है और जिसकी अभी तक किसी को ज़रूरत नहीं पड़ी। उन पाँच चोटियों पर हर सूर्योदय यह अच्छी ख़बर है कि सबसे बुरा दिन अभी नहीं आया है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It changes how you look at the mountain. On a clear morning the whole of Sikkim can see it — and what they are seeing, the old tradition says, is the world's emergency store, kept faithfully by its guardian, needed by nobody yet. Every sunrise on those five summits is the good news that the worst day has still not come.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khangchendzonga-five.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khangchendzonga-five|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khangchendzonga-five-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khangchendzonga-five:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Five Treasures of the Great Snow","text":"\"यही वजह है कि चोटी पर पाँव नहीं रखा जाता। 1955 में जब पर्वतारोही पहली बार ऊपर पहुँचे थे, तो वे आदर के कारण मुख्य चोटी से ज़रा पहले ही रुक गए थे, और तब से ज़्यादातर लोगों ने ऐसा ही किया है। आप ख़ज़ाने की चौखट तक जा सकते हैं। पर आप तहख़ाने की छत पर खड़े नहीं होते।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It is why the summit is not stood upon. When climbers first reached the top in 1955, they stopped short of the very summit out of respect, and most have done the same since. You may visit the treasury's doorstep. You do not stand on the roof of the vault.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khangchendzonga-five.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khangchendzonga-five|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabi-lungchok-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabi-lungchok:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brothers of the Standing Stones","text":"\"बहुत समय पहले सिक्किम में, दो समुदाय एक छोटे, ढलानों से भरे और खूबसूरत देश को आपस में साझा करने लगे। लेपचा लोग तो यादों से भी पुराने वक्त से वहाँ रह रहे थे — बर्फ़ीली चोटी की संतान। भूटिया लोग उत्तर के ऊँचे दर्रों को पार करके अपने याकों और प्रार्थना के झंडों के साथ आए थे। घाटियाँ वही थीं। भाषाएँ अलग। सब कुछ अलग।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Long ago in Sikkim, two peoples found themselves sharing one small, steep, beautiful country. The Lepcha had been there since before memory — the children of the snowy peak. The Bhutia had come over the high passes from the north with their yaks and their prayer flags. Same valleys. Different languages. Different everything.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabi-lungchok.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabi-lungchok|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabi-lungchok-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabi-lungchok:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brothers of the Standing Stones","text":"\"और हर कोई जानता है कि ऐसी कहानी का अगला हिस्सा क्या होता है, क्योंकि दुनिया इसे हज़ारों बार देख चुकी है: पहले शक, फिर झगड़े, और फिर उससे भी बुरा। दोनों समुदायों के मुखिया — लेपचा लोगों के महान बुज़ुर्ग थेकॉन्ग टेक, और भूटिया सरदार ख्ये बुमसा — दोनों ही इस आने वाले मोड़ को देख सकते थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And everyone knows the usual next chapter of that story, because the world has told it a thousand times: suspicion, then quarrels, then worse. The leaders of the two peoples — Thekong Tek, the great Lepcha elder, and Khye Bumsa, the Bhutia chief — could each see that chapter coming.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabi-lungchok.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabi-lungchok|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabi-lungchok-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabi-lungchok:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brothers of the Standing Stones","text":"\"इसलिए उन्होंने एक अलग कहानी रचने का फैसला किया। वे उत्तर में काबी लुंगचोक नाम की जगह पर, पेड़ों के बीच एक खुले मैदान में मिले — व्यापार करने नहीं, घाटियों को आपस में बाँटने नहीं, बल्कि कुछ इससे भी बड़ा करने: भाई बनने के लिए। दोस्त नहीं। भाई। बाक़ायदा, हमेशा-हमेशा के लिए, दोनों समुदाय एक साथ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So they chose to write a different one. They met at a place called Kabi Lungchok, in the north, in a clearing among the trees — not to trade, not to divide the valleys up, but to do something bigger: to become brothers. Not friends. Brothers. Formally, permanently, both peoples at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabi-lungchok.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabi-lungchok|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabi-lungchok-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabi-lungchok:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brothers of the Standing Stones","text":"\"पेड़ों के पार खड़े पहाड़ को गवाह मानकर, दोनों सरदारों ने लेपचा और भूटिया के बीच भाईचारे की कसम खाई — और उन्होंने काबी लुंगचोक में बड़े-बड़े पत्थर खड़े किए ताकि यह कसम अपनी जगह टिकी रहे, ठीक वैसे जैसे आप किसी ज़रूरी कागज़ पर कोई वज़न रख देते हैं, बस यहाँ वज़न ग्रेनाइट का था और वह कागज़ हमेशा के लिए था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"With the mountain standing witness over the trees, the two chiefs swore the bond of brothers between Lepcha and Bhutia — and they raised standing stones at Kabi Lungchok to hold the oath in place, the way you would set a weight on an important paper, except the weight was granite and the paper was forever.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabi-lungchok.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabi-lungchok|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabi-lungchok-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabi-lungchok:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brothers of the Standing Stones","text":"\"और वह कसम क़ायम रही। पूरी तरह से बिना किसी कमी के तो नहीं — दो समुदायों की कोई भी लंबी कहानी एकदम परिपूर्ण नहीं होती — लेकिन वह वैसे ही टिकी रही जैसे वे पत्थर टिके रहे: हर मौसम में, सदियों के पार, और उन तमाम बातों के बीच जो आम तौर पर ऐसे वादों को मिटा देती हैं। लेपचा और भूटिया ने आपस में रिश्ते जोड़े, मिलकर दावतें उड़ाईं, खेती की और साथ मिलकर दुख बाँटे — अपनी पसंद से बने हुए भाई।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the oath held. Not perfectly — no long story of two peoples is perfect — but it held the way the stones held: through weathers, through centuries, through everything that usually wears such promises away. Lepcha and Bhutia married, feasted, farmed and mourned together, brothers by their own choosing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabi-lungchok.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabi-lungchok|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabi-lungchok-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabi-lungchok:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brothers of the Standing Stones","text":"\"हर साल पांग ल्हाबसोल पर, जब सिक्किम अपने रक्षक पर्वत का आदर करता है, तब उस कसम को भी याद किया जाता है — यह त्योहार दोनों को एक साथ मनाता है, रक्षक को भी और भाईचारे को भी, क्योंकि सिक्किम में ये दोनों एक ही याद हैं: वह दिन जब पर्वत से दो समुदायों को उनके वादे पर कायम रखने को कहा गया था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every year at Pang Lhabsol, when Sikkim honours its guardian mountain, the oath is remembered too — the festival carries both at once, the guardian and the brotherhood, because in Sikkim the two are the same memory: the day the mountain was asked to hold two peoples to their word.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabi-lungchok.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabi-lungchok|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabi-lungchok-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabi-lungchok:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brothers of the Standing Stones","text":"\"और वे पत्थर आज भी वहीं हैं। आप आज भी गंगटोक से उत्तर की सड़क पर काबी लुंगचोक जा सकते हैं, और उनके सामने खड़े हो सकते हैं: जिन पर कुछ लिखा नहीं है, जिन्हें पढ़ा नहीं जा सकता, पर जिनका मतलब बिल्कुल साफ है। दो समुदायों ने एक परिवार बनने का फैसला किया, और अपनी सबसे बड़ी जानी-पहचानी चीज़ से कहा कि वह उन्हें इस वादे पर बाँधे रखे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the stones are still there. You can visit Kabi Lungchok today, on the road north from Gangtok, and stand in front of them: unwritten, unreadable, and perfectly clear. Two peoples decided to be family, and told the biggest thing they knew to hold them to it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabi-lungchok.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabi-lungchok|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mutanchi-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mutanchi:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Children of the Snowy Peak","text":"\"हर समुदाय के पास इस सबसे पुराने सवाल का एक जवाब होता है — हम कहाँ से आए हैं? — और सिक्किम के लेप्चा लोगों का जवाब शायद इन पहाड़ों में सबसे खूबसूरत है। उनकी कहानियों के मुताबिक, वे खुद उसी पर्वत से आए हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every people carries an answer to the oldest question — where do we come from? — and the Lepcha answer of Sikkim may be the most beautiful one in these mountains. They come, their telling says, from the mountain itself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mutanchi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mutanchi|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mutanchi-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mutanchi:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Children of the Snowy Peak","text":"\"शुरुआत में, इतबु-मू — सृष्टि रचने वाली माँ — ने बच्चों की चाह की। और उन्होंने उन्हें न तो मिट्टी से गढ़ा, न लकड़ी से, और न ही निचली गर्म घाटियों की किसी चीज़ से। उन्होंने खांगचेंदजोंगा के शिखर तक हाथ बढ़ाया और उसकी सबसे ऊँची चोटियों की सबसे पवित्र और ताज़ा बर्फ ली, और उसी से पहले पुरुष और पहली स्त्री को गढ़ा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the beginning, Itbu-mu — the Mother Creator — wished for children. And she did not shape them from clay, or from wood, or from anything of the low warm valleys. She reached to the crown of Khangchendzonga and took the purest, freshest snow of its highest peaks, and from it she shaped the first man and the first woman.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mutanchi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mutanchi|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mutanchi-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mutanchi:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Children of the Snowy Peak","text":"\"कहानियों में उनके नाम फुदोंगथिंग और नाज़ोंग-न्यु बताए गए हैं। और उन्हीं दोनों से लेप्चा समुदाय की शुरुआत हुई — इसीलिए, जब आप किसी लेप्चा से पूछेंगे कि वे कौन हैं, तो शायद आपको वह पुराना नाम सुनने को मिले जो उन्होंने अपने लिए रखा है: मुतांची रोंगकुप। यानी बर्फीली चोटी की संतान।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Fudongthing and Nazong-nyu, the tellings name them. And from those two came the Lepcha people — which is why, when you ask a Lepcha who they are, you may hear the old name they keep for themselves: Mutanchi Rongkup. The children of the snowy peak.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mutanchi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mutanchi|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mutanchi-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mutanchi:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Children of the Snowy Peak","text":"\"जरा एक पल के लिए इस बात पर रुकिए, क्योंकि यह जिस भी चीज़ को छूती है, सब बदल देती है। अगर आपके सबसे पहले पूर्वज पहाड़ की ही बर्फ से गढ़े गए थे, तो पहाड़ कोई देखने का नज़ारा नहीं है, न ही कोई जायदाद है, और न ही चढ़ाई करने की कोई चुनौती।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Stop on that for a moment, because it changes everything it touches. If your first ancestors were shaped from the mountain's own snow, then the mountain is not scenery, and not property, and not a challenge to be climbed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mutanchi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mutanchi|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mutanchi-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mutanchi:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Children of the Snowy Peak","text":"\"और इसी बात ने लेप्चा लोगों को एक खास तरह का बना दिया: ऐसे लोग जो अपने रिश्तेदारों का ख्याल रखते हैं। अपने सबसे बड़े बुजुर्ग की गोद में रहते हुए, उन्होंने उसके पूरे घर-संसार को अच्छी तरह समझ लिया — लेप्चा लोगों के पास अपनी पहाड़ियों की लगभग हर चिड़िया, हर तितली, हर पौधे और हर झरने के लिए अपने नाम हैं, जीती-जागती दुनिया का पूरा का पूरा पारिवारिक बहीखाता।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And it made the Lepcha a particular kind of people: the kind that pays attention to relatives. Living in the lap of their eldest kin, they learned its household completely — the Lepcha have their own names for nearly every bird, every butterfly, every plant and stream of their hills, a whole family register of the living world.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mutanchi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mutanchi|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mutanchi-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mutanchi:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Children of the Snowy Peak","text":"\"अपने पोते-पोतियों को यह बात सुनाते हुए एक लेप्चा दादी इसे सीधे-सादे ढंग से कहेंगी: \\\"पहाड़ हमारे आने से पहले यहाँ था, और हम उसी चीज़ से बने हैं जिससे वह बना है। इसलिए नदियाँ तुम्हारी रिश्तेदार हैं, और जंगल तुम्हारे रिश्तेदार हैं, और रिश्तेदारों से कोई चोरी नहीं करता, और न ही कोई उन्हें भूलता है।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"A Lepcha grandmother, telling this to her grandchildren, will put it simply: \"The mountain was here before us, and we are made of what it is made of. So the rivers are your relatives, and the forests are your relatives, and you do not steal from relatives, and you do not forget them.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mutanchi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mutanchi|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mutanchi-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mutanchi:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Children of the Snowy Peak","text":"\"जब पहले पर्वतारोही खांगचेंदजोंगा पर कदम रखने आए, तो सिक्किम ने उनसे बिल्कुल चोटी से थोड़ा पहले ही रुक जाने को कहा — और वे रुक गए, और तब से ज़्यादातर लोग ऐसा ही करते आए हैं। दुनिया इसे स्थानीय मान्यताओं का सम्मान करना कहती है। लेप्चा लोग इसे और अपनेपन से कहेंगे: मेहमान समझ गए थे कि वे किसी के दादा-दादी के घर में हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When the first climbers came to stand on Khangchendzonga, Sikkim asked them to stop short of the very top — and they did, and most have since. The world calls that respecting local belief. The Lepcha would say it more warmly: guests understood they were in somebody's grandparent's house.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mutanchi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mutanchi|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.snow-keeper-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.snow-keeper:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shy Keeper of the High Snows","text":"\"सिक्किम के आखिरी गाँवों के ऊपर, याक के चरागाहों के ऊपर, यहाँ तक कि प्रार्थना वाले झंडों के भी ऊपर, एक ऐसा इलाका है जो किसी का नहीं है — ऊँची बर्फ का इलाका। सिवाय इसके कि जो चरवाहे उसके पास गर्मियाँ बिताते हैं, भूटिया और लेप्चा दोनों, वे आपसे धीरे से कहेंगे कि वह सचमुच किसी का तो है। बस वे आपको ठीक-ठीक यह नहीं बता पाएँगे कि वह दिखता कैसा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Above the last villages of Sikkim, above the yak pastures, above even the prayer flags, there is a country that belongs to nobody — the high snows. Except that the herders who summer up near it, Bhutia and Lepcha both, will quietly tell you it does belong to somebody. They just could not tell you exactly what he looks like.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-snow-keeper.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.snow-keeper|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.snow-keeper-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.snow-keeper:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shy Keeper of the High Snows","text":"\"अलग-अलग घाटियों में लोग उसे अलग-अलग नामों से पुकारते हैं — बर्फ़ का जंगली आदमी, ग्लेशियर वाला; और बाहर की दुनिया उसे यति कहती है। लेपचा लोग, जो अपनी पहाड़ियों की हर चीज़ का नाम रखते हैं, ग्लेशियर की इस रूह को उन जीवों में गिनते हैं जिन्हें समझदार इंसान दूर ही से नमस्कार करता है। पर जिस बात पर सब सहमत हैं, वह सबसे ज़रूरी है: वह बहुत शर्मीला है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He goes by different names in different valleys — the wild man of the snows, the glacier one; the world outside calls him the yeti. The Lepcha, who name everything in their hills, count the spirit of the glaciers among the beings a sensible person greets from a distance. What everyone agrees on is the important part: he is shy.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-snow-keeper.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.snow-keeper|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.snow-keeper-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.snow-keeper:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shy Keeper of the High Snows","text":"\"ख़ूंख़ार नहीं। शर्मीला। उससे जुड़ी सारी कहानियाँ इशारों की कहानियाँ हैं: भोर के वक़्त बर्फ़ के मैदान को पार करते बड़े-बड़े पैरों के निशान, जो किसी ख़ास मक़सद से कहीं जा रहे हों। कोहरे में किसी पहाड़ी कगार से आती सीटी की आवाज़, जिसका जवाब कोई नहीं देता। नीली भेड़ों का एक झुंड जो किसी चट्टान के पास से यूँ मुड़कर निकल जाए जैसे वहाँ कोई खड़ा हो। वह रखवाला खुद कभी नहीं दिखता। बस वही जगह दिखती है जहाँ वह अभी-अभी मौजूद था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Not fierce. Shy. The stories are all sideways stories: a line of great prints crossing a snowfield at dawn, going somewhere with a purpose. A whistle off a ridge in the mist, answered by nothing. A herd of blue sheep flowing round a rock as though someone stood there. Never the keeper himself. Always the space where he just was.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-snow-keeper.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.snow-keeper|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.snow-keeper-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.snow-keeper:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shy Keeper of the High Snows","text":"\"गर्मियों के एक ऊँचे चरागाह में, एक लड़के ने अपने दादाजी से इस बारे में पूछा — ठीक वैसे ही जैसे आग धीमी पड़ने पर बात छेड़ी जाती है। \\\"क्या वह सचमुच होता है?\\\" दादाजी ने कुछ देर चाय का कटोरा घुमाया। उन्होंने कहा, \\\"ऊँचे पहाड़ों की बर्फ़ शांत और साफ़-सुथरी है और कोई उन्हें परेशान नहीं करता। कोई तो यह काम कर रहा है। और यह बात उतनी ही सच है जितनी बाकी चीज़ें।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"A boy at a high summer pasture asked his grandfather about it, the way you do when the fire is low. \"Is he real?\" His grandfather turned his tea bowl a while. \"The high snows are quiet and clean and nobody troubles them,\" he said. \"Somebody is doing that job. That is as real as most things.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-snow-keeper.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.snow-keeper|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.snow-keeper-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.snow-keeper:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shy Keeper of the High Snows","text":"\"दादाजी ने कहा, \\\"जब हम वहाँ ऊपर जाते हैं, तो संभलकर और हौले से चलते हैं। अपना कचरा घर वापस लाते हैं। पहाड़ियों की चोटियों पर चिल्लाते नहीं हैं। इसलिए नहीं कि हम डरते हैं — बल्कि इसलिए कि वह इलाक़ा उसका है, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे यह चरागाह हमारा है, और वह कभी हमारे लिए बुरा पड़ोसी नहीं बना।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"When we walk up there,\" his grandfather said, \"we walk gently. We take our rubbish home. We do not shout on the ridges. Not because we are afraid — because it is his, the way our pasture is ours, and he has never once been a bad neighbour to us.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-snow-keeper.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.snow-keeper|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.snow-keeper-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.snow-keeper:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shy Keeper of the High Snows","text":"\"और बर्फ़ के उस रखवाले की सबसे प्यारी बात यही है: एक ऐसा जीव जिसकी पूरी कहानी चीज़ों को उनके हाल पर छोड़ देने की सीख देती है। पहाड़ उसे कुछ ऐसे सँभालकर रखते हैं जैसे जेब में कोई क़ीमती चीज़ रखी हो — नज़रों से ओझल, और इसी में उसकी भलाई है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And that is the loveliest thing about the keeper of the snows: a being whose whole story is a lesson in leaving things be. The mountains hold him the way a pocket holds something precious — unseen, and better for it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-snow-keeper.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.snow-keeper|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.losoong-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.losoong:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Year Is Swept Out Dancing","text":"जब फ़सलें समेट ली जाती हैं और ऊँचे दर्रे बर्फ़ से सफ़ेद हो जाते हैं, तब सिक्किम में नया साल करवट लेता है। भूटिया लोग इस त्योहार को लोसूंग कहते हैं; और लेपचा लोग इसी बदलते मौसम में अपना त्योहार नामसूंग मनाते हैं — दो समुदाय, दो नाम, और दिसंबर की एक ही साझी ख़ुशी: कोठार भरे हुए हैं, सारा काम पूरा हो चुका है, अब पुराना साल विदा ले सकता है।","lang":"hi","body":"When the harvest is in and the high passes have gone white, Sikkim turns the year. The Bhutia call the festival Losoong; the Lepcha keep their own, Namsoong, in the same turning season — two peoples, two names, one shared December gladness: the granaries are full, the work is done, the year may now leave.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-losoong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.losoong|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.losoong-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.losoong:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Year Is Swept Out Dancing","text":"एक बच्ची ने यह त्योहार अपनी दादी के गाँव में बिताया, और उसने जाना कि साल को विदा करना अपने आप में एक पूरा हुनर है। घर के एक कोने से दूसरे कोने तक झाड़ू लगाई गई — बिल्कुल ठीक से, हर कोने-अतरे तक, \"क्योंकि जितनी धूल तुम बचा लोगे, वह तुम्हारे पास ही रह जाएगी।\" जो कुछ ठीक किया जा सकता था, उसकी मरम्मत की गई। जो कुछ उधार लिया गया था, वह सब लौटा दिया गया।","lang":"hi","body":"A girl spent it at her grandmother's village, and found that seeing out a year is a whole craft. The house swept end to end — properly, into the corners, \"because whatever dust you keep, you keep.\" Everything mended that could be mended. Everything returned that had been borrowed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-losoong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.losoong|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.losoong-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.losoong:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Year Is Swept Out Dancing","text":"त्योहार से पहले के दिनों में, मठ के आँगन में मुखौटों वाला छम नृत्य घूम-घूमकर होता है — ढोल की धड़कन और लंबे बिगुलों की गूँज पर थिरकते धीमे, भव्य रूप। गाँव वालों ने समझाया कि ये नृत्य पुराने साल की मुश्किलों का डटकर सामना करते हैं, ताकि उनमें से कोई भी दबे पाँव नए साल में न घुस आए।","lang":"hi","body":"At the monastery, in the days before, the masked cham dances turn in the courtyard — slow, magnificent figures to a heartbeat of drums and long horns. The dances face down the troubles of the old year, the villagers explained, so that none of them slink along into the new one.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-losoong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.losoong|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.losoong-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.losoong:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Year Is Swept Out Dancing","text":"और फिर वह हिस्सा जिसका हर बच्चा इंतज़ार करता है: तीरंदाज़ी। तीरंदाज़ी के बिना लोसूंग भला कैसा लोसूंग! गाँव के आदमी दिन भर होड़ लगाते हैं — असली धनुष, गज़ब का ध्यान, और ज़ोरदार शेखी — और जब निशाने पर तीर धप से लगते हैं, तो ऐसी ललकार गूँजती है जो पूरी घाटी के पार तक सुनाई देती है।","lang":"hi","body":"And then the part every child waits for: archery. Losoong without archery is not Losoong. The men of the villages compete all day — real bows, tremendous concentration, spectacular boasting — and the arrows thud home to roars you can hear across the valley.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-losoong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.losoong|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.losoong-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.losoong:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Year Is Swept Out Dancing","text":"आख़िरी शाम, बच्ची ने अपनी दादी से वही सवाल पूछा, जो पूरे त्योहार भर उसके भीतर धीरे-धीरे आकार ले रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"On the last evening, the girl asked her grandmother the question the whole festival had been assembling in her.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-losoong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.losoong|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.losoong-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.losoong:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Year Is Swept Out Dancing","text":"\"लोग पुराने सालों का बोझ अपने साथ ढोते फिरते हैं,\" सिलाई-रफ़ू का आखिरी कपड़ा तह करते हुए उसकी दादी ने कहा। \"पुराने झगड़े, पुरानी नाराज़गियाँ, पुरानी धूल। साल में एक बार, हम जान-बूझकर यह सब उतार कर रख देते हैं। इसमें पूरा एक त्योहार लग जाता है, क्योंकि चीज़ों को छोड़ना, उन्हें उठाने से कहीं ज़्यादा मुश्किल होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"People carry old years around with them,\" her grandmother said, folding the last of the mending. \"Old quarrels, old sulks, old dust. Once a year, we put it all down on purpose. It takes a whole festival, because putting things down is harder than picking things up.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-losoong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.losoong|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.losoong-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.losoong:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Year Is Swept Out Dancing","text":"नए साल की सुबह पूरा गाँव घर-घर जाकर आपस में मिला, और हर किसी ने हर किसी को बधाई दी। यहाँ तक कि वे दो पुराने पड़ोसी भी मिले, जिनके बारे में बच्ची जानती थी कि वसंत में उनका झगड़ा हुआ था — साफ़-सुथरी चौखट पर, नए साल में, पिछले साल को अपने पीछे झाड़-पोंछ कर, वे एक-दूसरे को नमस्कार कर रहे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"On new year's morning the village visited itself house to house, and everyone greeted everyone, including two old neighbours the girl happened to know had quarrelled in the spring — greeting each other on a clean doorstep, in a new year, with last year swept out behind them both.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-losoong.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.losoong|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.seven-cities-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.seven-cities:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City Made of Cities","text":"दिल्ली की एक बच्ची ने अपने दादाजी से एक सीधा-सा सवाल पूछा — हमारा शहर कितना पुराना है? — और जवाब देने के बजाय, उन्होंने टहलने वाले जूते पहन लिए। \"दिल्ली कोई एक शहर नहीं है,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"यह शहरों का एक ढेर है। आओ, इन्हें गिनते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A girl in Delhi asked her grandfather a simple question — how old is our city? — and instead of answering, he put on his walking shoes. \"Delhi is not one city,\" he said. \"It is a pile of cities. Come and count them.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-seven-cities.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.seven-cities|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.seven-cities-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.seven-cities:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City Made of Cities","text":"उन्होंने महरौली में शुरुआत की, क़ुतुब मीनार की तलहटी से, जो मीनार इतनी ऊँची थी कि उसकी चोटी देखने के लिए बच्ची को अपना दुपट्टा संभालना पड़ा। \"पहला शहर,\" दादाजी ने कहा। \"जब बस इतना ही था, तब राजा यहीं से राज करते थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"They started in Mehrauli, at the foot of the Qutb Minar, a tower so tall she had to hold her dupatta to look at the top of it. \"City one,\" said her grandfather. \"Kings ruled from here when this was all there was.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-seven-cities.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.seven-cities|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.seven-cities-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.seven-cities:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City Made of Cities","text":"फिर सीरी, जहाँ पुरानी दीवारें अब चुपचाप पार्कों से होकर और घरों के पास से गुज़रती हैं। फिर तुग़लक़ाबाद, इतना बड़ा और पथरीला क़िला कि लगता है जैसे किसी पहाड़ ने इमारत बनने का फ़ैसला कर लिया हो। दूसरा शहर। तीसरा शहर।","lang":"hi","body":"Then Siri, where the old walls now wander through parks and past houses, minding their own business. Then Tughlaqabad, a fort so huge and stony it looks like a mountain that decided to become a building. City two. City three.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-seven-cities.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.seven-cities|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.seven-cities-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.seven-cities:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City Made of Cities","text":"जहाँपनाह, जिसके नाम का मतलब है दुनिया की पनाह, जिसने दो शहरों को समेटकर एक कर दिया। फ़िरोज़ाबाद, जहाँ फ़िरोज़ शाह का कोटला आज भी क्रिकेट के मैदान के पास खड़ा है, ताकि एक बहुत पुराना शहर और एक बहुत शोरगुल वाला शहर एक ही दीवार साझा कर सकें। चार। पाँच।","lang":"hi","body":"Jahanpanah, whose name means the Refuge of the World, folded two cities into one. Firozabad, where Firoz Shah's kotla still stands by the cricket ground, so that a very old city and a very loud one share a wall. Four. Five.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-seven-cities.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.seven-cities|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.seven-cities-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.seven-cities:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City Made of Cities","text":"पुराना क़िला पर — छठा शहर — बच्ची रुक गई। \"लेकिन असली दिल्ली कौन-सी है?\" उसने पूछा। दादाजी ऐसे मुस्कुराए जैसे कोई पूरे दिन से इसी सवाल का इंतज़ार कर रहा हो।","lang":"hi","body":"At the Purana Qila — the Old Fort, city six — the girl stopped. \"But which one is the real Delhi?\" she asked. Her grandfather smiled the smile of a man who has been waiting all day for a question.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-seven-cities.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.seven-cities|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.seven-cities-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.seven-cities:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City Made of Cities","text":"सातवाँ शहर था शाहजहानाबाद — लाल क़िला जिसकी दीवारें शाम के रंग जैसी हैं, जामा मस्जिद जिसकी सीढ़ियाँ कबूतरों से भरी हैं, और पुरानी दिल्ली की ऐसी चहल-पहल से भरी तंग गलियाँ कि हवा में भी खाने की ख़ुशबू महकती है।","lang":"hi","body":"City seven was Shahjahanabad — the Red Fort with its walls the colour of evening, the Jama Masjid with its steps full of pigeons, and the lanes of Old Delhi packed so tight with life that the air itself smells of food.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-seven-cities.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.seven-cities|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.seven-cities-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.seven-cities:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City Made of Cities","text":"“और फिर अंग्रेज़ों ने नई दिल्ली बनाई, यानी आठ शहर, और तब से हर कोई कुछ न कुछ बनाता ही जा रहा है, यानी कुल मिलाकर—” उसके दादाजी ने पूरे क्षितिज की तरफ़ हाथ घुमाया “—सच कहूँ तो मेरी तो गिनती ही छूट गई है।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"And then the British built New Delhi, which makes eight, and everyone since has kept building, which makes — \" her grandfather waved his hand at the whole horizon \" — I have honestly lost count.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-seven-cities.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.seven-cities|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.seven-cities-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.seven-cities:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City Made of Cities","text":"घर लौटती बस में उसने बाहर देखा—मकबरों के ऊपर खड़े फ़्लाईओवर, पुराने दरवाज़ों के पास से सरकती मेट्रो ट्रेनें, और उस दीवार के आगे क्रिकेट खेलते बच्चे जिसने कभी सुल्तानों को आते-जाते देखा था।","lang":"hi","body":"On the bus home she looked out at flyovers standing over tombs, and metro trains sliding past old gateways, and children playing cricket against a wall that had watched sultans go by.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-seven-cities.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.seven-cities|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.iron-pillar-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.iron-pillar:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nail That Came Loose","text":"दिल्ली के क़ुतुब परिसर के आँगन में लोहे का एक खंभा खड़ा है, चार आदमियों से भी ऊँचा, अपने आस-पास की लगभग हर चीज़ से पुराना। पंद्रह सौ से भी ज़्यादा सालों से इस पर बारिश बरस रही है। इस पर कभी ज़ंग नहीं लगा। वैज्ञानिक आज भी यह समझने आते हैं कि ऐसा क्यों है।","lang":"hi","body":"In the courtyard of the Qutb complex in Delhi stands an iron pillar, taller than four men, older than almost anything around it. Rain has fallen on it for more than fifteen hundred years. It has never rusted. Scientists still come to study why.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-iron-pillar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.iron-pillar|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.iron-pillar-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.iron-pillar:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nail That Came Loose","text":"इतनी बात तो सच है और तुम जाकर इसे देख भी सकते हो। लेकिन दिल्ली इस खंभे के बारे में एक और भी पुरानी कहानी सुनाती है—कि इसे वहाँ क्यों लगाया गया था, और तब क्या हुआ जब एक राजा के मन में उत्सुकता जागी।","lang":"hi","body":"That much is true and you can go and see it. But Delhi tells an older story about that pillar — about why it was put there, and what happened when a king got curious.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-iron-pillar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.iron-pillar|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.iron-pillar-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.iron-pillar:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nail That Came Loose","text":"कहते हैं कि यह खंभा ज़मीन में एक बड़ी कील की तरह गाड़ा गया था, और नीचे बहुत गहराई में, किसी भी कुएँ से भी गहरे, यह दुनिया को थामने वाले नागराज वासुकि के सिर पर टिका था। “जब तक यह कील खड़ी रहेगी,” ज्ञानियों ने राजा से कहा, “तब तक आपका राजसिंहासन टिका रहेगा।”","lang":"hi","body":"They say the pillar was driven into the earth like a great nail, and that far below, deeper than any well, it rested on the head of Vasuki, the king of the serpents who holds the world steady. \"As long as the nail stands,\" the wise men told the king, \"your throne stands.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-iron-pillar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.iron-pillar|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.iron-pillar-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.iron-pillar:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nail That Came Loose","text":"राजा अनंगपाल थे, और अनंगपाल का स्वभाव ऐसा था कि वे किसी बात को बिना छेड़े नहीं रह सकते थे। एक कील। एक नाग के सिर पर। उनके अपने ही आँगन के नीचे। नाश्ते के वक़्त वे उसी के बारे में सोचते। दरबार में भी उसी के बारे में सोचते। और रात को जब नींद न आती, तो बिस्तर पर लेटे-लेटे भी उसी के बारे में सोचते।","lang":"hi","body":"The king was Anangpal, and Anangpal had the kind of mind that cannot leave a thing alone. A nail. On a serpent's head. Under his own courtyard. He thought about it at breakfast. He thought about it at durbar. He thought about it lying awake at night.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-iron-pillar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.iron-pillar|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.iron-pillar-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.iron-pillar:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nail That Came Loose","text":"इसलिए एक सुबह उन्होंने हुक्म दे ही दिया। वह खंभा ज़मीन से बाहर निकाला गया — और कहते हैं कि उसका निचला सिरा गहरे लाल रंग से रंगा हुआ था, किसी ऐसी चीज़ से जो बहुत-बहुत नीचे से आई थी, इतनी गहराई से जहाँ कोई खुदाई कभी नहीं पहुँच पाती।","lang":"hi","body":"So one morning he ordered it done. The pillar came up out of the ground — and the end of it, they say, was stained deep red, with something from far, far below, from a depth no digging ever reaches.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-iron-pillar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.iron-pillar|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.iron-pillar-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.iron-pillar:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nail That Came Loose","text":"विद्वानों ने अपने चेहरे ढक लिए। \"इसे वापस लगा दो,\" उन्होंने कहा। और उसी घड़ी, पूजा-पाठ के साथ उसे वापस गाड़ दिया गया। लेकिन जो कील एक बार उखड़ जाए, वह फिर कभी मज़बूती से नहीं बैठती। वह खड़ा तो रहा — पर ढीला ही रहा। ढिल्ली।","lang":"hi","body":"The wise men covered their faces. \"Put it back,\" they said. And it was put back, that same hour, with prayers. But a nail that has once been pulled never again sits tight. It stood — but it stood loose. Dhilli.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-iron-pillar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.iron-pillar|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.iron-pillar-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.iron-pillar:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nail That Came Loose","text":"और लोग तुकबंदी में कहने लगे, जिसे दिल्ली आज भी याद रखती है: 'किल्ली तो ढिल्ली भई' — यानी कील ढीली हो गई। कुछ लोग कहते हैं कि शहर का नाम यहीं से पड़ा। ढिल्ली। डिल्ली। दिल्ली। ढीली कील का शहर।","lang":"hi","body":"And people began to say it in a rhyme that Delhi still remembers: killi to dhilli bhai — the nail has come loose. Some say that is where the city's name comes from. Dhilli. Dilli. Delhi. The city of the loosened nail.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-iron-pillar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.iron-pillar|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.iron-pillar-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.iron-pillar:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nail That Came Loose","text":"कहानी कहती है कि इसके बाद अनंगपाल का वंश ज़्यादा समय तक राजगद्दी पर नहीं टिका, और हज़ार साल तक दिल्ली का तख़्त बदलता ही रहा — मानो यह शहर खुद ही थोड़ा ढीला पड़ गया हो, और फिर कभी पूरी तरह जम ही न पाया हो।","lang":"hi","body":"Anangpal's line did not keep the throne long after that, says the story, and thrones in Delhi kept changing hands for a thousand years — as if the city itself had come a little loose, and never quite settled again.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-iron-pillar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.iron-pillar|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.razia-sultan-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.razia-sultan:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ruler Nobody Expected","text":"लगभग आठ सौ साल पहले, दिल्ली पर सुल्तान इल्तुतमिश का राज था। उनके कई बेटे थे और एक बेटी थी—रज़िया। बेटे तो राजकुमार थे और राजकुमारों की तरह ही रहते थे। पर रज़िया अपने पिता के पास बैठकर उन्हें काम करते देखती और समझती कि असल में राज कैसे चलाया जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Almost eight hundred years ago, Delhi was ruled by Sultan Iltutmish, who had many sons and one daughter, Razia. The sons were princes and behaved like it. Razia sat with her father while he worked, and watched how a kingdom is actually run.","art":"art/story/sm/it-razia-sultan.jpg","route":"#/story/it.razia-sultan|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.razia-sultan-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.razia-sultan:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ruler Nobody Expected","text":"उसने घुड़सवारी सीखी, अगुआई करना सीखा और राजकाज के कागज़ात पढ़ना सीखा। और इल्तुतमिश ने एक ऐसी बात देखी जिसे उस ज़माने के इतिहासकारों ने भी लिखा: उनके सब बच्चों में, एक शासक जैसी समझ सिर्फ़ इस बेटी के पास ही थी।","lang":"hi","body":"She learned to ride, to lead, to read the papers of state. And Iltutmish noticed something that the chroniclers of the time wrote down: of all his children, the one with a ruler's head on her shoulders was the daughter.","art":"art/story/sm/it-razia-sultan.jpg","route":"#/story/it.razia-sultan|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.razia-sultan-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.razia-sultan:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ruler Nobody Expected","text":"इसलिए उन्होंने वह किया जो दिल्ली के किसी सुल्तान ने पहले कभी नहीं किया था। उन्होंने अपने बाद राज संभालने के लिए रज़िया को चुना। दरबारी सन्न रह गए। \"एक बेटी? जबकि बेटे मौजूद हैं!\" पुरानी किताबों में उनका जवाब दर्ज है: मेरे बेटे तो ऐश-ओ-आराम में खोए हैं। यह अकेली उन सब पर भारी है।","lang":"hi","body":"So he did something no Sultan of Delhi had done. He named Razia as the one fit to rule after him. The nobles were horrified. \"A daughter? There are sons!\" The old chronicle records his answer: my sons are lost in their pleasures. She is worth more than all of them.","art":"art/story/sm/it-razia-sultan.jpg","route":"#/story/it.razia-sultan|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.razia-sultan-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.razia-sultan:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ruler Nobody Expected","text":"जब इल्तुतमिश चल बसे, तो दरबारियों ने उनकी बात नहीं मानी और एक बेटे को गद्दी पर बिठा ही दिया। बहुत जल्द सब कुछ बिगड़ने लगा। और साल भर के भीतर ही दिल्ली—वहाँ के दरबारी, वहाँ की फ़ौज और वहाँ की जनता—आख़िरकार उस बेटी के पास ही आई।","lang":"hi","body":"When Iltutmish died, the nobles ignored his wish and crowned a son anyway. It went badly, fast. And within a year, Delhi — its nobles, its army, its people — turned to the daughter after all.","art":"art/story/sm/it-razia-sultan.jpg","route":"#/story/it.razia-sultan|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.razia-sultan-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.razia-sultan:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ruler Nobody Expected","text":"उसने खुद को सुल्तान कहलवाया, सुल्ताना नहीं—सुल्ताना तो किसी सुल्तान की पत्नी होती, और वह किसी की पत्नी नहीं, खुद हुक्मरान थी। उसके नाम के सिक्के ढाले गए। कुछ सिक्के आज भी बचे हुए हैं। तुम किसी म्यूज़ियम में ऐसा सिक्का देख सकते हो और उस पर उसका नाम पढ़ सकते हो।","lang":"hi","body":"She called herself Sultan, not Sultana — a queen was a king's wife, and she was nobody's wife; she was the ruler. Coins were struck with her name on them. Some of those coins still exist. You can see one in a museum and read her name on it.","art":"art/story/sm/it-razia-sultan.jpg","route":"#/story/it.razia-sultan|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.razia-sultan-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.razia-sultan:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ruler Nobody Expected","text":"उसने पर्दा छोड़ दिया और सुल्तान का चोगा पहनकर, हाथी पर सवार होकर खुलेआम अपनी फ़ौज के आगे चली, ताकि उसके सैनिक और उसकी प्रजा साफ़ देख सकें कि उनकी अगुआई कौन कर रहा है। वह खुद लोगों की फ़रियादें सुनती थी। उसने अपने अफ़सर भी खुद चुने, सिर्फ़ उनकी काबिलियत देखकर।","lang":"hi","body":"She gave up the veil and rode openly at the head of her army on an elephant, dressed in a ruler's coat, so her soldiers and her people could see exactly who was leading them. She heard petitions herself. She appointed her own officers, on ability.","art":"art/story/sm/it-razia-sultan.jpg","route":"#/story/it.razia-sultan|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.razia-sultan-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.razia-sultan:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ruler Nobody Expected","text":"यह राज तीन-चार साल तक ही चला। उनके आसपास के कुछ ताकतवर लोगों के लिए यह बात बर्दाश्त से बाहर थी, जो किसी हुक्मरान की हर बात माफ कर सकते थे, सिवाय इसके कि वह उनसे बेहतर काम करे। वे उनके खिलाफ खड़े हो गए, और उनसे उनका राज छीन लिया गया।","lang":"hi","body":"It lasted between three and four years. That was too much for some of the powerful men around her, who could forgive a ruler almost anything except being better at the job than they were. They rose against her, and her rule was taken from her.","art":"art/story/sm/it-razia-sultan.jpg","route":"#/story/it.razia-sultan|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.razia-sultan-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.razia-sultan:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ruler Nobody Expected","text":"उस दौर के इतिहासकार मिन्हाज ने उनके बारे में साफ-साफ लिखा था: वे एक समझदार और इंसाफपसंद हुक्मरान थीं, जिनमें बादशाहों वाले सारे गुण थे — और फिर उन्होंने उदास होकर लिखा कि उस ज़माने के मर्दों की नज़र में, उनका औरत होना ही बाकी सब बातों पर भारी पड़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"The chronicler Minhaj, who lived in those times, wrote of her plainly: she was a wise and just ruler, with every kingly quality — and then he added, sadly, that in the eyes of the men of her age, being a woman outweighed all of it.","art":"art/story/sm/it-razia-sultan.jpg","route":"#/story/it.razia-sultan|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandni-chowk-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandni-chowk:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square of Moonlight","text":"जब शाहजहाँ ने अपना नया शहर शाहजहानाबाद बसाया — लाल किला, बड़ी मस्जिद और शहरपनाह — तो वहाँ का सबसे शानदार नया बाज़ार बादशाह ने बिल्कुल नहीं बनाया था। उसे उनकी बेटी, जहाँआरा बेगम ने तैयार किया था।","lang":"hi","body":"When Shah Jahan built his new city of Shahjahanabad — the Red Fort, the great mosque, the walls — the finest new bazaar in it was not designed by the emperor at all. It was designed by his daughter, Jahanara Begum.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandni-chowk.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandni-chowk|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandni-chowk-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandni-chowk:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square of Moonlight","text":"इमारतों को सजाने-संवारने में जहाँआरा का हुनर वैसा ही था, जैसा कुछ लोगों का संगीत में होता है। उन्होंने किले से निकलती दुकानों की एक लंबी, चौड़ी सड़क बनाई, जिसके बीच में एक हौज था, और — सबसे खास बात तो यह थी कि — पूरी सड़क के ठीक बीचों-बीच साफ पानी की एक नहर बहती थी।","lang":"hi","body":"Jahanara was clever with buildings the way some people are clever with music. She laid out a long, wide street of shops leading from the fort, with a pool at its centre, and — this was the touch — a canal of clear water running straight down the middle of the whole street.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandni-chowk.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandni-chowk|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandni-chowk-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandni-chowk:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square of Moonlight","text":"दिन में यह नहर सड़क को ठंडा रखती और पेड़ों को पानी देती। लेकिन यह कहानी तो रात की है। कहते हैं कि पूनम की रातों में, पानी चाँद को थाम लेता और झिलमिलाते हुए पूरे बाज़ार में बहा ले जाता — बंद दुकानों के बीच बहती चाँदी की रोशनी की एक लंबी लकीर।","lang":"hi","body":"By day the canal cooled the street and watered the trees. But the story is about the night. On full-moon nights, they say, the water caught the moon and carried it, shimmering, down the entire length of the bazaar — one long ribbon of silver light between the shuttered shops.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandni-chowk.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandni-chowk|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandni-chowk-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandni-chowk:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square of Moonlight","text":"और इस तरह लोगों ने उस सड़क को वही एक नाम दिया जो उस पर जँचता था: चाँदनी चौक। यानी चाँदनी का चौक।","lang":"hi","body":"And so people gave the street the only name that would do: Chandni Chowk. The moonlight square.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandni-chowk.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandni-chowk|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandni-chowk-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandni-chowk:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square of Moonlight","text":"वह नहर तो कब की गायब हो चुकी है — उसे पाट दिया गया, उस पर इमारतें बन गईं, और वह बस नाम में ही याद रह गई है। इससे एक पहेली बनती है: उस सड़क पर बहुत लंबे समय से चाँदनी नहीं दिखी है। तो क्या वह नाम भी चले जाना चाहिए था?","lang":"hi","body":"The canal is long gone — filled in, built over, remembered only in the name. Which leaves a puzzle: the moonlight has not been seen on that street for a very long time. Should the name have gone too?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandni-chowk.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandni-chowk|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandni-chowk-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandni-chowk:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square of Moonlight","text":"आज चाँदनी चौक भारत की सबसे भीड़-भाड़ वाली जगहों में से एक है — रिक्शे, शादी के लहँगों की दुकानें, सिर के ऊपर आसमान जितने बड़े चिड़िया के घोंसले जैसे उलझे तार, और तरह-तरह का खाना: एक गली में जलेबियाँ, तो एक पूरी गली ही पराठों की दुकानों से भरी हुई।","lang":"hi","body":"Today Chandni Chowk is one of the most crowded places in India — rickshaws, wedding-lehenga shops, wires overhead like a bird's nest the size of the sky, and food: jalebis in one lane, parathas in a lane entirely made of paratha shops.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandni-chowk.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandni-chowk|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandni-chowk-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandni-chowk:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square of Moonlight","text":"और उस सारे शोर-शराबे के बीच, अगर तुम्हें कहानी मालूम हो, तो तुम वहीं खड़े होकर जहाँ पानी बहता था, सोच सकते हो: ठीक यहीं, मेरे पैरों के नीचे, कभी एक राजकुमारी ने चाँद को सड़क पर उतारा था।","lang":"hi","body":"And in the middle of all that noise, if you know the story, you can stand where the water ran and think: right here, under my feet, a princess once made the moon walk down a street.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandni-chowk.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandni-chowk|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabootarbaz-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabootarbaz:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sky Over Old Delhi","text":"पुरानी दिल्ली में, ढलती दोपहर के वक़्त, एक लड़का अपने चाचा की छत पर चढ़ा और उसने देखा कि वे मुंडेर पर खड़े, ऊपर आसमान में देखते हुए, लंबी आवाज़ लगा रहे थे — आओ, आओ, आ — किसी ऐसे को पुकारते हुए जो लड़के को दिखाई नहीं दे रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"In the old city of Delhi, late in the afternoon, a boy climbed to his uncle's rooftop and found him standing at the edge, looking up, making a long call — aao, aao, aa — to nobody the boy could see.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabootarbaz.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabootarbaz|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabootarbaz-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabootarbaz:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sky Over Old Delhi","text":"तभी उसने उन्हें देखा। कबूतरों का एक झुंड, बहुत ऊँचाई पर, एक साथ ऐसे मुड़ रहा था जैसे आसमान में किसी ने सलेटी दुपट्टा लहरा दिया हो। उसके चाचाजी ने सीटी बजाई, कपड़ा फहराया, फिर आवाज़ दी — और पूरा झुंड चक्कर काटकर, पंखों की फड़फड़ाहट के साथ, अपनी ही छत पर नीचे उतर आया।","lang":"hi","body":"Then he saw them. A flock of pigeons, high up, turning all together like one grey scarf thrown across the sky. His uncle whistled, flagged a cloth, called again — and the whole flock wheeled and came down, in a rush of wings, onto their own roof.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabootarbaz.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabootarbaz|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabootarbaz-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabootarbaz:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sky Over Old Delhi","text":"\"इसे कबूतरबाज़ी कहते हैं,\" चाचाजी ने कहा। \"कबूतर उड़ाना। मेरे पिताजी भी यही करते थे, और उनके पिताजी भी, और इस छत पर तो बादशाहों के ज़माने से कोई न कोई यह करता आ रहा है। ये परिंदे मेरी आवाज़ पहचानते हैं। यहाँ की हर छत की अपनी एक टोली है, और हर टोली अपनी छत को पहचानती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"This is kabootarbazi,\" said his uncle. \"Pigeon-flying. My father did it, and his father, and on this roof, someone has been doing it since the time of the emperors. The birds know my voice. Every roof around here has its own flock, and every flock knows its own roof.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabootarbaz.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabootarbaz|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabootarbaz-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabootarbaz:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sky Over Old Delhi","text":"बगल वाली छत से एक पड़ोसी ने आवाज़ लगाई: \"आज अपने नए परिंदों का ध्यान रखना!\" — क्योंकि असली खेल यही है। जब दो झुंड एक साथ उड़ते हैं, तो हवा में आपस में मिल जाते हैं। और जब वे नीचे उतरते हैं, तो कुछ कबूतर ग़लत पुकार के पीछे-पीछे किसी और की छत पर पहुँच जाते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"From the next roof, a neighbour called across: \"Careful with your new birds today!\" — because here is the game. When two flocks fly at once, they mix in the air. And when they come down, some birds follow the wrong caller home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabootarbaz.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabootarbaz|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabootarbaz-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabootarbaz:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sky Over Old Delhi","text":"सारा हुनर आवाज़ में होता है। एक अच्छा कबूतरबाज़ मिले-जुले झुंड में से भी अपने कबूतरों को वापस बुला लेता है — और कभी-कभी, अगर उसकी पुकार बहुत पक्की हो, तो पड़ोसी के भी कुछ कबूतर साथ चले आते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The skill is in the voice. A good kabootarbaz can call his own birds back out of a mixed flock — and sometimes, if his call is very good, a few of the neighbour's birds come too.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabootarbaz.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabootarbaz|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabootarbaz-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabootarbaz:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sky Over Old Delhi","text":"लड़के ने इसके पीछे की मेहनत समझी: नाप-तौल कर दाना डालना, पानी बदलना, दड़बों की सफ़ाई, और हर कबूतर को उसके नाम और रंग से पहचानना — चितकबरा वाला, सफ़ेद पूँछ वाला, और वह आलसी कबूतर जो हमेशा सबसे आख़िर में उतरता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The boy learned the work behind it: grain measured out, water changed, the loft cleaned, every bird known by name and colour — the checkered one, the white-tailed one, the lazy one who always lands last.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabootarbaz.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabootarbaz|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kabootarbaz-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kabootarbaz:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sky Over Old Delhi","text":"और उसने उस ख़ास वक़्त को भी पहचाना। दिन की रोशनी की वह आख़िरी घड़ी, जब गलियों से तपिश उतरने लगती है, एक के बाद एक छत से कबूतरों के झुंड आसमान में उठते हैं, और वह पूरा भीड़-भाड़, शोर-शराबे से भरा पुराना शहर बस एक पल के लिए ठहरकर ऊपर आसमान की तरफ़ देखने लगता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And he learned the hour. That last hour of light, when the heat lets go of the lanes, and roof after roof sends its flock up, and the whole crowded, noisy, jam-packed old city stands still for a moment, looking up.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kabootarbaz.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kabootarbaz|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ghalib-mangoes-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ghalib-mangoes:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Poet and the Mangoes","text":"\"क़रीब डेढ़ सौ साल पहले, पुरानी दिल्ली की बल्लीमारान नाम की एक गली में मिर्ज़ा ग़ालिब रहते थे — इतने शानदार शायर कि लोग आज भी उनके शेर ज़बानी याद करते हैं, और हम सबके बाद भी बहुत समय तक याद करते रहेंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A hundred and fifty-odd years ago, in a lane of Old Delhi called Ballimaran, lived Mirza Ghalib — a poet so good that people are still learning his verses by heart today, and will be long after all of us.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ghalib-mangoes.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ghalib-mangoes|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ghalib-mangoes-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ghalib-mangoes:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Poet and the Mangoes","text":"\"ग़ालिब ने मोहब्बत, दुख और दुनिया के अजब-गज़ब रंगों के बारे में लिखा। और उन्होंने आमों के बारे में भी खूब लिखा। उनके असली ख़त आज भी मौजूद हैं, और उनमें गहरी बातों के बीच-बीच, वे दूसरे शहरों के दोस्तों से बस आम भेजने की फ़रमाइश करते रहते हैं — अच्छे आम, और ढेर सारे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Ghalib wrote about love and sorrow and the strangeness of the world. And he wrote, quite a lot, about mangoes. His real letters survive, and in them, between deep thoughts, he is forever asking friends in other cities to send him mangoes — good ones, and plenty.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ghalib-mangoes.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ghalib-mangoes|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ghalib-mangoes-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ghalib-mangoes:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Poet and the Mangoes","text":"\"जब किसी ने उनसे पूछा कि एक उम्दा आम में क्या ख़ूबी होनी चाहिए, तो उनका जो जवाब हम तक पहुँचा है वह ठेठ ग़ालिब वाला है: बस दो ही बातें होनी चाहिए। एक तो मीठा हो। और दूसरा, बहुत सारा हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When someone asked him what makes a mango truly great, the answer that has come down to us is pure Ghalib: only two things are required. It should be sweet. And there should be a lot of it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ghalib-mangoes.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ghalib-mangoes|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ghalib-mangoes-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ghalib-mangoes:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Poet and the Mangoes","text":"\"अब सुनिए वह मशहूर क़िस्सा। ग़ालिब आँगन में अपने एक दोस्त के साथ बैठे थे — ऐसा दोस्त जिसे, अफ़सोस, आम बिल्कुल पसंद नहीं थे और जो पूरा मौसम ग़ालिब से आमों की तारीफ़ें सुन-सुनकर पक चुका था। तभी गली से एक गधा गुज़रा, उसने वहाँ पड़े आम के छिलकों के ढेर को सूँघा, और बिना मुँह लगाए आगे बढ़ गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Now, the famous story. Ghalib was sitting in a courtyard with a friend — a friend who, sadly for him, did not care for mangoes, and had endured a whole season of Ghalib praising them. A donkey wandered down the lane, sniffed at a heap of mango peels lying there, and walked on without touching them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ghalib-mangoes.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ghalib-mangoes|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ghalib-mangoes-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ghalib-mangoes:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Poet and the Mangoes","text":"\"ग़ालिब ने गधे को देखा। फिर अपने दोस्त को देखा। और बिना एक पल गँवाए बोले: \\\"देखा! सिर्फ़ गधे ही आम नहीं खाते।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"Ghalib looked at the donkey. He looked at his friend. And without missing a beat he said: \"Quite so. Only donkeys don't eat mangoes.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ghalib-mangoes.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ghalib-mangoes|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ghalib-mangoes-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ghalib-mangoes:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Poet and the Mangoes","text":"दोस्त ने मुँह खोला, कहने को कुछ न मिला, और फिर बंद कर लिया। सुना है कि उसने उसी दोपहर एक आम खाया, सिर्फ़ खुद को उस गिनती से बाहर करने के लिए।","lang":"hi","body":"The friend opened his mouth, found nothing whatsoever in it, and closed it again. It is reported that he ate a mango that very afternoon, if only to remove himself from the category.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ghalib-mangoes.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ghalib-mangoes|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ghalib-mangoes-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ghalib-mangoes:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Poet and the Mangoes","text":"दिल्ली तब से यह किस्सा सुनाती आ रही है — आमों के मौसम में, कटे हुए फलों की थाली पर, और अक्सर उस मेहमान की चुटकी लेते हुए जिसने अभी-अभी कहा हो, \"जी नहीं, शुक्रिया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Delhi has told this story ever since — at mango time, over cut fruit, usually at the expense of whichever guest has just said no thank you.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ghalib-mangoes.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ghalib-mangoes|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.republic-day-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.republic-day:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Whole Country Comes to One Road","text":"छब्बीस जनवरी को दिल्ली अँधेरे में ही जाग जाती है। कड़ाके की ठंड होती है — बिल्कुल दिल्ली की सर्दियों वाली ठंड, कोहरे से भरी — और सब परिवार शॉल और मंकी कैप लपेटकर एक लंबी, चौड़ी सड़क की ओर चल पड़ते हैं, जिसके छोर पर इंडिया गेट खड़ा है।","lang":"hi","body":"On the twenty-sixth of January, Delhi gets up in the dark. It is cold — proper Delhi-winter cold, the kind with fog in it — and families wrap up in shawls and monkey caps and head for one long, wide road with India Gate standing at the end of it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-republic-day.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.republic-day|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.republic-day-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.republic-day:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Whole Country Comes to One Road","text":"यह तारीख कोई इत्तेफ़ाक नहीं है। सन् 1950 में इसी दिन भारत का संविधान लागू हुआ था — नियमों की वह किताब जो देश ने खुद अपने लिए लिखी थी, जिसकी शुरुआत होती है इन शब्दों से: हम, भारत के लोग। गणतंत्र दिवस उसी किताब का जन्मदिन है।","lang":"hi","body":"The date is not an accident. On this day in 1950, India's Constitution came into force — the book of rules the country wrote for itself, that begins with the words We, the people of India. Republic Day is the birthday of that book.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-republic-day.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.republic-day|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.republic-day-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.republic-day:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Whole Country Comes to One Road","text":"और फिर परेड आती है। सैनिक ऐसे सटीक ताल मिलाकर कदमताल करते हैं कि उनकी आवाज़ एक विशाल कदम जैसी लगती है। बैंड। घोड़े। ऊँट — ऊँटों का दस्ता, ऊँचा और बेपरवाह। और ऊपर, आसमान को चीरते हुए ऐसी बनावट में उड़ते जेट विमान कि पूरी भीड़ एक साथ दंग रह जाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"And then the parade comes. Soldiers marching so exactly together they sound like one enormous footstep. Bands. Horses. Camels — the camel regiment, tall and unbothered. And overhead, jets ripping the sky open in formations that make the whole crowd gasp at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-republic-day.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.republic-day|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.republic-day-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.republic-day:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Whole Country Comes to One Road","text":"\"मगर बाद में किसी बच्चे से पूछिए कि उसे सबसे अच्छा क्या लगा, तो वह आमतौर पर झांकियाँ ही होती हैं। हर राज्य एक झांकी भेजता है: पहियों पर चलता एक मंच, जो अपने एक हिस्से को साथ लिए चलता है। केरल की नावें। राजस्थान का रेगिस्तान। नाचता हुआ पूर्वोत्तर। हर तीस सेकंड में एक अलग ही भारत।\"","lang":"hi","body":"But ask a child afterwards what they loved best and it is usually the jhaankis — the tableaux. Every state sends one: a rolling stage carrying a piece of itself. Kerala's boats. Rajasthan's desert. The Northeast dancing. A different India every thirty seconds.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-republic-day.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.republic-day|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.republic-day-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.republic-day:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Whole Country Comes to One Road","text":"\"अपनी दादी के साथ देख रही एक बच्ची ने पूछा कि यह परेड दिल्ली में ही क्यों होती है। उसकी दादी ने पलटकर उसी से सवाल पूछ लिया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A girl watching with her grandmother asked why Delhi gets the parade. Her grandmother turned the question around.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-republic-day.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.republic-day|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.republic-day-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.republic-day:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Whole Country Comes to One Road","text":"\"परेड में बच्चे भी होते हैं — पुरस्कार जीतने वाले, नाचने वाले, और वे स्कूली बच्चे जिन्होंने कोहरे में महीनों तक अभ्यास किया था। और एक पल ऐसा आता है जब झंडा ऊपर फहराया जाता है और लाखों लोगों की पूरी भीड़ एक साथ खड़ी होकर बिल्कुल शांत हो जाती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"There are children in the parade too — award winners, dancers, schools that practised for months in the fog. And there is one moment when the flag goes up and the whole crowd, lakhs of people, stands and goes quiet together.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-republic-day.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.republic-day|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.republic-day-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.republic-day:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Whole Country Comes to One Road","text":"\"पूरे देश में वही सुबह: हर राज्य के स्कूल के मैदानों में झंडे फहराए जा रहे होते हैं, मिठाइयाँ बाँटी जाती हैं, हज़ारों तरह के लहजों में राष्ट्रगान गाया जाता है। परेड दिल्ली में होती है, मगर यह दिन हर जगह होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"All over the country, the same morning: flags going up in school yards in every state, sweets given out, the anthem sung in a thousand accents. The parade is in Delhi, but the day is everywhere.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-republic-day.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.republic-day|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.hauz-khas-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.hauz-khas:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Mended Things","text":"\"लगभग सात सौ साल पहले, सुल्तान अलाउद्दीन ख़लजी ने दिल्ली में अपने लिए एक नया शहर बनवाया, जिसका नाम था सीरी। शहर को पानी की ज़रूरत होती है, और दिल्ली की गर्मियाँ बड़ी बेरहम होती हैं — इसलिए उसने मानसून का पानी इकट्ठा करने के लिए पास ही एक बहुत बड़ा तालाब खुदवाया: हौज-ए-अलाई, यानी शाही जलाशय।\"","lang":"hi","body":"About seven hundred years ago, Sultan Alauddin Khalji built himself a new city at Delhi, called Siri. A city is thirsty, and Delhi's summers are merciless — so he had a vast tank dug nearby to catch the monsoon: the Hauz-i-Alai, the royal reservoir.","art":"art/story/sm/it-hauz-khas.jpg","route":"#/story/it.hauz-khas|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.hauz-khas-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.hauz-khas:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Mended Things","text":"काम बन गया। बारिश ने उसे लबालब भर दिया, और झुलसती गर्मी के पूरे मौसम में पानी टिका रहा — पीने के लिए, नहाने-धोने के लिए, जानवरों के लिए, हर किसी के लिए। पुरानी दिल्ली में कोई बड़ा तालाब सिर्फ़ सजावट की चीज़ नहीं था। वही तय करता था कि कोई जगह एक शहर बने या फिर वीराना।","lang":"hi","body":"It worked. The rains filled it, and all through the burning months the water lasted — for drinking, for washing, for animals, for everyone. A big tank in old Delhi was not a decoration. It was the difference between a city and an empty place.","art":"art/story/sm/it-hauz-khas.jpg","route":"#/story/it.hauz-khas|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.hauz-khas-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.hauz-khas:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Mended Things","text":"लेकिन बाकी सब चीज़ों की तरह, तालाबों को भी देखरेख की ज़रूरत होती है। राजा बदलते गए, ध्यान हटता गया, और साल-दर-साल गाद भरती गई और नालियाँ बंद होती गईं, यहाँ तक कि उस बड़े तालाब में नाममात्र का पानी भी न बचा। उस ज़माने के इतिहास बताते हैं कि लोगों ने उसके सूखे तलवे में कुएँ तक खोदने शुरू कर दिए थे।","lang":"hi","body":"But tanks, like everything, need looking after. Kings changed, attention wandered, and year by year the silt crept in and the channels choked, until the great tank held hardly any water at all. The chronicles say people had even begun digging wells in its dry bed.","art":"art/story/sm/it-hauz-khas.jpg","route":"#/story/it.hauz-khas|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.hauz-khas-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.hauz-khas:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Mended Things","text":"फिर आए फ़िरोज़ शाह तुग़लक़ — और फ़िरोज़ शाह बड़े अनोखे सुल्तान थे। ज़्यादातर राजा अपने नाम से नई चीज़ें बनवाना चाहते हैं। मगर फ़िरोज़ शाह का एक ऐसा शौक़ था जिसके बारे में उनके दौर के इतिहासकारों ने बड़े अचरज के साथ लिखा है: उन्हें पुरानी चीज़ों की मरम्मत करना पसंद था।","lang":"hi","body":"Then came Firoz Shah Tughlaq — and Firoz Shah was an unusual sort of Sultan. Most kings want to build new things with their own names on them. Firoz Shah had a passion the histories of his own time wrote about with some wonder: he liked repairing old things.","art":"art/story/sm/it-hauz-khas.jpg","route":"#/story/it.hauz-khas|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.hauz-khas-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.hauz-khas:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Mended Things","text":"उन्होंने पूरी दिल्ली में यही किया — पुराने मक़बरे, पुराने तालाब, सदियों पहले गुज़रे राजाओं की पुरानी इमारतें, सब उनके हुक्म से फिर से दुरुस्त की गईं। यहाँ तक कि उन्होंने अपने शासन के ब्योरे में इसे उन कामों में लिखवाया जिन पर उन्हें सबसे ज़्यादा गर्व था। नई जीत नहीं। पुरानी चीज़ों की देखभाल।","lang":"hi","body":"He did the same all over Delhi — old tombs, old tanks, old buildings of kings long gone, patched up at his order. He even had it written down, in his own account of his reign, as one of the things he was proudest of. Not conquest. Maintenance.","art":"art/story/sm/it-hauz-khas.jpg","route":"#/story/it.hauz-khas|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.hauz-khas-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.hauz-khas:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Mended Things","text":"और उस संवारे गए तालाब के किनारे उन्होंने एक मदरसा — यानी एक कॉलेज — बनवाया, जिसमें पत्थर के हवादार कमरे थे जिनका रुख़ पानी की तरफ़ था, ताकि छात्र पानी की आवाज़ सुनते-सुनते अपने सबक याद कर सकें। उस जगह का नाम पड़ा हौज़ ख़ास: यानी शाही तालाब।","lang":"hi","body":"And on the banks of the restored tank he built a madrasa — a college — with airy stone rooms looking out over the water, so that students learned their lessons to the sound of it. The place came to be called Hauz Khas: the royal tank.","art":"art/story/sm/it-hauz-khas.jpg","route":"#/story/it.hauz-khas|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.hauz-khas-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.hauz-khas:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Mended Things","text":"यह सब कुछ आज भी वहीं मौजूद है। मॉनसून में तालाब आज भी भर जाता है। पानी के किनारे मदरसे के वे पत्थर के कमरे आज भी खड़े हैं। अब उसके आस-पास एक हिरन पार्क है, कैफ़े हैं, और आर्ट गैलरी हैं, और विद्यार्थी आज भी आकर ठीक वहीं बैठते हैं जहाँ छह सौ साल पहले विद्यार्थी बैठा करते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"All of it is still there. The tank still fills in the monsoon. The madrasa's stone rooms still stand at the water's edge. Around it now there is a deer park, and cafes, and art galleries, and students still come and sit where students sat six hundred years ago.","art":"art/story/sm/it-hauz-khas.jpg","route":"#/story/it.hauz-khas|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Cities of Dilli"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"जब चंडीगढ़ बन रहा था, तो नेक चंद नाम के एक नौजवान रोड इंस्पेक्टर हर रोज़ साइकिल से निर्माण की जगहों का चक्कर लगाते थे। और जहाँ भी वे जाते, उन्हें दिखता कि बनता हुआ शहर अपने पीछे क्या छोड़ जाता है: टूटी टाइलें, चटके हुए बर्तन, फ़्यूज़ बल्ब, टूटी चूड़ियाँ, अजीबोगरीब पत्थर। कचरा, सब यही मानते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"While Chandigarh was being built, a young roads inspector named Nek Chand cycled around the works every day. And everywhere he went, he saw what a rising city leaves behind: broken tiles, cracked pots, dead bulbs, smashed bangles, odd stones. Rubbish, everyone agreed.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"नेक चंद ऐसा बिल्कुल नहीं मानते थे। उन्होंने चुपचाप चीज़ें इकट्ठा करना शुरू कर दिया। यहाँ से टूटी चूड़ियों की एक बोरी। वहाँ से नदी के पत्थरों का एक ढेर, जिनमें से हर पत्थर किसी न किसी चीज़ जैसा दिखता था — कोई चिड़िया, कोई चेहरा, कोई बैठा हुआ भालू। वे उन्हें साइकिल पर लादकर झील के पास जंगल की एक ऐसी घाटी में ले जाते, जहाँ कभी कोई नहीं जाता था।","lang":"hi","body":"Nek Chand did not quite agree. He began, quietly, to collect. A sack of broken bangles here. A load of river stones there, each one shaped like something — a bird, a face, a sitting bear. He carried them by bicycle into a forest gorge near the lake where nobody ever went.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"बस एक मुश्किल थी, और वह कोई छोटी मुश्किल नहीं थी: वह ज़मीन संरक्षित थी। वहाँ किसी को भी कुछ भी बनाने की इजाज़त नहीं थी। किसी को भी नहीं। और शहर के ही कचरे से, एक सरकारी रोड इंस्पेक्टर के ज़रिये, चुपके-चुपके कुछ बनाने की तो बिल्कुल भी नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"There was one problem, and it was not small: that land was protected. Nothing was allowed to be built there. Not by anyone. Certainly not a secret anything, by a government roads inspector, out of the city's own rubbish.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"फिर भी वे बनाते रहे। शामें, रातें, छुट्टियाँ — बरसों तक, अकेले। उन्होंने थोड़ी सी जगह साफ़ करके एक झोपड़ी बनाई, फिर तरह-तरह की आकृतियाँ: चूड़ियों के टुकड़ों वाले घाघरे पहने नाचती हुई मूर्तियाँ, टूटी क्रॉकरी की खाल वाले जानवर, पत्थर के चेहरों वाले छोटे लोगों की फ़ौजें, आँगन, झरने, और इतने नीचे दरवाज़ों वाली घुमावदार दीवारें कि बड़ों को भी झुककर अंदर जाना पड़े।","lang":"hi","body":"He built anyway. Evenings, nights, holidays — alone, for years. He cleared a little space and made a hut, then figures: dancers with bangle-shard skirts, animals with crockery skins, armies of little people with stone faces, courtyards, waterfalls, winding walls with low doorways that make even grown-ups bow to enter.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"लगभग बीस सालों तक, किसी को भी पता नहीं चला। पेड़ों के बीच उनका यह साम्राज्य फलता-फूलता रहा — पहले सैकड़ों आकृतियाँ, फिर हज़ारों — जबकि पहाड़ी की दूसरी तरफ़ बसे शहर को भनक तक नहीं थी कि उसका कोई जुड़वाँ भी है।","lang":"hi","body":"For close to twenty years, almost nobody knew. His kingdom grew in the trees — hundreds of figures, then thousands — while the city on the other side of the ridge had no idea it had a twin.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"फिर, 1970 के दशक में, जंगल साफ़ करने वाली सरकारी कर्मचारियों की एक टोली झाड़ियों को हटाती हुई आगे बढ़ी और एकदम सन्न रह गई। पेड़ों के बीच पत्थर के लोग कतारों में खड़े उन्हें ताक रहे थे। एकड़ों में फैले हुए। किसी ने यहाँ अंदर एक पूरी दुनिया बसा दी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"Then, in the 1970s, a government clearing party working in the forest pushed through the undergrowth and stopped dead. Stone people stood in ranks between the trees, watching them. Acres of them. Somebody had built a world in here.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"अफ़सरों के सामने एक असली मुश्किल आ खड़ी हुई। नियम साफ़ थे: यह सब ग़ैरक़ानूनी था, इसकी एक-एक दीवार, और क़ानून कहता था कि इसे तोड़ दिया जाए। लेकिन फ़ैसला लेने से पहले अफ़सर इसे देखने आए — और फिर और भी अफ़सर आए, और फिर उनके परिवार भी।","lang":"hi","body":"The officials had a genuine problem. The rules were clear: it was all illegal, every wall of it, and the law said demolish. But officials came to see it before deciding — and then more officials, and then their families.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"रॉक गार्डन सबके लिए खोल दिया गया। नेक चंद, जिन्होंने बीस साल तक अपने काम को छिपाकर रखा था, अपनी बाक़ी की लंबी ज़िंदगी खुलेआम इसे ही बनाते हुए बिताई — झरने, झूलों वाला एक बड़ा दालान, मूर्तियों से भरे पूरे-पूरे आँगन — जिन्हें देखने दुनिया भर से हज़ारों-हज़ार लोग आए।","lang":"hi","body":"The Rock Garden opened to everyone. Nek Chand, the man who had hidden his work for twenty years, spent the rest of his long life building it in the open — waterfalls, a hall of swings, whole courtyards of figures — visited by thousands upon thousands of people from all over the world.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.nek-chand-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.nek-chand:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Secret Kingdom of Broken Things","text":"और सबसे प्यारी बात यह है: यह सब अब भी टूटी-फूटी चीज़ों से ही बना है। किसी भी नर्तकी को ध्यान से देखो, तो तुम्हें किसी के टूटे हुए चाय के कप, किसी के जले हुए सॉकेट, किसी के बाथरूम की चटकी हुई टाइलें नज़र आएँगी — हर वह चीज़ जिसे शहर ने बेकार मान लिया था, आज एक-दूसरे का हाथ थामे नाच रही है।","lang":"hi","body":"And here is the loveliest part: it is all still broken things. Look closely at any dancer and you are looking at somebody's smashed teacups, somebody's burnt-out sockets, somebody's cracked bathroom tiles — everything a city decided was worthless, holding hands and dancing.","art":"art/story/sm/it-nek-chand.jpg","route":"#/story/it.nek-chand|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.open-hand-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.open-hand:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hand That Turns With the Wind","text":"चंडीगढ़ के सबसे ऊपरी हिस्से में, जहाँ पीछे पहाड़ियों के सामने कंक्रीट के एक बड़े से मैदान में सरकारी इमारतें खड़ी हैं, स्कूल की सैर पर आई एक लड़की ने आसमान में कुछ अनोखा देखा: एक ऊँचे खंभे पर धातु का बना एक विशालकाय हाथ, जो इस तरह खुला था जैसे कोई हाथ हिलाकर नमस्ते कह रहा हो।","lang":"hi","body":"At the top of Chandigarh, where the government buildings stand in a great concrete plaza with the hills behind them, a girl on a school trip saw something strange against the sky: an enormous metal hand, high on a mast, open like a wave hello.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-open-hand.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.open-hand|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.open-hand-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.open-hand:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hand That Turns With the Wind","text":"\"वह 'ओपन हैंड' है,\" टीचर ने कहा। \"हमारे शहर का प्रतीक। यह पाँच मंज़िला इमारत से भी ऊँचा है, इसका वज़न दर्जन भर हाथियों जितना है — और ज़रा एक मिनट इसे ध्यान से देखो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"That is the Open Hand,\" said the teacher. \"The symbol of our city. It is taller than a five-storey building, it weighs as much as a dozen elephants — and watch it for a minute.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-open-hand.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.open-hand|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.open-hand-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.open-hand:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hand That Turns With the Wind","text":"उसने देखा। शिवालिक की पहाड़ियों से हवा बहकर आई, और वह पूरा विशाल हाथ अपनी धुरी पर हौले से घूमकर एक नई दिशा की ओर मुड़ गया, जैसे किसी पुरानी लोककथा जितना बड़ा कोई वेदरवेन हो। कुछ बच्चों को लगा कि अब यह एक खुली हथेली जैसा दिख रहा है। दूसरों ने कहा, उड़ती हुई कोई चिड़िया।","lang":"hi","body":"She watched. The wind came down off the Shivaliks, and the whole gigantic hand swung gently on its bearings and faced a new direction, like a weathervane the size of a myth. Some children thought it now looked like an open palm. Others said a bird in flight.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-open-hand.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.open-hand|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.open-hand-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.open-hand:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hand That Turns With the Wind","text":"\"हमारे शहर का नक्शा बनाने वाले वास्तुकार ने इसे यहाँ लगाया था,\" टीचर ने बताया, \"और उन्होंने इसे एक विचार दिया: देने के लिए भी खुला, और लेने के लिए भी खुला। वे चाहते थे कि यह शहर ख़ुद यह वादा करे। जो हाथ मुट्ठी बन जाए, वह इन दोनों में से कुछ नहीं कर सकता।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"The architect who drew our city put it here,\" said the teacher, \"and he gave it a motto: open to give, and open to receive. He wanted the city itself to make that promise. A hand that is a fist can do neither.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-open-hand.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.open-hand|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.open-hand-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.open-hand:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hand That Turns With the Wind","text":"लौटती हुई बस में, वह लड़की इसी बारे में सोचती रही — एक ऐसा स्मारक जो घोड़े पर सवार कोई राजा नहीं है, न तलवार थामे कोई सेनापति। बस एक हाथ, जो खुला है और घूम रहा है।","lang":"hi","body":"On the bus back, the girl kept thinking about it — a monument that is not a king on a horse, not a general with a sword. Just a hand, open, turning.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-open-hand.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.open-hand|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.open-hand-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.open-hand:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hand That Turns With the Wind","text":"उस शाम उसके दादाजी को यह सवाल बहुत पसंद आया। \"देने के लिए भी खुला और पाने के लिए भी खुला,\" उन्होंने दोहराया। \"यह बात किसी शहर पर भी लागू होती है और किसी इंसान पर भी। पूरे एक दिन इनमें से कोई एक बनकर तो देखो। तुम देखोगे कि पाना उतना आसान नहीं होता जितना देना।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Her grandfather liked the question that evening. \"Open to give and open to receive,\" he repeated. \"It works for a city and it works for a person. Try being one or the other for a whole day. The giving is easier than the receiving, you will find.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-open-hand.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.open-hand|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.open-hand-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.open-hand:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hand That Turns With the Wind","text":"वह हाथ आज भी वहीं ऊपर घूम रहा है। दशकों से वह पहाड़ियों से आने वाली हर हवा का सामना करता आ रहा है — न कभी किसी की तरफ इशारा करता है, न कभी मुट्ठी बांधता है, और न ही कभी पूरी तरह थमता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The hand is still up there, turning. It has faced every wind that has come off the hills for decades — never pointing at anyone, never closing, never quite still.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-open-hand.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.open-hand|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sukhna-birds-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sukhna-birds:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Invites Winter Guests","text":"जब चंडीगढ़ नया-नया था, तो इसे बनाने वालों ने शिवालिक की पहाड़ियों से लुढ़कते-बहते 'सुखना चो' नाम के एक बरसाती नाले को देखा और उसके आगे मिट्टी का एक बांध बना दिया। उस नाले का पानी रुका, चारों तरफ फैला और एक झील बन गया — सुखना झील, जिसे इंसानों ने अपने हाथों से, बड़े जतन से बनाया था।","lang":"hi","body":"When Chandigarh was young, its makers looked at a seasonal stream called the Sukhna Choe, tumbling down from the Shivalik hills, and built an earthen dam across it. The stream pooled and spread and became a lake — Sukhna Lake, made by hands, on purpose.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sukhna-birds.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sukhna-birds|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sukhna-birds-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sukhna-birds:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Invites Winter Guests","text":"फिर एक ऐसा नियम बना जिसने आगे की हर बात तय कर दी: कोई भी शोर मचाने वाली मोटरबोट नहीं चलेगी। झील को शांत ही रहना था — टहलने वालों के लिए, चप्पू से नाव चलाने वालों के लिए, सुबह-सवेरे योग करने वालों के लिए, और उन मेहमानों के लिए भी जिनके बारे में शहर की योजना बनाने वालों ने शायद सोचा भी नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"A rule was set that shaped everything after: no roaring motorboats. The lake was to stay quiet — for walkers, for rowers, for people doing yoga at dawn, and for guests the planners had perhaps not even thought about.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sukhna-birds.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sukhna-birds|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sukhna-birds-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sukhna-birds:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Invites Winter Guests","text":"क्योंकि यह खबर चारों तरफ फैल गई। इंसानों में नहीं — परिंदों में। हर सर्दी में, हैरान कर देने वाली दूरियों से पक्षी यहां आने लगे: बत्तखें और पानी में चलने वाले पक्षी जो सुदूर उत्तर में, साइबेरिया और मध्य एशिया में अंडे देते हैं, और ठंड आते ही हज़ारों किलोमीटर उड़कर दक्षिण की ओर चले आते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Because word got around. Not among people — among birds. Every winter, birds began arriving from astonishingly far away: ducks and waders that breed in the far north, in Siberia and Central Asia, and fly south for thousands of kilometres when the cold comes.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sukhna-birds.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sukhna-birds|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sukhna-birds-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sukhna-birds:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Invites Winter Guests","text":"पहाड़ों को पार करके आए किसी थके हुए पक्षी के लिए सवाल यह नहीं होता कि झील किसने बनाई या कब बनाई। सवाल तो यह होता है: क्या पानी है, क्या खाना है, क्या यहाँ सुकून है? सुखना कहती है—हाँ, हाँ, हाँ। इसलिए वे नीचे उतरते हैं, छप-छप करते हैं, और पूरे मौसम यहीं ठहरते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"To a tired bird that has crossed mountains, the question is not who made a lake or when. The question is: is there water, is there food, is it calm? Sukhna answers yes, yes, yes. So they come down, splash, and stay for the season.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sukhna-birds.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sukhna-birds|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sukhna-birds-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sukhna-birds:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Invites Winter Guests","text":"अपनी दादी के साथ झील के रास्ते पर टहलते हुए एक लड़के ने बत्तखों की एक कतार को कागज़ के तीरों की तरह उतरते देखा। \"लेकिन झील तो इंसानों ने बनाई है,\" उसने कहा। \"पक्षियों को कैसे पता चलता है कि यह भी काम की है?\"","lang":"hi","body":"A boy walking the lake path with his grandmother watched a line of ducks land like paper darts. \"But the lake is man-made,\" he said. \"How do the birds know it counts?\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sukhna-birds.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sukhna-birds|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sukhna-birds-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sukhna-birds:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Invites Winter Guests","text":"झील के अपने इंसानी मौसम भी होते हैं। सुबह ठीक छह बजे एक-दूसरे का अभिवादन करते सैर करने वाले लोग। चमकती कतारों में अभ्यास करते नाविक—इस झील में नौकायन की बड़ी-बड़ी प्रतियोगिताएँ हुई हैं। शाम को किनारे पर टहलते और आइसक्रीम खाते लोगों की भीड़, जबकि पहाड़ियाँ बैंगनी रंग में ढलने लगती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The lake has its human seasons too. Morning walkers who greet each other at six sharp. Rowers training in flashing lines — the lake has hosted big rowing competitions. Evening crowds eating ice cream on the promenade while the hills go purple.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sukhna-birds.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sukhna-birds|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sukhna-birds-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sukhna-birds:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Invites Winter Guests","text":"और इस सब के बीच, सर्दियों के ये मेहमान बिना किसी बात पर ध्यान दिए पानी में तैरते और डुबकी लगाते रहते हैं, जब तक कि वसंत के किसी दिन मौसम बदल नहीं जाता। फिर वे सब एक साथ ऊपर उठते हैं और उत्तर की ओर, वापस पहाड़ों के पार उड़ चलते हैं, मानो किसी ने ऐसी घंटी बजा दी हो जो सिर्फ़ उन्हें ही सुनाई देती है।","lang":"hi","body":"And in the middle of it all, the winter guests bob and dive and pay no attention, until one day in spring the weather turns, and they rise together and head north, back over the mountains, as if someone had rung a bell only they can hear.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sukhna-birds.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sukhna-birds|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rose-garden-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rose-garden:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · A City With Gardens for Rooms","text":"जब योजनाकारों ने चंडीगढ़ का नक़्शा बनाया, तो उन्होंने इसके ठीक बीचों-बीच, एक सेक्टर से दूसरे सेक्टर तक फैली हरियाली की एक पट्टी खींची, और उसके पास एक नियम लिख दिया: यह हमेशा बाग़ ही रहेगा। हमेशा। चाहे कुछ भी हो जाए।","lang":"hi","body":"When the planners drew Chandigarh, they drew a ribbon of green running right through the middle of it, sector after sector, and wrote a rule beside it: this stays garden. Forever. No matter what.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rose-garden.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rose-garden|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rose-garden-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rose-garden:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · A City With Gardens for Rooms","text":"लोग उसे लेज़र वैली कहते थे, और इसके किनारे-किनारे और चारों तरफ एक के बाद एक कई बगीचे बनते चले गए, हर एक का अपना ही अलग मिज़ाज था — यहाँ तक कि पूरे शहर में बगीचे ऐसे हो गए जैसे किसी घर में कमरे होते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"They called it the Leisure Valley, and along it and around it grew garden after garden, each with its own character — until the city ended up with gardens the way a house has rooms.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rose-garden.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rose-garden|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rose-garden-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rose-garden:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · A City With Gardens for Rooms","text":"सबसे शानदार कमरा है 'रोज़ गार्डन' — एशिया के सबसे बड़े गुलाब के बगीचों में से एक — जहाँ दूर-दूर तक फैली क्यारियों में सैकड़ों किस्मों के गुलाब खिलते हैं: ऐसे लाल गुलाब जो भीतर से चमकते हुए लगते हैं, सफेद, लगभग काले दिखने वाले, मशहूर हस्तियों के नाम पर रखे गए गुलाब, और ऐसे गुलाब जिनकी खुशबू किसी मिठाई की दुकान जैसी लगती है।","lang":"hi","body":"The grandest room is the Rose Garden — one of the largest in Asia — where hundreds and hundreds of kinds of roses grow in great sweeping beds: reds that look lit from inside, whites, near-blacks, roses named after famous people, roses that smell like the inside of a sweet shop.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rose-garden.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rose-garden|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rose-garden-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rose-garden:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · A City With Gardens for Rooms","text":"वहाँ के एक माली — जो दशकों से इन क्यारियों की देखभाल कर रहे थे — स्कूल के बच्चों से कहना पसंद करते थे: \"लोगों को लगता है कि बगीचा सिर्फ फूलों से बनता है। बगीचा तो मेहनत से बनता है। सही हफ्ते में छँटाई करना। सही वक्त पर पानी देना। फूल तो बस बगीचे का 'धन्यवाद' कहने का तरीका हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A gardener there — a maali who had tended the beds for decades — liked to tell schoolchildren: \"People think the garden is the flowers. The garden is the work. Pruning in the right week. Water at the right hour. The flowers are just the garden saying thank you.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rose-garden.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rose-garden|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rose-garden-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rose-garden:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · A City With Gardens for Rooms","text":"हर साल, सर्दियों के आखिर में, शहर में 'रोज़ फेस्टिवल' मनाया जाता है — लाखों खिले फूलों के बीच लोगों की भीड़, तरह-तरह के मुकाबले और बच्चों की चहल-पहल के दिन। इतने सारे फूल देखकर हैरान एक बच्ची ने बूढ़े माली से पूछा कि सबसे अच्छा गुलाब कौन-सा है।","lang":"hi","body":"Every year, at the end of winter, the city throws its Rose Festival — days of crowds, competitions and children among a million blooms. One girl, overwhelmed, asked the old maali which rose was the best one.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rose-garden.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rose-garden|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rose-garden-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rose-garden:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · A City With Gardens for Rooms","text":"यहाँ कुछ और भी अनोखे कमरे हैं। सिर्फ कैक्टस का एक बगीचा। बोगनवेलिया का एक बगीचा, जो हर बसंत में बैंगनी लपटों की तरह दमक उठता है। जड़ी-बूटियों का एक बगीचा। और एक सीढ़ीदार बगीचा, जो शाम की रोशनी को किसी प्याले की तरह सहेज लेता है।","lang":"hi","body":"There are stranger rooms too. A garden only of cactuses. A bougainvillea garden that goes up in purple flames every spring. A garden of medicinal herbs. A terraced garden that holds evening light like a bowl.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rose-garden.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rose-garden|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rose-garden-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rose-garden:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · A City With Gardens for Rooms","text":"और इन सबके पीछे एक ऐसी फ़ौज है जिसके लिए कोई तालियाँ नहीं बजाता: शहर के माली, जो पानी के पाइप और कैंची लेकर सुबह तड़के ही निकल पड़ते हैं, और कागज़ पर किए गए उस वादे को निभा रहे हैं जो उनमें से ज़्यादातर के पैदा होने से भी पहले किया गया था।","lang":"hi","body":"And behind all of them, an army nobody claps for: the city's gardeners, out at dawn with hoses and secateurs, keeping a promise made on paper before most of them were born.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rose-garden.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rose-garden|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.village-before-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.village-before:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Villages Under the Sectors","text":"चंडीगढ़ के एक लड़के ने एक बार अपनी परदादी से वही सवाल पूछा जो किसी नए शहर का हर बच्चा कभी न कभी पूछता ही है: \"यहाँ पहले क्या था?\" उन्होंने एक पल के लिए उसे देखा, फिर फ़्लैट के फ़र्श की तरफ़ इशारा किया। \"इसके नीचे? गेहूँ,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"जहाँ तुम्हारा बिस्तर है, वहाँ मैंने गेहूँ काटा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A boy in Chandigarh once asked his great-grandmother the question every child of a new city asks eventually: \"What was here before?\" She looked at him for a moment, then pointed at the floor of the flat. \"Under this? Wheat,\" she said. \"I have cut wheat where your bed is.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-village-before.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.village-before|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.village-before-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.village-before:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Villages Under the Sectors","text":"\"शहर बनने से पहले, यह पहाड़ियों के नीचे की खेती की ज़मीन थी — पुराने नामों वाले दूर-दूर बसे कुछ गाँव, आम के बाग़, कुएँ, मवेशी, और सर्दियों में सुनहरी होती सरसों के खेत। लोग यहाँ कई-कई पीढ़ियों से रहते और खेती करते आए थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Before the city, this was farmland below the hills — a scatter of villages with old names, mango groves, wells, cattle, mustard going gold in winter. People had lived and farmed here for generations upon generations.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-village-before.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.village-before|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.village-before-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.village-before:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Villages Under the Sectors","text":"\"और फिर शहर आया, और सच तो यह कहना ही पड़ेगा: गाँव वालों के लिए यह बिल्कुल भी आसान नहीं था। नई राजधानी के लिए जो ज़मीन चुनी गई, वह उन्हीं की ज़मीन थी। वे खेत, जिन्होंने सदियों से परिवारों का पेट भरा था, नापे गए, ले लिए गए और उन पर इमारतें बना दी गईं। कई गाँव दूसरी जगह हटा दिए गए। लोगों को पैसे तो मिले, लेकिन खेत सिर्फ़ पैसा नहीं होता, और यह बात हर कोई जानता था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And then the city came, and it must be said honestly: for the villagers, it did not come gently. The land for the new capital was their land. Fields that had fed families for centuries were measured, acquired and built over. Many villages were moved. People were paid, but a field is not only money, and everyone knew it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-village-before.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.village-before|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.village-before-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.village-before:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Villages Under the Sectors","text":"“एक ही हफ़्ते में हमें गर्व भी हुआ और दुख भी,” परदादी ने कहा। “उन्होंने हमें भविष्य के चित्र दिखाए। जो आप खो रहे हैं, उसकी तस्वीर कोई नहीं बनाता।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"We were proud and we were sad in the same week,\" the great-grandmother said. \"They showed us drawings of the future. Nobody draws you a picture of what you are losing.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-village-before.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.village-before|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.village-before-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.village-before:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Villages Under the Sectors","text":"\"लेकिन सब कुछ ख़त्म नहीं हुआ। कुछ गाँव तो कभी तोड़े ही नहीं गए—बस उनके चारों तरफ़ सेक्टर बना दिए गए। आज भी अगर आप चंडीगढ़ के किसी बाज़ार की सही गली से होकर निकलें, तो सड़कों का यह ग्रिड अचानक रुक जाता है: गलियाँ सँकरी और घुमावदार हो जाती हैं, घर एक-दूसरे से सट जाते हैं, और आप एक ऐसे गाँव में पहुँच जाते हैं जो अपने चारों ओर बसे इस शहर से भी पुराना है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"But not everything vanished. Some villages were never demolished at all — the sectors were simply drawn around them. Walk through the right gap in a Chandigarh market today and the grid suddenly stops: lanes narrow and bend, houses lean together, and you are in a village older than the city wrapped around it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-village-before.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.village-before|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.village-before-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.village-before:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Villages Under the Sectors","text":"\"पुराने नाम भी बचे हुए हैं, बस स्टॉप और बाज़ार के बोर्डों पर, चुपचाप नंबरों से आगे टिके हुए। और यहाँ-वहाँ किसी कार पार्किंग में बरगद या आम का कोई पुराना पेड़ बाकी सब चीज़ों से ज़रा हटकर एक अजीब से कोण पर खड़ा है — क्योंकि वह वहाँ पहले आया था, और शहर का बड़प्पन देखिए कि वह उसके किनारे से होकर गुज़र गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The old names survive too, on bus stops and market boards, quietly outlasting the numbers. And here and there an ancient banyan or mango tree stands in a car park at a strange angle to everything — because it was there first, and the city, to its credit, went around it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-village-before.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.village-before|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.village-before-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.village-before:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Villages Under the Sectors","text":"\"लड़के ने ध्यान दिया कि परदादी को दया नहीं चाहिए थी। वह बस चाहती थीं कि उसे पता रहे। \"शहर तो अच्छा शहर है,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"लेकिन जब तुम सेक्टर 22 में चलो, तो किसी मेहमान की तरह चलना। उसके नीचे किसी के खेत दबे हैं।\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"The great-grandmother did not want pity, the boy noticed. She wanted him to know. \"The city is a good city,\" she said. \"But when you walk in Sector 22, walk like a guest. Somebody's fields are under there.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-village-before.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.village-before|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandi-name-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandi-name:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess the City Is Named For","text":"\"हर नाम एक छोटी सी कहानी होती है, जो तह करके रखी गई हो। चंडीगढ़ को ही लीजिए और उसकी तहें खोलिए: चंडी-गढ़। यानी चंडी का किला। कंक्रीट और गोल चक्करों का एक बिल्कुल नया शहर, जो एक देवी का नाम लिए हुए है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every name is a little story folded up small. Take Chandigarh and unfold it: Chandi-garh. The fort of Chandi. A brand-new city of concrete and roundabouts, carrying the name of a goddess.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandi-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandi-name|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandi-name-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandi-name:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess the City Is Named For","text":"\"चंडी, देवी का एक उग्र और रक्षा करने वाला रूप हैं — वही महान देवी जिन्हें कई लोग दुर्गा के नाम से भी जानते हैं। इस इलाके की पहाड़ियों और मैदानों में सदियों से उन्हें पूजा और याद किया जाता रहा है: वही देवी, जिनके पास आप तब जाते हैं जब किसी मुश्किल का सामना करना हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Chandi is a fierce and protective form of the Devi — the great Goddess whom many also know as Durga. In the hills and plains of this region she has been loved and called on for centuries: the one you go to when something must be faced.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandi-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandi-name|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandi-name-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandi-name:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess the City Is Named For","text":"\"शहर से थोड़ी ही दूर, जहाँ मैदान शिवालिक की पहाड़ियों से मिलते हैं, उनका पुराना मंदिर है — चंडी मंदिर। यह मंदिर तब से वहाँ था, जब किसी ने सेक्टरों का सपना भी नहीं देखा था। तीर्थयात्री पैदल चलकर यहाँ आते थे, जब यह सब कुछ सिर्फ़ खेत हुआ करता था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A little way from the city, where the plains meet the Shivalik hills, stands her old temple — the Chandi Mandir. It was there long before anyone dreamed of sectors. Pilgrims walked to it when all this was fields.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandi-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandi-name|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandi-name-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandi-name:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess the City Is Named For","text":"जब पास ही नई राजधानी बनने लगी, तो उसे एक नाम की ज़रूरत थी। और कोई नया-चमकीला नाम गढ़ने के बजाय, शहर ने वही नाम अपना लिया जो उस ज़मीन का पहले से था — यह इलाका बहुत पहले से देवी के मंदिर के नाम से जाना जाता था।","lang":"hi","body":"When the new capital rose nearby, it needed a name. And rather than inventing something shiny, the city took the name the land already had — the area had long been known by the goddess's temple.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandi-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandi-name|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandi-name-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandi-name:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess the City Is Named For","text":"तो इस तरह भविष्य का यह शहर, नाम के हिसाब से, देवी का किला ही है। इस इलाके के कई परिवारों में, खासकर नवरात्रि पर चंडी की पूजा होती है, जब नौ रातों तक उनकी शक्ति का उत्सव मनाया जाता है — हालांकि हर परिवार का अपना अलग तरीका होता है। अपने परिवार से पूछो कि उनके यहाँ क्या रिवाज़ है।","lang":"hi","body":"So the city of the future is, by name, the goddess's fort. In many families of the region, Chandi is honoured especially at Navratri, when her strength is celebrated for nine nights — though every family keeps its own way. Ask your family what they keep.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandi-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandi-name|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandi-name-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandi-name:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess the City Is Named For","text":"लोग कहते हैं, इसमें कुछ बहुत सटीक बात है। एक मुश्किल दौर के बाद हिम्मत से बसाया गया शहर, जिसका नाम उस देवी पर रखा गया जिन्हें किसी चुनौती का सामना करते वक्त याद किया जाता है। शहर की योजना बनाने वालों ने यह सोचा था या नहीं, पर नाम ने यह बात पूरी कर दी।","lang":"hi","body":"There is something fitting in it, people say. A city built from courage after a hard year, named for the goddess you call on when something must be faced. Whether the planners thought of that or not, the name did.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandi-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandi-name|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chandi-name-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chandi-name:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess the City Is Named For","text":"वह मंदिर आज भी वहीं है, और श्रद्धालु आज भी वहाँ जाते हैं — अब तो शहर की बसें भी लगभग पूरे रास्ते तक जाती हैं। सबसे नया शहर और प्राचीन देवी, दोनों आपस में बड़े अच्छे पड़ोसी बन गए हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The temple still stands, and pilgrims still go — now with the city's buses running most of the way. The newest city and the old goddess have settled into being neighbours.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chandi-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chandi-name|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-streets-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-streets:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City That Planted Its Own Calendar","text":"जब चंडीगढ़ की योजना बनी, तो पेड़ों की भी पूरी योजना बनाई गई — और यूँ ही नहीं। योजनाकारों ने हर सड़क के लिए सोच-समझकर पेड़ों की किस्में चुनीं, जैसे कोई चित्रकार अपनी रंग-पेटी से रंग चुनता है, और हर सड़क पर एक ही किस्म के हज़ारों पेड़ लगाए, इससे पहले कि कई घरों पर छतें भी पड़ पातीं।","lang":"hi","body":"When Chandigarh was planned, the trees were planned too — and not casually. The planners chose species avenue by avenue, like an artist choosing colours from a paintbox, and planted each road with its own kind of tree, thousands of them, before many of the houses even had roofs.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-streets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-streets|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-streets-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-streets:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City That Planted Its Own Calendar","text":"बरसों तक वह नया शहर किसी नर्सरी में खड़े शहर जैसा लगता था — हर सड़क पर खूँटियों से बँधे पतले-दुबले पौधे, जिनकी छाया इतनी कम थी कि रूमाल में समेट लो। लोग उन्हें पानी देते और इंतज़ार करते।","lang":"hi","body":"For years the young city looked like a city standing in a nursery — thin saplings tied to stakes down every avenue, casting shade you could fold into a handkerchief. People watered them and waited.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-streets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-streets|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-streets-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-streets:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City That Planted Its Own Calendar","text":"फिर पेड़ बड़े हुए, और पूरी योजना सामने आ गई। मई में अमलतास वाली सड़कें झूलते हुए सोने जैसी बन जाती हैं, मानो पूरी सड़क से पीला रंग टपक रहा हो। गर्मियों में गुलमोहर सुर्ख लाल हो जाते हैं। बसंत में सेमल पक्षियों के लिए बड़े-बड़े लाल प्याले थाम लेता है, और जकारंदा पर बैंगनी धुंध छा जाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Then the trees grew up, and the plan revealed itself. In May, the amaltas avenues turn to hanging gold, whole streets dripping yellow. In summer the gulmohars go scarlet. In spring the semal holds out big red cups for the birds, and the jacarandas haze over in purple.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-streets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-streets|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-streets-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-streets:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City That Planted Its Own Calendar","text":"क्योंकि हर सड़क पर एक खास किस्म का पेड़ है, इसलिए हर सड़क की अपनी बहार का एक महीना होता है — इस तरह पूरा शहर साल भर, एक-एक इलाक़ा करके, धीरे-धीरे अपने रंग बदलता रहता है। पक्षी और बंदर यह टाइम-टेबल किसी से भी बेहतर जानते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Because each avenue has its own species, each avenue has its own month of glory — so the city changes colour in slow waves, one neighbourhood at a time, all year round. The birds and the monkeys know the timetable better than anyone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-streets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-streets|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-streets-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-streets:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City That Planted Its Own Calendar","text":"सोने की छत जैसी सड़क के नीचे साइकिल से स्कूल जाती एक बच्ची ने अपने पिताजी से पूछा कि किसी ने ऐसी योजना क्यों बनाई होगी, जब पहली अच्छी बहार आने से पहले ही योजना बनाने वाले खुद बूढ़े हो चुके होंगे।","lang":"hi","body":"A girl cycling to school under a gold-roofed avenue asked her father why anyone would plan a thing like that, when the planners themselves would be old before the first good bloom.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-streets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-streets|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-streets-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-streets:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City That Planted Its Own Calendar","text":"यह शहर अपने पेड़ों की हिफ़ाज़त वैसे ही करता है जैसे दूसरे शहर अपनी ऐतिहासिक इमारतों की करते हैं। किसी एक को भी काटना बहुत गंभीर बात है; किसी भले पुराने पेड़ के लिए सड़कों तक को मुड़ते देखा गया है। चंडीगढ़ खुद को 'द सिटी ब्यूटीफुल' कहता है, और सब जानते हैं कि इसकी आधी वजह ये पेड़ ही हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The city guards its trees the way other cities guard monuments. Cutting one is a serious matter; roads have been known to bend around a good old tree. Chandigarh calls itself the City Beautiful, and everyone knows the trees are half the reason.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-streets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-streets|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-streets-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-streets:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The City That Planted Its Own Calendar","text":"और यह योजना बिना किसी के कहे यूँ ही चलती रहती है। तोते अपना पूरा साल सेमल के हिसाब से तय करते हैं। स्कूल के बच्चे जान जाते हैं कि उनकी अपनी सड़क किस महीने सुनहरी होगी। हर मानसून में अब भी नए पौधे लगाए जाते हैं, खूँटियों से बँधे, रूमाल जितनी छाया देते हुए — अगले पचास साल, जो आज ही रोप दिए गए हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And the plan keeps working without being asked. Parakeets budget their year around the semal. Schoolchildren learn which month their own street turns gold. New saplings still go in every monsoon, tied to their stakes, casting handkerchief shade — the next fifty years, already planted.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-streets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-streets|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The City Beautiful"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kullu-dussehra-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kullu-dussehra:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where the Gods Travel","text":"हिमाचल की कुल्लू घाटी में, लगभग हर गाँव के अपने एक देवता होते हैं — अपने ईष्टदेव, जो गाँव के मंदिर में रहते हैं, गाँव का हर हाल-चाल जानते हैं, और किसी समझदार बुज़ुर्ग की तरह उनसे सलाह ली जाती है। यह कोई बहुत पुरानी कहानी नहीं है। आज भी यह घाटी ऐसे ही चलती है।","lang":"hi","body":"In the Kullu valley of Himachal, nearly every village has its own devta — its own deity, who lives in the village temple, knows the village's business, and is consulted like a wise elder. This is not a story from long ago. It is how the valley works today.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kullu-dussehra.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kullu-dussehra|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kullu-dussehra-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kullu-dussehra:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where the Gods Travel","text":"और साल में एक बार, जब दशहरा आता है, तो कुछ ऐसा होता है जो इतने बड़े पैमाने पर दुनिया में कहीं और नहीं होता: देवता यात्रा पर निकलते हैं। हर देवता अपने गाँव से एक पालकी — यानी रथ — में सवार होकर निकलते हैं, जो चाँदी के मुखौटों और गेंदे के फूलों से चमक रहा होता है, और जिसे गाँव वाले अपने कंधों पर उठाकर चलते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And once a year, when Dussehra comes, something happens that happens nowhere else on this scale: the devtas travel. Each one sets out from its village in a palanquin — a rath — gleaming with silver masks and marigolds, carried on the shoulders of its own villagers.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kullu-dussehra.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kullu-dussehra|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kullu-dussehra-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kullu-dussehra:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where the Gods Travel","text":"पहाड़ी रास्तों से उतरते हुए वे आते हैं, दर्जनों के दर्जनों, जिनमें से कुछ तो कई दिनों तक पैदल चलते हैं — आगे-आगे बजते ढोल, गूँजते हुए नरसिंगे, झूलती हुई पालकी — और खेतों में काम करने वाले लोग हाथ रोककर अपने पड़ोसियों के देवताओं को गुज़रते हुए देखने लगते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Down the mountain paths they come, dozens upon dozens of them, some walking for days — drums in front, horns crying out, the palanquin swaying — while the fields stop work to watch their neighbours' gods go by.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kullu-dussehra.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kullu-dussehra|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kullu-dussehra-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kullu-dussehra:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where the Gods Travel","text":"वे सब एक ही जगह जा रहे होते हैं: कुल्लू का बड़ा मैदान, रघुनाथ-जी के दर्शन करने — भगवान राम, जिन्हें यह घाटी इसी नाम से जानती है — जिनका अपना रथ लंबी रस्सियों से भीड़ के बीच खींचा जाता है, और हर कोई उस रस्सी को एक बार छूना चाहता है।","lang":"hi","body":"They are all going to the same place: the great maidan at Kullu, to visit Raghunath-ji — Lord Rama as this valley knows him — whose own chariot is drawn through the crowds by long ropes that everyone wants a hand on.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kullu-dussehra.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kullu-dussehra|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kullu-dussehra-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kullu-dussehra:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where the Gods Travel","text":"और इसका एक खास नियम होता है जो इस घाटी का हर बच्चा सीखता है। यह उत्सव यूँ ही शुरू नहीं हो जाता। वह इंतज़ार करता है — मनाली के ऊपर देवदार के जंगलों से आने वाले एक खास मेहमान का।","lang":"hi","body":"And there is an order to it that every child of the valley learns. The festival does not simply start. It waits — for one particular guest from the cedar woods above Manali.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kullu-dussehra.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kullu-dussehra|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kullu-dussehra-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kullu-dussehra:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where the Gods Travel","text":"एक हफ्ते तक वह मैदान देवताओं और उनके मेहमानों का शहर बन जाता है। देवता कतारों में विराजते हैं और किसी शादी में आए रिश्तेदारों की तरह एक-दूसरे से मिलने जाते हैं। उनके चारों तरफ मेला सजता है — शॉल बेचने वाले, गन्ने का रस निकालने वाले, बड़े-बड़े झूले और मानो आधा हिमाचल वहाँ उमड़ पड़ा हो।","lang":"hi","body":"For a week the maidan becomes a city of gods and their guests. The devtas are set up in rows, visiting each other like relatives at a wedding. Around them swirls the mela — shawl sellers, sugar-cane crushers, giant wheels, and half of Himachal.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kullu-dussehra.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kullu-dussehra|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kullu-dussehra-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kullu-dussehra:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where the Gods Travel","text":"\"लोग कहते हैं कि वहाँ देवता अपने पुराने दोस्तों से मिलते हैं। गाँव वाले तो ज़रूर मिलते हैं। उस मैदान पर, पालकियों के बीच मचे शोर-शराबे में शादियाँ तय हुई हैं, झगड़े सुलझे हैं और बिछड़े हुए भाई-बहन मिले हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"People say the devtas meet old friends there. Villagers certainly do. Marriages have been arranged, quarrels patched, and lost cousins found on that maidan, in the noise between the palanquins.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kullu-dussehra.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kullu-dussehra|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kullu-dussehra-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kullu-dussehra:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival Where the Gods Travel","text":"\"फिर, जब सब पूरा हो जाता है, तो घाटी उल्टे क्रम में खाली होने लगती है: हर देवता को फिर से कांधे पर उठाया जाता है और आगे-आगे बजते ढोलों के साथ, अपने-अपने पहाड़ पर घर वापस ले जाया जाता है, अगले साल तक के लिए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then, when it is done, the valley empties in reverse: every devta is shouldered again and carried home up its own mountain, drums going before it, until next year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kullu-dussehra.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kullu-dussehra|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gaddi-dog-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gaddi-dog:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shepherd's Other Shepherd","text":"\"गद्दी हिमाचल के चरवाहे हैं, जो भरमौर और कांगड़ा के आसपास धौलाधार के इलाके से आते हैं। साल में दो बार वे अपने रेवड़ों को ऊँचे दर्रों के पार ले जाते हैं — गर्मियों में ऊपर चरागाहों की तरफ, और बर्फबारी से पहले नीचे — महीनों तक लगातार चलते-फिरते ही बसर करते हुए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The Gaddis are the shepherd people of Himachal, from the Dhauladhar country around Bharmour and Kangra. Twice a year they walk their flocks over the high passes — up to the summer meadows, down before the snow — living for months on the move.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gaddi-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gaddi-dog|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gaddi-dog-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gaddi-dog:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shepherd's Other Shepherd","text":"\"एक गद्दी चरवाहा दो साथियों के साथ चलता है: उसका रेवड़, और उसका कुत्ता। वह कुत्ता कोई पालतू जानवर नहीं है। वह तो उसका एक साथी है — घने बालों वाला एक बड़ा और शांत पहाड़ी कुत्ता, जो रास्ता पहचानता है, हर भेड़ को उसकी गंध से पहचानता है, और जब चरवाहा सोता है, तो रात भर पहरा देता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A Gaddi shepherd walks with two companions: his flock, and his dog. The dog is not a pet. He is a colleague — a big, calm, heavy-coated mountain dog who knows the route, knows every sheep by smell, and takes the night watch while the shepherd sleeps.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gaddi-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gaddi-dog|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gaddi-dog-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gaddi-dog:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shepherd's Other Shepherd","text":"\"यह कहानी ऐसी ही एक जोड़ी की है। चरवाहा साल के बहुत आखिर में दर्रा पार कर रहा था — बहुत ही देर से, जैसा कि बुज़ुर्ग सिर हिलाकर कहते — तभी दर्रे पर मौसम अचानक बदल गया, जैसा कि वहाँ होता ही है: पहले धूप, फिर हवा, और फिर भरी दोपहर में ही बर्फ की एक सफ़ेद दीवार।\"","lang":"hi","body":"This tale is told of one such pair. The shepherd was crossing late in the year — too late, the old people would say, shaking their heads — when the weather turned on the pass, the way it does: sunshine, then wind, then a white wall of snow with the afternoon still in it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gaddi-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gaddi-dog|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gaddi-dog-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gaddi-dog:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shepherd's Other Shepherd","text":"वह भेड़ों के झुंड को दर्रे के नीचे बाड़े में सुरक्षित ले आया और हर रात की तरह सुन्न पड़ चुके होंठों से दरवाज़े पर उन्हें गिनने लगा। पर गिनती में एक कम निकला। एक मेमना — वही छोटा वाला, जो सबसे बाद में जन्मा था। ऊपर कहीं उस तूफ़ान में।","lang":"hi","body":"He got the flock down to shelter below the pass, counting them through the gate of the fold with numb lips the way he did every night. And the count came up one short. A lamb — the late-born one, the small one. Somewhere up there in the storm.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gaddi-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gaddi-dog|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gaddi-dog-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gaddi-dog:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shepherd's Other Shepherd","text":"बर्फ़ के साथ-साथ रात भी घिरती जा रही थी। वापस ऊपर जाने का मतलब था अपनी जान जोखिम में डालना। न जाने का मतलब था मेमने की जान जाना। वह बाड़े के दरवाज़े पर कशमकश में खड़ा रहा — और तभी उसे एहसास हुआ कि वह वहाँ अकेला है। कुत्ता उसके साथ नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"Night was coming down with the snow. Going back up meant risking his life. Not going meant the lamb's. He stood in the doorway of the shelter, torn — and then realised he was alone in it. The dog was not at his side.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gaddi-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gaddi-dog|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gaddi-dog-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gaddi-dog:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shepherd's Other Shepherd","text":"पूरी रात तूफ़ान बाड़े से टकराता रहा, और गड़ेरिया लालटेन लिए दरवाज़े के पास जागता बैठा रहा। वह हवा के थपेड़ों को सुनता रहा और बीतते हर पहर से नफ़रत करता रहा।","lang":"hi","body":"All night the storm leaned on the shelter, and the shepherd sat awake by the door with a lamp, listening to the wind and hating every hour of it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gaddi-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gaddi-dog|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gaddi-dog-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gaddi-dog:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shepherd's Other Shepherd","text":"सुबह के धुंधलके में वह ऊपर गया — और दर्रे के ठीक नीचे एक झुकी हुई चट्टान की आड़ में उसने उन्हें ढूँढ़ निकाला: बर्फ़ का एक ढेर, उस ढेर में बनी एक खोह, और उस खोह में वह मेमना, बिल्कुल सुरक्षित, गरमा-गरम और थोड़ा झल्लाया हुआ, कुत्ते के घने रोएँ में दुबका बैठा था, जो उसके इर्द-गिर्द धड़कती हुई दीवार की तरह घेरा बनाकर बैठा हुआ था।","lang":"hi","body":"At grey first light he went up — and found them under a leaning rock just below the pass: a snowdrift, a hollow in the snowdrift, and in the hollow the lamb, warm and cross and completely unharmed, pressed into the deep coat of the dog, who had curled around it like a wall with a heartbeat.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gaddi-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gaddi-dog|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gaddi-dog-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gaddi-dog:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Shepherd's Other Shepherd","text":"कुत्ता उठ खड़ा हुआ, उसने अपने ऊपर से बर्फ़ झाड़ी, और गड़ेरिये की तरफ़ ऐसे मुँह बनाकर देखा जैसे कह रहा हो: तुम देर से आए। फिर वह उन सबसे आगे-आगे बाड़े की तरफ़ चल दिया, मानो यह सब तो बस उसका रोज़ का काम था। जो कि, उसके लिए, सच में था।","lang":"hi","body":"The dog stood up, shook off a small avalanche, and looked at the shepherd with a face that said: you are late. Then he walked down to the fold ahead of them, as if the whole thing were simply the job. Which, to him, it was.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gaddi-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gaddi-dog|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.vipasha-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.vipasha:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The River That Unties Knots","text":"\"ब्यास नदी हिमाचल के ऊंचे पहाड़ों में, रोहतांग दर्रे के पास जन्म लेती है, और पंजाब के मैदानों के अपने लंबे रास्ते पर कुल्लू घाटी से होकर कलकल बहती, हरी-भरी और ठंडी-ठंडी नीचे उतरती है। इतनी पुरानी नदियां सिर्फ पानी ही नहीं बहातीं। वे अपने साथ नाम भी लेकर चलती हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The Beas is born high in the mountains of Himachal, near the Rohtang pass, and comes down through the Kullu valley loud and green and cold, on its long way to the plains of Punjab. Rivers this old carry more than water. They carry names.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-vipasha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.vipasha|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.vipasha-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.vipasha:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The River That Unties Knots","text":"\"और ब्यास के पास दो नाम हैं। एक नाम ऋषि व्यास की याद दिलाता है, जिनके बारे में कहा जाता है कि वे इसके झरनों के पास रहते थे और तपस्या करते थे। लेकिन पुराना नाम और भी अनोखा और सुंदर है: विपाशा। इसका मतलब कुछ ऐसा है जैसे बंधनों से मुक्त करने वाली — जो गांठे खोल दे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the Beas carries two. One remembers the sage Vyas, who is said to have lived and meditated by its springs. But the older name is stranger and more beautiful: Vipasha. It means something like the unbinder — the one who unties.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-vipasha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.vipasha|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.vipasha-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.vipasha:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The River That Unties Knots","text":"\"इसके पीछे की पुरानी कहानी महान ऋषि वशिष्ठ के बारे में है। उनके परिवार पर बहुत गहरा दुख आ पड़ा — कहानी इसकी बारीकियों से दूर ही रहती है, और हम भी दूर ही रहेंगे — और वे ऋषि, जिन्होंने बड़े-बड़े राजाओं को ढांढस बंधाया था और वीरों को सिखाया था, खुद अपने मन को सांत्वना नहीं दे पाए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The old story behind it is about the great sage Vashishtha. A terrible sadness came upon his family — the story keeps its distance from the details, and so shall we — and the sage, who had comforted kings and taught heroes, found that he could not comfort himself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-vipasha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.vipasha|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.vipasha-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.vipasha:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The River That Unties Knots","text":"\"उनका दुख इतना भारी हो गया कि वे बस सब खत्म कर देना चाहते थे — खुद को नदी को सौंप देना चाहते थे ताकि वह उन्हें बहा ले जाए। और क्योंकि घोर निराशा में भी वे पक्के इरादे वाले थे, उन्होंने पहले खुद को बांधा, मजबूत रस्सियों से खुद को बार-बार लपेटकर गांठ पर गांठ लगा दी, ताकि कोई भी बात उनका फैसला न बदल सके।\"","lang":"hi","body":"His grief grew so heavy that he wanted only to be done — to give himself to the river and let it carry him away. And because even in despair he was thorough, he bound himself first, wrapping himself around and around with strong rope, knot upon knot, so that nothing could change his mind.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-vipasha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.vipasha|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.vipasha-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.vipasha:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The River That Unties Knots","text":"\"फिर वे पानी में उतर गए। और उस नदी ने — बर्फ से पोषित इस ठंडी, तेज़ पहाड़ी नदी ने — कुछ ऐसा किया जिसकी किसी को, और सबसे कम खुद ऋषि को, उम्मीद थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then he walked into the water. And the river — this cold, fast, snow-fed mountain river — did something no one, least of all the sage, expected.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-vipasha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.vipasha|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.vipasha-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.vipasha:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The River That Unties Knots","text":"\"ऋषि हर तरह से बंधनों से मुक्त होकर गर्म पत्थरों पर लेटे रहे, और पास से बहती नदी को सुनते रहे। कहानी कहती है कि रस्सियों के साथ-साथ उनके भीतर की कोई गांठ भी ढीली पड़ गई। उस दिन उनका दुख खत्म तो नहीं हुआ। लेकिन वे उठ खड़े हुए। और वे वहीं रुके रहे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The sage lay on the warm stones, unbound in every sense, and listened to the river go by. The story says something in him loosened along with the ropes. He did not stop being sad that day. But he stood up. And he stayed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-vipasha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.vipasha|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.vipasha-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.vipasha:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The River That Unties Knots","text":"और तब से उस नदी को विपाशा कहा जाने लगा — बंधनों को खोलने वाली, गांठें सुलझाने वाली — क्योंकि निराशा ने उसे जो सौंपना चाहा था, नदी ने उसे अपने पास नहीं रखा।","lang":"hi","body":"And the river was called Vipasha ever after — the unbinder, the untier of knots — because it would not keep what despair had tried to give it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-vipasha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.vipasha|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.vipasha-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.vipasha:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The River That Unties Knots","text":"घाटी के लोग आज भी ब्यास नदी के बारे में कुछ-कुछ ऐसा ही मानते हैं, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे कोई उस नदी पर यकीन करता है जिसके किनारे वह बड़ा हुआ हो: कि उसकी आवाज़ भारी सीने को हल्का कर देती है, और जो कोई उसके पास देर तक बैठता है, वह उठते समय हल्का महसूस करता है।","lang":"hi","body":"People in the valley still half-believe it of the Beas, in the way one believes things about a river one has grown up beside: that its sound loosens a tight chest, and that a person who sits by it long enough gets up lighter.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-vipasha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.vipasha|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.apple-road-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.apple-road:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man Who Brought the Apples","text":"सौ से कुछ ही साल पहले, फ़िलाडेल्फ़िया शहर से सैमुअल इवांस स्टोक्स नाम का एक नौजवान अमरीकी हिमाचल की पहाड़ियों में आया। वह शिमला के पास बीमार लोगों के एक घर में मदद करने आया था — और पहाड़ों ने उसके साथ वही किया जो वे कुछ लोगों के साथ करते हैं: उन्होंने उसे वहीं रोक लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"A little more than a hundred years ago, a young American named Samuel Evans Stokes came from the city of Philadelphia to the hills of Himachal. He came to help at a home for sick people near Shimla — and the mountains did to him what mountains do to some people: they kept him.","art":"art/story/sm/it-apple-road.jpg","route":"#/story/it.apple-road|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.apple-road-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.apple-road:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man Who Brought the Apples","text":"वह सतलुज के ऊपर कोटगढ़ में बस गया, वहाँ की भाषा सीखी, वहीं के एक परिवार में शादी की, और अपने पड़ोसियों की तरह ही जीने लगा। और पड़ोसियों की तरह जीते हुए, उसे उनकी सबसे बड़ी मुश्किल समझ में आई: इन खूबसूरत पहाड़ी ढलानों पर बमुश्किल ही कुछ उग पाता था। परिवार साल भर सीढ़ीदार खेतों में मेहनत करते, फिर भी गरीब ही रहते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"He settled in Kotgarh, above the Sutlej, learned the language, married into the community, and lived like his neighbours. And living like his neighbours, he learned their hardest problem: the beautiful hillsides grew barely enough. Families worked terraced fields all year and stayed poor.","art":"art/story/sm/it-apple-road.jpg","route":"#/story/it.apple-road|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.apple-road-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.apple-road:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man Who Brought the Apples","text":"स्टोक्स इस बात पर लगातार सोचता रहा। ज़मीन ढलान वाली थी, सर्दियाँ बहुत ठंडी और गर्मियाँ खिली धूप वाली — न गेहूँ के लिए अच्छी, न चावल के लिए। और तभी उसे एक बात समझ आई: ये कोई कमियाँ नहीं थीं। ठंडी सर्दियाँ और खिली धूप वाली गर्मियाँ तो ठीक वही मौसम था, जो एक ख़ास फ़सल को सबसे ज़्यादा पसंद था।","lang":"hi","body":"Stokes kept turning the problem over. The land was steep, the winters cold, the summers bright — bad for wheat, bad for rice. And then it struck him: those were not flaws. Cold winters and bright summers were exactly what one particular crop loved.","art":"art/story/sm/it-apple-road.jpg","route":"#/story/it.apple-road|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.apple-road-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.apple-road:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man Who Brought the Apples","text":"इसलिए उन्होंने यहाँ के मौसम के अनुकूल अमरीकी सेब की उम्दा किस्मों के पौधे मँगवाए और कोटगढ़ में एक बगीचा लगाया। पड़ोसी बड़े अदब से उन्हें देखते रहे, जैसे किसी धुन के पक्के इंसान को देखा जाता है। पेड़ों के बड़े होने में तो कई साल लगते हैं। उन्होंने खरपतवार हटाई, क़लम बाँधी और इंतज़ार किया।","lang":"hi","body":"So he sent for saplings of fine American apple varieties suited to the climate, and planted an orchard at Kotgarh. Neighbours watched politely, the way one watches an enthusiast. Trees take years. He weeded, grafted, waited.","art":"art/story/sm/it-apple-road.jpg","route":"#/story/it.apple-road|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.apple-road-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.apple-road:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man Who Brought the Apples","text":"और फिर पेड़ों पर फल लद गए, और सेब इतने लाजवाब थे — कि अचानक इन पहाड़ों का पूरा हिसाब-किताब ही हमेशा के लिए बदल गया। सेबों के चंद सीढ़ीदार खेत इतनी कमाई कर सकते थे, जितनी अनाज से भरी पूरी पहाड़ियाँ भी नहीं कर पाती थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"And then the trees came into bearing, and the apples were superb — and suddenly the mathematics of the mountainside had changed forever. A few terraces of apples could earn what whole hillsides of grain could not.","art":"art/story/sm/it-apple-road.jpg","route":"#/story/it.apple-road|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.apple-road-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.apple-road:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man Who Brought the Apples","text":"और इन पहाड़ों को सबसे ज़्यादा जो बात याद है, वह यह: उन्होंने यह फ़ायदा सिर्फ़ अपने तक नहीं रखा। उन्होंने अपने पड़ोसियों को पौधे दिए और क़लम लगाना सिखाया। वे लोगों को समझाते रहे, उनके पीछे पड़े रहे और हौसला बढ़ाते रहे, जब तक कि ढलानों पर एक के बाद एक सेब के बगीचे नहीं लहलहा उठे — पहले कोटगढ़, फिर एक के बाद एक घाटियाँ, और आख़िरकार कुल्लू और किन्नौर तक, जिनके सेब आज पूरे भारत में मशहूर हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Here is the part the hills remember best: he did not keep it. He gave saplings and grafting lessons to his neighbours, and argued, badgered and encouraged until orchard after orchard climbed the slopes — Kotgarh first, then valley after valley, on eventually to Kullu and Kinnaur, whose apples are now famous across India.","art":"art/story/sm/it-apple-road.jpg","route":"#/story/it.apple-road|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.apple-road-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.apple-road:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man Who Brought the Apples","text":"स्टोक्स ख़ुद भी हर तरह से इन पहाड़ों के होकर रह गए। वे भारत की आज़ादी की लड़ाई में शामिल हुए और इसके लिए जेल भी गए। उन्होंने पुराने धर्मग्रंथ पढ़े और आगे चलकर हिंदू धर्म अपना लिया, साथ ही अपना नाम सत्यानंद रखा। वे अपने पेड़ों के बीच, कोटगढ़ में ही जिए और वहीं उन्होंने आख़िरी साँस ली।","lang":"hi","body":"Stokes himself became a man of these hills in every way. He joined India's freedom struggle and went to jail for it. He studied the old scriptures, and in time embraced Hinduism, taking the name Satyanand. He lived and died in Kotgarh, among his trees.","art":"art/story/sm/it-apple-road.jpg","route":"#/story/it.apple-road|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.spiti-ghost-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.spiti-ghost:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grey Ghost of Spiti","text":"हिमाचल के दूरदराज़ ऊँचे कोने में बसा स्पीति एक ठंडा रेगिस्तान है — सूखे भूरे पहाड़, नदी के साथ-साथ चलती हरियाली की एक पतली लकीर, और गहरे सन्नाटे के बीच सफ़ेद घरों के गाँव। सर्दियों में यहाँ ठंड शून्य से बहुत नीचे चली जाती है और यह सन्नाटा और भी गहरा हो जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Spiti, in the far high corner of Himachal, is a cold desert — bare brown mountains, a ribbon of green along the river, villages of white houses under enormous silence. In winter it drops far below freezing and the silence gets even bigger.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-spiti-ghost.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.spiti-ghost|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.spiti-ghost-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.spiti-ghost:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grey Ghost of Spiti","text":"\"और उसी सन्नाटे में कहीं, लगभग हमेशा सबकी नज़रों से छिपा, रहता है हिम तेंदुआ। सलेटी-सुनहरा, जिसका रूप-रंग खुद पहाड़ जैसा है, एक बड़ी और मुलायम रस्सी जैसी पूंछ, और बर्फ के लिए ही बने पंजे। ऊंचे गांवों के लोग इसे सलेटी भूत कहते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And somewhere in that silence, almost always unseen, lives the snow leopard. Grey-gold, patterned like the mountain itself, with a tail like a great soft rope and paws made for snow. The people of the high villages call it the grey ghost.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-spiti-ghost.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.spiti-ghost|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.spiti-ghost-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.spiti-ghost:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grey Ghost of Spiti","text":"\"उसे यह नाम एक सीधी-सी वजह से मिला है: वह वहीं होता है, पर आप उसे देख नहीं पाते। पथरीली ढलान पर बैठा हिम तेंदुआ मानो ढलान का ही हिस्सा बन जाता है — चरवाहे मिनटों तक उसी की तरफ देखते रहे और उन्हें सिर्फ पत्थर ही नज़र आए, जब तक कि उनमें से एक पत्थर धुएं की तरह चुपचाप ऊपर पहाड़ की ओर खिसक नहीं गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It is called that for a simple reason: it is there, and you cannot see it. A snow leopard on a rocky slope simply becomes the slope — herders have stared straight at one for minutes and seen only stones, until one stone flowed away uphill like smoke.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-spiti-ghost.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.spiti-ghost|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.spiti-ghost-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.spiti-ghost:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grey Ghost of Spiti","text":"\"सर्दियों में, जब जंगली भेड़ें और आइबेक्स नीचे उतरते हैं, तो यह भूत भी उनके पीछे-पीछे नीचे आ जाता है — और यही उसे ढूंढने का मौसम होता है। दुनिया भर से लोग पार्सल की तरह गर्म कपड़ों में खुद को लपेटकर स्पीति आते हैं, ताकि इस कड़ाके की ठंड में घंटों दूरबीन के पीछे बैठकर उम्मीद भरी नज़रों से ताक सकें।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In winter, when the wild sheep and ibex come down lower, the ghost follows them down — and that is the season of looking. People come to Spiti from across the world, wrapped like parcels, to sit for hours behind telescopes in the cold, hoping.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-spiti-ghost.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.spiti-ghost|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.spiti-ghost-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.spiti-ghost:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grey Ghost of Spiti","text":"\"उन्हें सबसे बढ़िया पहचानने वाले यहीं के स्थानीय लोग होते हैं — वे गांव वाले जिन्होंने ज़िंदगी भर इन ढलानों को पढ़ा है। और गांवों तथा इस भूत के बीच एक पुरानी और असली मुश्किल भी है: हिम तेंदुआ कभी-कभार किसी बकरी या भेड़ को उठा ले जाता है, और किसी भी परिवार की बकरियां ही उनकी असली पूंजी होती हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The best spotters are local — villagers who have read these slopes all their lives. And between the villages and the ghost there is an old, real difficulty: a snow leopard sometimes takes a goat or a sheep, and a family's goats are a family's wealth.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-spiti-ghost.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.spiti-ghost|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.spiti-ghost-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.spiti-ghost:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grey Ghost of Spiti","text":"\"स्पीति के बच्चे सबसे अनोखी भूतिया कहानियों को सुनते हुए बड़े होते हैं: उस पड़ोसी की कहानी जिसे तड़के गांव के चारों ओर बड़े-बड़े मुलायम पंजों के निशान मिले; उस सर्दी की कहानी जब एक तेंदुआ छत पर ऐसे बैठा था मानो कोई राजा अपनी रियासत का मुआयना कर रहा हो; और दूरबीन का वह पल जब दूर की एक सलेटी चट्टान ने अचानक जम्हाई ले ली।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Children in Spiti grow up on ghost stories of the best kind: the neighbour who found big soft pawprints circling the village at dawn; the winter a leopard sat on a rooftop like a king surveying his country; the telescope moment when a far grey rock yawned.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-spiti-ghost.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.spiti-ghost|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.spiti-ghost-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.spiti-ghost:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grey Ghost of Spiti","text":"\"उन पर अध्ययन करने वाले वैज्ञानिकों का कहना है कि दुनिया भर के ऊंचे पहाड़ों में अब बस कुछ हज़ार हिम तेंदुए ही बचे हैं, जो स्पीति की इन ढलानों को बेहद अनमोल बनाता है: धरती की उन चुनिंदा जगहों में से एक, जहां यह भूत आज भी टहलता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Scientists who study them say there are only a few thousand snow leopards left in all the world's high mountains, which makes Spiti's slopes something precious: one of the places on Earth where the ghost still walks.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-spiti-ghost.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.spiti-ghost|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.malana-sabha-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.malana-sabha:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village That Governs Itself","text":"\"कुल्लू घाटी से अलग, एक खड़ी तंग घाटी के ऊपर मलाना बसा है — नदी से बहुत ऊँचाई पर पत्थरों और लकड़ी के घरों वाला एक गाँव, जहाँ इतिहास के ज़्यादातर समय में सिर्फ़ पैदल ही पहुँचा जा सकता था। यहाँ के लोग अपनी ही एक भाषा बोलते हैं, कनाशी, जो धरती पर कहीं और नहीं बोली जाती।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Off the Kullu valley, up a steep side gorge, sits Malana — a village of stone and timber houses high above the river, reachable for most of its history only on foot. Its people speak their own language, Kanashi, spoken nowhere else on Earth.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-malana-sabha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.malana-sabha|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.malana-sabha-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.malana-sabha:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village That Governs Itself","text":"\"मलाना में फ़ैसले करने का अपना ही तरीक़ा है, और यह बहुत पुराना है — इतना पुराना कि बाहर से आने वाले लोग अर्से से इस गाँव को दुनिया के सबसे प्राचीन जीवित लोकतंत्रों में से एक कहते आए हैं। गाँव वाले इसे और सीधे शब्दों में कहते हैं: जमलू यही चाहते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Malana keeps its own way of deciding things, and it is old — so old that visitors have long called the village one of the world's most ancient living democracies. The villagers put it more simply: this is how Jamlu wants it done.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-malana-sabha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.malana-sabha|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.malana-sabha-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.malana-sabha:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village That Governs Itself","text":"\"जमलू गाँव के देवता हैं — मलाना के देवता, जिनकी बात गाँव का सबसे बड़ा क़ानून है। लेकिन जमलू अकेले राज नहीं करते, और कमाल की बात यही है: गाँव अपना काम-काज अपनी सभा के ज़रिए चलाता है, जिसमें सदस्यों की एक परिषद होती है और इन ज़िम्मेदारियों को ख़ुद गाँव के लोग ही संभालते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Jamlu is the village devta — the deity of Malana, whose word is the village's highest law. But Jamlu does not rule alone, and this is the remarkable part: the village runs its affairs through its own assembly, with a council of members whose roles the village itself fills.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-malana-sabha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.malana-sabha|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.malana-sabha-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.malana-sabha:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village That Governs Itself","text":"\"जब किसी बात को सुलझाना होता है — खेत की मेड़ को लेकर कोई झगड़ा, जंगल को पहुँचा नुक़सान, या मंदिर से जुड़ा कोई सवाल — तो यह सभा खुले में, गाँव के बीचों-बीच जुटती है, और हर संबंधित इंसान अपनी बात रखता है। ज़ोर से। सबके सामने।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When something must be settled — a dispute over a field boundary, damage to the forest, a question about the temple — the assembly gathers in the open, in the middle of the village, and everyone concerned has their say. Out loud. In front of everyone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-malana-sabha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.malana-sabha|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.malana-sabha-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.malana-sabha:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village That Governs Itself","text":"\"और फ़ैसला जल्दबाज़ी के उस तरीक़े से नहीं किया जाता, जिसमें बस हाथ गिनकर ज़्यादा गिनती वाले हिस्से को जिता दिया जाए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And a decision is not done the quick way, by counting hands and letting the bigger half win.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-malana-sabha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.malana-sabha|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.malana-sabha-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.malana-sabha:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village That Governs Itself","text":"जब सभा पूरी तरह उलझ जाती है, तो सवाल उनके माध्यम के ज़रिए खुद जमलू देवता के पास जाता है — और जो भी जवाब आए, गाँव के दोनों पक्ष बिना किसी बहस के उसे स्वीकार कर लेते हैं। देवता का फैसला मामले को ऐसे शांत कर देता है जैसे बारिश धूल को।","lang":"hi","body":"When the assembly is truly stuck, the question goes to Jamlu himself, through his oracle — and whatever answer comes, the village accepts, both sides, without appeal. A verdict from the devta ends the matter the way rain ends dust.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-malana-sabha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.malana-sabha|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.malana-sabha-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.malana-sabha:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village That Governs Itself","text":"मलाना अपने रिवाज़ों को मज़बूती से थामे हुए है, और बाहर से आने वालों से उसके नियमों का आदर करने को कहा जाता है — कहाँ चलना है, किसे हाथ नहीं लगाना है — जैसा कि मेहमानों को कहीं भी करना चाहिए। यह गाँव कोई म्यूज़ियम नहीं है। यह एक ऐसा समुदाय है जिसने सभा-दर-सभा यही तय किया है कि वह जैसा है, वैसा ही रहेगा।","lang":"hi","body":"Malana keeps its customs firmly, and visitors are asked to respect its rules — where to walk, what not to touch — as guests should anywhere. The village is not a museum. It is a community that has decided, assembly after assembly, to remain itself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-malana-sabha.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.malana-sabha|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangra-brush-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangra-brush:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Painters of the Small Monsoon","text":"दो सौ से कुछ साल पहले, धौलाधार की बर्फ़ीली चोटियों के नीचे बसी हरी-भरी काँगड़ा घाटी में, चित्रकारों के ऐसे परिवार काम करते थे जिनकी बनाई तस्वीरें इतनी छोटी थीं कि दोनों हाथों में आ जाएँ — और फिर भी, न जाने कैसे, उनमें सब कुछ समाया हुआ था।","lang":"hi","body":"Two hundred and some years ago, in the green Kangra valley under the Dhauladhar snows, there worked families of painters whose paintings were small enough to hold in two hands — and held, somehow, everything.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangra-brush.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangra-brush|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangra-brush-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangra-brush:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Painters of the Small Monsoon","text":"नीले-काले बादलों से घिरा सावन का आसमान, और उसे पार करता हुआ एक सफ़ेद बगुला। शहद की बूँदों जैसे दीयों से जगमगाता रात का एक बगीचा। पहाड़ियाँ, नदियाँ, मवेशियों के झुंड — और हर जगह, बार-बार, वही कृष्ण: शाम की तरह साँवले, पेड़ों के नीचे अपनी बाँसुरी बजाते हुए, और उस चित्रित दुनिया का हर जीव जैसे झुककर उन्हें सुन रहा हो।","lang":"hi","body":"A monsoon sky stacked with blue-black clouds, and one white crane crossing it. A garden at night with lamps like drops of honey. Hills, rivers, herds — and everywhere, again and again, Krishna: blue as evening, playing his flute under the trees while the whole painted world leans in to listen.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangra-brush.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangra-brush|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangra-brush-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangra-brush:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Painters of the Small Monsoon","text":"यह है काँगड़ा चित्रकला — काँगड़ा क़लम — जो भारतीय लघुचित्रों की महान पहाड़ी शैलियों में से एक है। इन चित्रकारों को सबसे ज़्यादा लगाव कृष्ण और राधा के काव्य से था, और उन्होंने उसी की कोमलता हर पत्ते और हर बादल में पिरो दी।","lang":"hi","body":"This is Kangra painting — Kangra kalam, the Kangra brush — one of the great pahari, or hill, schools of Indian miniature painting. The painters loved the poetry of Krishna and Radha above all, and painted its tenderness into every leaf and cloud.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangra-brush.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangra-brush|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangra-brush-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangra-brush:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Painters of the Small Monsoon","text":"और यह सब कैसे बना, यह अपने आप में एक कहानी है। पलकों और बारिश की बूँदों के लिए इतने बारीक ब्रश कि शायद उनमें सिर्फ़ एक ही बाल हो। दुनिया भर की चीज़ों से हाथ से पीसे गए रंग: लाल और पीले के लिए खनिज और मिट्टी, नीले के लिए कीमती पत्थर, और मुकुट की चमक के लिए असली सोना।","lang":"hi","body":"And the how of it is a story in itself. Brushes so fine they might hold a single hair, for eyelashes and raindrops. Colours ground by hand from the world: minerals and earths for reds and yellows, precious stone for the blues, real gold for the light on a crown.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangra-brush.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangra-brush|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangra-brush-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangra-brush:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Painters of the Small Monsoon","text":"ऐसी किसी कार्यशाला में काम सीखने वाला — जो अक्सर कोई बेटा या भतीजा होता था, क्योंकि यह परिवार का ही हुनर होता था — अपने शुरुआती साल शायद बिना एक भी तस्वीर बनाए ही बिता देता था।","lang":"hi","body":"An apprentice in such a workshop — often a son or nephew, for these were family ateliers — might spend his first years never painting a single picture.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangra-brush.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangra-brush|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangra-brush-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangra-brush:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Painters of the Small Monsoon","text":"कला से प्यार करने वाले पहाड़ी राजाओं की छत्रछाया में ये चित्रकार खूब फले-फूले — कांगड़ा के महाराजा संसार चंद के दौर में यह कला सबसे ज़्यादा चमकी, जिनके दरबार में कई उस्ताद चित्रकार काम करते थे — और उनकी बनाई तस्वीरें पहाड़ों से बहुत दूर-दूर तक पहुँचीं और सहेजी गईं।","lang":"hi","body":"The painters flourished under hill rajas who loved the art — the school shone brightest under Maharaja Sansar Chand of Kangra, whose court kept many master painters at work — and their paintings travelled and were treasured far beyond the hills.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangra-brush.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangra-brush|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangra-brush-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangra-brush:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Painters of the Small Monsoon","text":"यह परंपरा कोई बंद किताब नहीं है। पुरानी नायाब कलाकृतियाँ भारत और दुनिया भर के संग्रहालयों में लगी हैं — और आज भी कांगड़ा घाटी में कलाकार इस क़लम को सीखते और साधते हैं, रंग पीसते हैं, और इस परंपरा को ज़िंदा रखते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The tradition is not a closed book. The old masterpieces hang in museums in India and across the world — and in the Kangra valley today, artists still learn and practise the kalam, grinding colours, keeping the line alive.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangra-brush.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangra-brush|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.satisar-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.satisar:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Valley That Was a Lake","text":"\"बहुत, बहुत पुरानी बात है — जैसा कश्मीर की अपनी सबसे पुरानी कहानी बताती है — तब कश्मीर की कोई घाटी थी ही नहीं। बड़े-बड़े पहाड़ों के घेरे के बीच बस एक बहुत बड़ी झील फैली थी, विशाल, गहरी और ठंडी, जिसे सतीसर कहते थे, यानी देवी सती की झील।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Long, long ago — so says Kashmir's own oldest telling — there was no valley of Kashmir at all. Between the ring of great mountains lay one enormous lake, vast and deep and cold, called Satisar, the lake of the goddess Sati.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-satisar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.satisar|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.satisar-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.satisar:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Valley That Was a Lake","text":"\"वह सुंदर तो थी, पर जिसे सूखी ज़मीन चाहिए थी उसके किसी काम की नहीं थी। इससे भी बुरी बात यह थी कि उसकी गहराइयों में कुछ ऐसा रहता था जिसने पानी को ख़तरनाक बना रखा था, इतना कि लोग उसके किनारों पर भी नहीं बस सकते थे। कहानी उस जीव को अंधेरे में ही रहने देती है, और हम भी उसे वहीं छोड़ देते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It was beautiful and it was useless to anyone who needed dry ground. Worse: something dwelt in its depths that made the waters dangerous, so that people could not settle even on the shores. The story keeps that creature down in the dark, and we will leave it there.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-satisar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.satisar|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.satisar-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.satisar:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Valley That Was a Lake","text":"\"उस झील के पास महान ऋषि कश्यप आए — पुरानी कहानियों में कई जातियों के पितामह, बड़े ही शांत स्वभाव वाले। वे पहाड़ों के पूरे घेरे पर घूमे और उस फंसे हुए पानी को ठीक वैसे देखा जैसे कोई कारीगर लकड़ी की किसी गांठ को देखता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"To that lake came the great sage Kashyapa, grandfather of many peoples in the old stories, a man of enormous calm. He walked the whole rim of the mountains, looking at the trapped water the way a craftsman looks at a knot in wood.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-satisar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.satisar|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.satisar-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.satisar:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Valley That Was a Lake","text":"\"गहराइयों में छिपी उस आफ़त से निपटने के लिए खुद देवताओं ने भी हाथ बढ़ाया — ठीक कैसे, इस पर कहानियों के अपने-अपने तरीके हैं, और कश्मीरी लोग दो हज़ार सालों से इन बारीकियों पर मज़े से बहस करते आए हैं। पर ऋषि की भूमिका को लेकर हर कहानी एकमत है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The gods themselves took a hand against the trouble in the depths — the tellings differ on exactly how, and Kashmiris have argued the details pleasantly for two thousand years. But every telling agrees on the sage's part.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-satisar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.satisar|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.satisar-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.satisar:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Valley That Was a Lake","text":"\"और जैसे-जैसे पानी कम होता गया, घाटी उसमें से ऐसे बाहर निकल आई जैसे कोई तोहफ़ा खोला जा रहा हो: पहले चोटियां, फिर ढलानें, और फिर दूर तक फैला हरा-भरा मैदान जिसमें नदियां पहले से ही बह रही थीं — और बीच में से झेलम किसी दस्तख़त की तरह बलखाती हुई गुज़र रही थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And as the water sank, the valley rose out of it like a gift being unwrapped: ridges first, then slopes, then the wide green floor with its rivers already running — the Jhelum winding down the middle like a signature.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-satisar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.satisar|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.satisar-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.satisar:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Valley That Was a Lake","text":"\"लोग आए और इस नई ज़मीन पर बस गए, और यह धरती की सबसे सुंदर जगहों में से एक निकली: सेब और अख़रोट के बाग़, केसर के खेत — दुनिया का सबसे कीमती मसाला, जो पतझड़ में बैंगनी हो जाता है — चिनार के पेड़, और पीछे छूट गई झीलें जो पुराने सतीसर के टुकड़ों की तरह उसकी याद संजोए हुए थीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"People came and settled the new land, and it turned out to be one of the loveliest places on Earth: orchards of apples and walnuts, fields of saffron — the world's most precious spice, purple in autumn — chinar trees, and lakes left behind like pieces of the old Satisar keeping the memory.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-satisar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.satisar|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.satisar-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.satisar:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Valley That Was a Lake","text":"मान्यता है कि इस घाटी का नाम खुद उस ऋषि के नाम पर पड़ा: कश्यप की भूमि — कश्मीर। और नौ सौ साल पहले जब कश्मीर के पहले महान इतिहासकार, कल्हण, राजाओं की गाथा लिखने बैठे, तो उन्होंने इसी कहानी से शुरुआत की।","lang":"hi","body":"They named the valley, says the tradition, for the sage himself: Kashyapa's land — Kashmir. And when Kashmir's first great historian, Kalhana, sat down nine hundred years ago to write his chronicle of kings, this is the story he began with.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-satisar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.satisar|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.himal-nagrai-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.himal-nagrai:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Himal and the Serpent Prince","text":"कश्मीर चश्मों की घाटी है — चिनार के पेड़ों के नीचे ज़मीन से फूटते ठंडे, साफ़ पानी के ताल। और कश्मीरी हमेशा से कहते आए हैं कि ये चश्मे दरवाज़े हैं: कि पुरानी कहानियों के नाग लोग, पानी के उस पार अपने चमकते राज्यों में रहते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Kashmir is a valley of springs — cold, clear pools that rise out of the earth under the chinar trees. And Kashmiris have always said that springs are doors: that the naga folk, the serpent people of the old stories, live in shining kingdoms on the other side of the water.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-himal-nagrai.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.himal-nagrai|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.himal-nagrai-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.himal-nagrai:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Himal and the Serpent Prince","text":"कश्मीरी कहानियों में सबसे प्यारी कहानी ऐसे ही एक चश्मे से शुरू होती है। नागराय नागों का राजकुमार था — अपने राज्य में एक तेजस्वी युवा राजा; और हमारी दुनिया में, जब उसकी मर्ज़ी हो, चाँदी के फीते की तरह पानी में सरकता हुआ एक साँप।","lang":"hi","body":"The most beloved of all Kashmiri tales begins at such a spring. Nagrai was a prince of the naga people — in his own kingdom a shining young king; in ours, when he chose, a serpent slipping through the water like a ribbon of silver.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-himal-nagrai.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.himal-nagrai|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]}});
